DENTITY`\n- `GCE_DON`\n- `Projects`\n- Durable functional estates:\n  - Strategic Governance\n  - Technical Strategy / Systems Intelligence\n  - Architecture\n  - Operations\n  - Implementation\n  - Verification\n  - Data\n  - Shared Enterprise Services\n  - Projects\n  - Archive / Frozen State\n- Historical/project provenance with original naming intact:\n  - `01_Corrado_Kimi`\n  - historical Kimi references\n  - historical Calibro references\n  - old Corrado methodology/advisor documents\n  - archived seat bootstraps\n  - dated migration records\n  - project-specific historical folder names\n  - Sep-20 Framework DOCX\n\nThe governing test is **function, not current seat-name parity**. A folder is not stale simply because its name is not a seat. fileciteturn0file0L135-L163 fileciteturn0file0L383-L397\n\n---\n\n# C. RENAME LIST\n\n## Approved candidate, but **not part of the immediate Framework repair**\n\n`RESTART-KEEL-VOICE.cmd`  \n→ `RESTART-VOICEBRIDGE.cmd`\n\nThis belongs under the later **GCE Stack / VoiceBridge cleanup**, not the current Framework taxonomy execution. The `\"hey keel\"` wake phrase should remain untouched because it is an interaction contract, not necessarily an authority label. fileciteturn0file0L400-L418\n\n## No broad folder renames authorized\n\nNo functional estate should be renamed merely to match Vittorio, Chiave, Nico, Corrado, etc.\n\nRenaming is justified only where a **live name encodes retired authority and materially misroutes ownership/work**. fileciteturn0file0L245-L270\n\n---\n\n# D. MOVE LIST\n\n### Immediate move list: **NONE established from this handoff alone**\n\nThere is not enough path-by-path evidence here to justify physical moves of existing estates.\n\nA move becomes justified only when:\n\n1. content demonstrably belongs to a different current function/project authority; and\n2. its present placement causes authority confusion.\n\nTherefore the next physical-filesystem phase should **inventory first,