rent seat authority;\n- identity-first / seat-first operating doctrine;\n- Sep-22 frozen roster is current;\n- projects own implementation truth;\n- historical materials remain historically accurate;\n- current continuation uses the current Framework anchor;\n- current Drive anchor/reference once reconciled/materialized.\n\nThat treatment is explicitly prescribed by the handoff. fileciteturn0file0L97-L132\n\n## 2. Current Framework authority artifact — **REQUIRED**\n\nProposed naming pattern:\n\n`GCE_FRAMEWORK_CURRENT_2026-09-23.md`\n\nIts role should be tightly bounded to **current authority**, not a rewrite of the entire Framework history.\n\nMinimum contents:\n\n- current roster;\n- authority hierarchy;\n- identity/seat/model separation;\n- Framework vs Project boundary;\n- current root doctrine;\n- current continuation pointer;\n- explicit supersession relationship to the Sep-20 DOCX.\n\n## 3. Framework Reconciliation parent — **REQUIRED**\n\nThis is a distinct project/workstream and must remain separate from live Framework governance.\n\nScope:\n\n- stale-chat intake;\n- Wave registry;\n- authority classification;\n- artifact mapping;\n- read-only Drive reconciliation;\n- conflict/supersession registry;\n- successor-anchor preparation.\n\nIts current state is **HANDOFF ONLY**, so durable materialization is justified. fileciteturn0file0L338-L358\n\n## 4. GCE Stack parent — **REQUIRED**\n\nMaterialize the parent first.\n\nThen map:\n\n- VoiceBridge;\n- Web Bridge/scraping;\n- transport;\n- synchronization;\n- runtime plumbing;\n- local services/daemons;\n- APIs/adapters;\n- developer utilities;\n- archival/recovery tooling;\n- Command Center supporting tech;\n- Walking Capture.\n\nDo **not** perform a component migration sweep at the same time. fileciteturn0file0L307-L335\n\n## 5. Model Test Registry — **REQUIRED, lightweight**\n\nClassification:\n\n**Framework research workstream / Technical Strategy**\n\nRegistry should point to, not duplicate:\n\n-