`GCE_IDENTITY` = live identities, `GCE_DON` = operating floor, `Projects` = implementation truth, and archive/frozen areas = provenance. fileciteturn0file0L185-L207\n\nI would use this as the **target Google Drive structure**:\n\n```text\nGCE/\n│\n├── 00_START_HERE/\n│   ├── README_CURRENT_GCE.md\n│   ├── CURRENT_AUTHORITY_POINTERS.md\n│   └── CURRENT_PROJECT_INDEX.md\n│\n├── 01_GCE_ORG/\n│   │\n│   ├── 01_Strategic_Governance/\n│   │   ├── Current/\n│   │   ├── Handoffs/\n│   │   └── Supporting/\n│   │\n│   ├── 02_Technical_Strategy/\n│   │   ├── Current/\n│   │   ├── Model_Testing/\n│   │   │   ├── Registry/\n│   │   │   ├── Black_Pearl/\n│   │   │   ├── Disney_Test/\n│   │   │   └── Historical_Evaluations/\n│   │   ├── Handoffs/\n│   │   └── Supporting/\n│   │\n│   ├── 03_Architecture/\n│   │   ├── Current/\n│   │   ├── Decisions/\n│   │   ├── Handoffs/\n│   │   └── Supporting/\n│   │\n│   ├── 04_Operations/\n│   │   ├── Current/\n│   │   ├── Routing/\n│   │   ├── Handoffs/\n│   │   └── Supporting/\n│   │\n│   ├── 05_Implementation/\n│   │   ├── Standards/\n│   │   ├── Build_Handoffs/\n│   │   └── Supporting/\n│   │\n│   ├── 06_Verification/\n│   │   ├── Verification_Reports/\n│   │   ├── Ground_Truth/\n│   │   └── Handoffs/\n│   │\n│   ├── 07_Data/\n│   │   ├── Acquisition/\n│   │   ├── Retrieval/\n│   │   └── Supporting/\n│   │\n│   └── 08_Shared_Enterprise_Services/\n│       ├── Registries/\n│       ├── Templates/\n│       ├── Shared_Standards/\n│       └── Supporting/\n│\n├── 02_GCE_IDENTITY/\n│   │\n│   ├── Don/\n│   ├── Coda/\n│   ├── Vittorio/\n│   ├── Chiave/\n│   ├── Nico/\n│   ├── Corrado/\n│   ├── Falcon/\n│   ├── Talon/\n│   ├── Keel/\n│   ├── Luce/\n│   ├── Ragno/\n│   ├── Magpie/\n│   ├── Pigeon/\n│   └── Raven/\n│\n├── 03_PROJECTS/\n│   │\n│   ├── 00_Project_Index/\n│   │\n│   ├── GCE_Framework_Reconciliation/\n│   │   ├── 00_CURRENT/\n│   │   ├── 01_Handoffs/\n│   │   ├── 02_Recon/\n│   │   ├── 03_Registries/\n│   │   ├── 04_Decisions/\n│   │   └── 90_Historical/\n│   │\n│   ├── GCE_Stack/\n│   │   ├── 00_CURRENT/\n│   │   ├── 01_Handoffs/\n│   │   ├── 02_VoiceBridge/\n│   │   ├── 03_Web_Bridge/\n│   │   ├── 04_Transport/\n│   │   ├── 05_State_Sync/\n│   │   ├── 06_Runtime_Plumbing/\n│   │   ├── 07_Local_Services/\n│   │   ├── 08_APIs_Adapters/\n│   │   ├── 09_Dev_Utilities/\n│   │   ├── 10_Command_Center_Tech/\n│   │   ├── 11_Walking_Capture/\n│   │   └── 90_Historical/\n│   │\n│   ├── EC8_Edge_Crew/\n│   │   ├── 00_CURRENT/\n│   │   ├── 01_Handoffs/\n│   │   ├── MLB/\n│   │   ├── NCAA/\n│   │   ├── Parent_Quant/\n│   │   └── Historical/\n│   │\n│   └── [OTHER PROJECTS]/\n│\n├── 04_GCE_DON/\n│   │\n│   ├── 00_Current_Operating_Surface/\n│   ├── 01_Command_Center/\n│   ├── 02_Working_Handoffs/\n│   ├── 03_Decision_Queue/\n│   ├── 04_Inbox_Intake/\n│   └── 90_Temporary_Working/\n│\n├── 05_REGISTRIES/\n│   │\n│   ├── Master_Artifact_Register/\n│   ├── Authority_Register/\n│   ├── Project_Register/\n│   ├── Handoff_Register/\n│   ├── Supersession_Register/\n│   ├── Model_Test_Register/\n│   └── Verification_Register/\n│\n└── 06_FROZEN_STATE_AND_ARCHIVE/\n    │\n    ├── 01_Superseded/\n    ├── 02_Historical_Framework/\n    ├── 03_Historical_Identity/\n    ├── 04_Completed_Projects/\n    ├── 05_Old_Handoffs/\n    ├── 06_Migration_Records/\n    └── 99_Cold_Archive/\n```\n\n### The important routing trick\n\nThe folder tree should answer **two different questions** without mixing them:\n\n**`01_GCE_ORG` answers:** *Who/functionally owns this kind of work?*  \n**`03_PROJECTS` answers:** *Where does the actual implementation truth live?*\n\nThat distinction is already canonical: Framework owns authority, seat doctrine, canon, supersession, cross-project reconciliation, taxonomy, and promotion of reusable lessons; Projects own code, active methodology, project artifacts, and execution. fileciteturn0file0L273-L304\n\nSo, for example:\n\n```text\nArchitecture question\n    ↓\n01_GCE_ORG/03_Architecture\n    ↓\nChiave ruling / architecture handoff\n    ↓\n03_PROJECTS/GCE_Stack\n    ↓\nNico implementation\n    ↓\n01_GCE_ORG/06_Verification\n    ↓\nLuce verification\n```\n\nThat is the part that will make **our handoffs dramatically cleaner**.\n\n## The handoff convention I want us to use\n\nInside every serious project, use the same small spine:\n\n```text\nPROJECT_NAME/\n├── 00_CURRENT/\n├── 01_HANDOFFS/\n├── 02_WORK/\n├── 03_REGISTRY/\n├── 04_DECISIONS/\n└── 90_HISTORICAL/\n```\n\nThen a fresh session never has to hunt.\n\n`00_CURRENT` = what is true **right now**.  \n`01_HANDOFFS` = session/seat transfer packages.  \n`02_WORK` = working material appropriate to that project.  \n`03_REGISTRY` = indexes/state/artifact maps.  \n`04_DECISIONS` = accepted Don/gate rulings.  \n`90_HISTORICAL` = superseded but preserved material.\n\nThis directly serves the end-state defined in the handoff: a fresh human/model should be able to determine what is current, historical, authoritative, project-owned, superseded, and where new work belongs **without inferring it from filenames**. fileciteturn0file0L421-L436\n\n### One thing I would **not** do\n\nI would **not** make the top-level Drive:\n\n```text\nCoda/\nVittorio/\nChiave/\nNico/\nCorrado/\n...\n```\n\nThat would recreate the exact coupling we're removing.\n\nSeats belong under **Identity**. Functions belong under **ORG**. Projects belong under **Projects**. The taxonomy should represent durable functions rather than whatever model or seat happens to occupy the function at a moment in time. fileciteturn0file0L135-L163\n\nAnd this lines up very closely with the existing Drive baseline already identified — `GCE_ORG`, `03_Projects`, and `06_Frozen_State_and_Archive`, plus the functional estates already present. So we're **evolving the current Drive, not replacing it with another architecture.** fileciteturn0file0L210-L242\n\n**For the Cable Car cleanup we're doing right now, this is the structure I'd use as the target map.** We can take each existing Drive folder and mark it **KEEP → TARGET PATH / MOVE → TARGET PATH / SUPERSEDE / ARCHIVE**, rather than trying to reorganize the whole estate from scratch."]}, "create_time": 1790266636.384269, "end_turn": true, "id": "f027dd99-709d-4f11-a82e-ea9c90a1f80b", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 596, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "4b08ab6c-d4c9-4c5d-92b7-cfb9d659d414", "cited_message_idx": 17, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_ccb2b8102f588191a4d36e8ed94d401b", "line_range": [185, 207], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 0, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id": "file_00000000c87c81fdb13b0867b8c8b55b", "name": "Pasted text.txt", "source": "my_files", "text": "6. KNOWN CURRENT ROOT MODEL\n==================================================\nCurrent local root doctrine should be reconciled around:", "type": "file"}, "start_ix": 565}, {"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 4176, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "4b08ab6c-d4c9-4c5d-92b7-cfb9d659d414", "cited_message_idx": 17, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_ccb2b8102f588191a4d36e8ed94d401b", "line_range": [273, 304], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 0, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id": "file_00000000c87c81fdb13b0867b8c8b5