hip must not be conflated.\n\nA Nico-created artifact must be representable as Nico-created without pretending Nico has Don authority.\n\nIf needed separate:\n\n    created_by.seat\n    authority_source / authority_level\n    requested_destination\n\nPreserve routing-as-hint semantics.\n\nDo not make destination own the artifact.\n\nDo not perform Google Drive writes.\n\n==================================================\n11. STORAGE / TAXONOMY\n==================================================\n\nDO NOT perform the big migration yet.\n\nFreeze this principle in implementation/config/docs where required:\n\n    PROJECT-SCOPED → PROJECT ROOT\n    FRAMEWORK-GENERAL → GCE_ORG\n    IDENTITY → GCE_IDENTITY\n    ROUTING → REGISTRY / METADATA / TRANSPORT\n    DESTINATION SEAT ≠ ARTIFACT OWNER\n\nThe existing 06_HANDOFFS tree should not be deleted.\n\nWhere runtime clients currently depend on it:\n- freeze/supersede as appropriate\n- re-point safely\n- maintain compatibility if necessary\n\nDo not create another fifth handoff bus.\n\n==================================================\n12. THINGS NOT TO DO\n==================================================\n\nDO NOT:\n\n- start another broad taxonomy study\n- ask Don to rule on trivial implementation choices\n- create certification slices\n- create a second routing architecture\n- rewrite historical handoffs\n- mass-move EC8\n- move active project roots\n- touch Google Drive\n- rename seats\n- reopen frozen roster\n- introduce model names into authority fields\n- break existing working bootstrap behavior\n- wait for perfect archival cleanup before fixing live control-plane defects\n\n==================================================\n13. ESCALATION STANDARD\n==================================================\n\nNico should solve implementation details.\n\nEscalate ONLY if the pass encounters a genuine authority contradiction that changes the intended behavior.\n\nExamples worthy of stopping:\n\n- two live canonical source