ACT\nExact schema and example.\n\nG. DEVPAD CAROUSEL STATE\nWhat works now:\n- highlighted next seat?\n- click-to-load?\n- project/workstream persistence?\n- gate/confidence visibility?\n\nH. CABLE CAR STATE\nWhat schema/transport changes were made.\n\nI. COMPATIBILITY\nWhat old paths remain and why.\n\nJ. TESTS\nExact test commands/results.\n\nK. REMAINING DEBT\nOnly debt that is genuinely outside this pass.\n\nL. DON ACTION\nIdeally:\n    NONE — READY FOR LUCE VERIFY\nIf Don actually must rule, state ONE precise decision and why implementation cannot safely choose.\n\n==================================================\n16. SUCCESS CONDITION\n==================================================\n\nThis pass succeeds when Don can stop being the clipboard/router.\n\nA project runtime must be able to say:\n\n    I am EC8 / Parent Quant.\n    Nico is acting.\n    Luce is next.\n    This is a verification gate.\n    Confidence is X.\n    Load Luce without changing project ownership.\n\nAnd the infrastructure must know how to carry that state cleanly.\n\nONE PASS.\n\nUse sub-agents.\nBuild it.\nTest it.\nReturn to Luce only after it is materially done.\n```\n\nThat is the right **Nico mandate** now.\n\nLuce already gave us enough evidence to stop studying: it found the four competing buses, identity-directory pollution, free-text `NEXT_ROUTE`, incomplete carousel dimensions, and the Cable Car schema mismatch. fileciteturn1file0L9-L13 fileciteturn1file0L37-L41\n\nAnd I deliberately **did not make Nico solve the giant archive/migration cleanup**. Luce's own sequence says the live blockers are authority/bootstrap → footer contract → project-aware board → cwd → Cable Car, *then* project-handoff migration. fileciteturn1file0L48-L53\n\n**That’s the one-pass kill shot: fix the causes, not spend today moving 165 files around.**"]}, "create_time": 1790367598.004088, "end_turn": true, "id": "47691c7a-e228-4baf-81fc-d4d5e8729e3d", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations