r multiply lives in explicit appendices.\n\n# GCE SESSION HEADER — CORE\n\n```text\nGCE SESSION HEADER\n\nTIMESTAMP:            2026-09-25 16:56 PT\nAUTHORITY:            Don\nPRIMARY SEAT:         Coda\nOCCUPANT / MODEL:     GPT-5.6 Sol\nMODE:                 Reconciliation\nCURRENT THREAD:       Framework Taxonomy / Routing Reconciliation\nCURRENT CONTEXT:      Reconcile live machine state against frozen Framework authority,\n                      then prepare the bounded Nico correction package.\nMATURITY:             POC | DEVELOPMENT | VALIDATION | PRODUCTION-READY | PRODUCTION\nSTATUS:               ACTIVE\nCONFIDENCE:           97%\nCURRENT ANCHOR:       <current authoritative artifact / ruling / handoff>\n```\n\nThat is the **orientation block**.\n\nThe important distinctions are now explicit:\n\n- **MODE** = what kind of work we are doing: `RECONCILIATION`, `IMPLEMENTATION`, `VERIFICATION`, `ARCHITECTURE`, etc.\n- **CURRENT THREAD** = the named thing we are talking about.\n- **CURRENT CONTEXT** = one or two sentences explaining where we are inside that thread.\n- **MATURITY** = how mature the thing is.\n- **STATUS** = what the session itself is doing.\n- **CONFIDENCE** = current confidence in the active frame/state.\n\n---\n\n# SESSION HEADER APPENDIX — ACTIVE CONTEXT BOARD\n\nThis sits **immediately underneath the header**.\n\n```text\nACTIVE CONTEXT APPENDIX\n\nPROMOTED / CURRENT:\n  Framework Taxonomy / Routing Reconciliation\n\nPARKED IN THIS THREAD:\n  1. Cable Car / Google Drive handoff transport\n     State: functional transport; schema/taxonomy reconciliation pending\n\n  2. Session Controller / Carousel\n     State: concept accepted; implementation intentionally deferred\n\n  3. Open Handoff utility\n     State: Nico implementation spec prepared\n\n  4. Mobile Orchestration / Vomit Runtime\n     State: architectural concept; not current implementation lane\n```\n\nThis is the piece I think is going to help us enormously.\n\nWhen you say:\n\n> “Hold