t belongs in the core header**, because it describes the lifecycle of the overall thread/workstream, not whichever item happens to be promoted today.\n\nAnd I like where you're going with it: this becomes the first piece of **session/workstream KPIs**.\n\nI would add a compact lifecycle block:\n\n```text\nSTARTED:              2026-09-23 15:59 PT\nDAYS RUNNING:         3\nACTIVE DAYS:          3\nLAST ACTIVE:          2026-09-25 16:56 PT\n```\n\nBut I want the semantics deterministic:\n\n- **STARTED** = timestamp the overall thread/workstream was established.\n- **DAYS RUNNING** = calendar days from `STARTED` through now, inclusive. This keeps it human-readable: started Wednesday, working Friday = Day 3.\n- **ACTIVE DAYS** = distinct calendar days on which the thread actually had recorded activity.\n- **LAST ACTIVE** = latest recorded activity timestamp.\n\nLater we can add deeper KPIs without bloating the header: elapsed hours, active work hours, number of handoffs, seat transitions, gates passed, blockers, rework loops, average confidence, etc. Those belong in a **KPI appendix**, not the core header.\n\nSo the revised header becomes:\n\n```text\n==================================================\nGCE SESSION HEADER\n==================================================\n\nTIMESTAMP:            2026-09-25 16:56 PT\nAUTHORITY:            Don\nPRIMARY SEAT:         Coda\nOCCUPANT / MODEL:     GPT-5.6 Sol\n\nMODE:                 RECONCILIATION\nCURRENT THREAD:       Framework Taxonomy / Routing Reconciliation\nCURRENT CONTEXT:      Reconciling live machine state against frozen\n                      Framework authority before implementation.\n\nMATURITY:             DEVELOPMENT\nSTATUS:               ACTIVE\nCONFIDENCE:           97%\n\nSTARTED:              <original thread/workstream timestamp>\nDAYS RUNNING:         <calculated automatically>\nACTIVE DAYS:          <calculated from recorded activity>\nLAST ACTIVE:          <latest activity timestamp>\n\nCURRENT ANCHOR:       <current authoritative artifact>\n```\n\nThen below it remains:\n\n```text\n--------------------------------------------------\nACTIVE CONTEXT APPENDIX\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nPROMOTED / CURRENT:\n- Taxonomy / Routing Reconciliation\n\nPARKED:\n- Cable Car\n- Session Controller / Carousel\n- Open Handoff\n- Mobile Orchestration\n```\n\n### And here's the important design rule\n\n**Promotion does not reset the clock.**\n\nIf we spend Monday on taxonomy, Tuesday on Cable Car, Wednesday back on taxonomy, this is still the same overall thread:\n\n```text\nSTARTED:       Monday\nDAYS RUNNING:  3\nACTIVE DAYS:   3\n```\n\nThe promoted item changes. The lifecycle doesn't.\n\nThat gives us the beginnings of actual operational telemetry instead of vibes about how long something has been going.\n\nEventually we should be able to say:\n\n> **Project has been running 11 days, 7 active days, 18 handoffs, 4 gates, 2 blockers, 1 rework loop, 96% current confidence.**\n\nNow we're starting to measure the Framework itself."]}, "create_time": 1790380942.237699, "end_turn": true, "id": "f95cef02-66e8-4a68-a488-67b1dbe4ddab", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "b42myu", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id": "6tgq2b", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "2": {"edited": false, "id": "1xwirv", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "3": {"edited": false, "id": "6pkeld", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}}, "content_references": [], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_tokens": [200002], "type": "stop"}, "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab43fca21d0819183966405a724bf5d", "is_complete": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "7153a48a-c1f8-4877-b5fa-0746f8da9624", "request_id": "cceb1f56-af6e-4f94-bcb1-f6c1c61a09d5", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "story_events": [], "turn_exchange_id": "165a78b3-94c6-4526-aa9e-a37a35afbb6b", "working_turn_id": "165a78b3-94c6-4526-aa9e-a37a35afbb6b"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790380957.366065, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "user"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Also in the header, I want priority: high, medium, low. That's all we need, high, medium, low. Right? So right now the dev pad is high priority. Something like Voice Bridge tweaks is low priority. Session controller, high, medium priority. Right?"]}, "create_time": 1790380969.5418, "end_turn": null, "id": "c66c509f-db6f-479d-b890-b687894e335f", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "dictation": true, "dictation_asset_format": "m4a", "dictation_asset_pointer": "sediment://file_00000000353c81fb979d20fbf9e3e94a", "dictation_auto_submitted": true, "dictation_edited": false, "dictation_original_text": "Also in the header, I want priority: high, medium, low. That's all we need, high, medium, low. Right? So right now the dev pad is high priority. Something like Voice Bridge tweaks is low priority. Session controller, high, medium priority. Right?", "message_source": null, "request_id": "7a8b34fd-d48c-475d-9096-3ecdf3cf7b5c", "triggered_by_system_hint_suggestion": false, "turn_exchange_id": "b3e8d362-0b40-4337-aefe-b3eb2bc3ea37", "working_turn_id": "b3e8d362-0b40-4337-aefe-b3eb2bc3ea37"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790380983.543158, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "system"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": [""]}, "create_time": 1790380972.865583, "end_turn": null, "id": "2ed315d9-af89-4063-9015-06d666a9553c", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "chime_version": 1, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab43fca21d0819183966405a724bf5d", "is_visually_hidden_from_conversation": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "parent_id": "5d907ee0-7de0-4fdc-a82b-f1ecd9578290", "request_id": "7a8b34fd-d48c-475d-9096-3ecdf3cf7b5c", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "turn_exchange_id": "b3e8d362-0b40-4337-aefe-b3eb2bc3ea37", "working_turn_id": "b3e8d362-0b40-4337-aefe-b3eb2bc3ea37"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790380972.865583, "weight": 0}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yes. **Priority belongs in the core header** because it tells the whole team how much attention/resources the current thread deserves.\n\nAnd keep it deliberately simple:\n\n**HIGH · MEDIUM · LOW**\n\nNo P0/P1/P2, no five-level scoring system.\n\nI’d put it beside maturity/status:\n\n```text\n==================================================\nGCE SESSION HEADER\n==================================================\n\nTIMESTAMP:            2026-09-25 16:56 PT\nAUTHORITY:            Don\nPRIMARY SEAT:         Coda\nOCCUPANT / MODEL:     GPT-5.6 Sol\n\nMODE:                 RECONCILIATION\nCURRENT THREAD:       Framework Taxonomy / Routing Reconciliation\nCURRENT CONTEXT:      Reconciling live machine state against frozen\n                      Framework authority before implementation.\n\nPRIORITY:             HIGH\nMATURITY:             DEVELOPMENT\nSTATUS:               ACTIVE\nCONFIDENCE:           97%\n\nSTARTED:              <original start timestamp>\nDAYS RUNNING:         <automatic>\nACTIVE DAYS:          <automatic>\nLAST ACTIVE:          <automatic>\n\nCURRENT ANCHOR:       <current authoritative artifact>\n```\n\nAnd I’d define the priority semantics tightly:\n\n- **HIGH** — central build, active blocker, production-critical, or something Don is actively driving. **Main DevPad** is a good example.\n- **MEDIUM** — important enabling work, but it doesn't displace the primary build. **Session Controller/Carousel** could sit here while DevPad is the active high-priority work.\n- **LOW** — worthwhile improvement/tweak that can wait without materially blocking the estate. **VoiceBridge polish/tweaks** is the right example.\n\nThe useful future behavior is that **priority becomes routable metadata**, too. If five parked threads exist, the Framework doesn't have to guess what Don cares about:\n\n```text\nHIGH     DevPad\nMEDIUM   Session Controller\nLOW      VoiceBridge tweaks\n```\n\nThen when we start building the KPI layer, we can measure things like **days running by priority, aging high-priority work, high-priority blockers, and time spent on low-priority work while high-priority work remains blocked.**\n\nThat's operationally useful without making the header complicated."]}, "create_time": 1790380972.889518, "end_turn": true, "id": "1d4a50dc-5c8a-4cc4-8d40-74d661719bd8", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "c3mwiw", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id": "jcg5e8", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}}, "content_references": [], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_tokens": [200002], "type": "stop"}, "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab43fca21d0819183966405a724bf5d", "is_complete": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "2ed315d9-af89-4063-9015-06d666a9553c", "request_id": "7a8b34fd-d48c-475d-9096-3ecdf3cf7b5c", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "story_events": [], "turn_exchange_id": "b3e8d362-0b40-4337-aefe-b3eb2bc3ea37", "working_turn_id": "b3e8d362-0b40-4337-aefe-b3eb2bc3ea37"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790382709