s actually trying to achieve>\n\nCONTEXT:\n<why this matters / what surrounding constraint or situation applies>\n```\n\nFor example, from what you just said:\n\n```text\nDON INTENT SNAPSHOT\n\nRAW INTENT:\nDon wants every voice-to-text input reduced to a short, visible interpretation\nso he can immediately validate whether the session understood him correctly.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\nExpose intent before execution so misunderstandings are caught early\nwithout forcing Don to rewrite or formalize his raw voice input.\n\nCONTEXT:\nThis is especially important in long-running sessions with multiple promoted\nand parked workstreams, where raw voice input may jump context quickly.\n```\n\nAnd I’d add one rule: **this block is interpretive, not authoritative.**\n\nIf you say, “No, that’s not what I meant,” we correct the snapshot immediately. It should never silently become canon just because I summarized you.\n\nSo the header stack is now:\n\n```text\nGCE SESSION HEADER\n- timestamp\n- authority\n- primary seat\n- occupant/model\n- mode\n- current thread\n- current context\n- priority\n- maturity\n- status\n- confidence\n- started\n- days running\n- active days\n- last active\n- current anchor\n\nHEADER APPENDIX A — DON INTENT SNAPSHOT\n- raw intent\n- objective\n- context\n\nHEADER APPENDIX B — ACTIVE CONTEXT BOARD\n- promoted/current\n- parked\n```\n\nThat gives you a really nice visual check at the top of every session:\n\n**What are we doing? Why are we doing it? Did the system understand me? What else is parked?**"]}, "create_time": 1790381019.996262, "end_turn": true, "id": "919fea18-0511-44b1-9f6b-6a627bcdbfc4", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "0u2z4d", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id": "aptuse", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "2": {"edited": false, "id": "low3pp", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}}, "content_references": [], "conversati