ture amendment  \\n**Sources:** Kimi methodology `v0.3.1` in both archives; fixed `HANDOFF_v0.3.1`; Chiave `Architecture Specification v1.0` / `EC8_Architecure_Brief.txt`; production prompts 01-09.\\n\\nClaim labels used below: **FACT**, **DERIVED**, **PROPOSED**, **UNKNOWN**, **CONFLICT**, **OUTSIDE AUTHORITY**.\\n\\n## 1. Executive Reconciliation\\n\\n**FACT:** The intended system is a scheduled MLB Sovereign Analysis Pipeline. It creates five independent analyst landscapes, not a consensus pick, validates each analysis through L1/L2/L3, normalizes confidence, and emits immutable SAP artifacts.\\n\\n**FACT:** The accepted architecture is structurally aligned with the accepted methodology on isolation, request-gated evidence delivery, market-persona exclusivity, forward-only validation, deterministic G4, effective-N, provenance, metering, and terminal `SAP-PreGame`.\\n\\n**CONFLICT / record defect:** The fixed handoff declares “Ready for Coder,” while Chiave v1.0 declares “Post-gate, pre-build,” companion methodology pending six v0.3.2 record fixes, and Phase 0 still has exit criteria. This is a status contradiction, not permission to choose a side.\\n\\n**CONFLICT:** The package's older architecture brief and v0.3 source retain OnDemand and an `OnDemand` framing enum; the accepted v0.3.1 methodology and Chiave v1.0 remove OnDemand from pilot scope and bind the build to the corrected enum. The old artifacts are provenance only.\\n\\n**CONFLICT:** Ruling IDs drift. In the handoff, CR-1..CR-4 are evidence gating, deterministic G4, cost, and framing. In Chiave v1.0, CR-1 is evidence gating, CR-2 is OnDemand scope/revival conditions, CR-3 is cost, CR-4 is G4, and CR-5 is framing. The fixed methodology text also assigns differing names to CR-2/CR-4 in places.\\n\\n**IMPLEMENTATION CLARIFICATION REQUIRED:** “53 calls/slate” is a budget fact, but the supplied documents do not provide a machine-checkable call decomposition. Fresh framing is required for Overnight, Morning, and Pre-Game, yet Overnight is described as one call and full runs as 26. The ledger must count actual calls; Kimi/Chiave must document the intended baseline decomposition before budget assertions become tests.\\n\\n**VERDICT:** **PARTIALLY BLOCKED.** Phase 0 store/secrets design and non-semantic orchestration scaffolding can proceed. Framing scheduler, call-budget assertions, ruling-keyed traceability, terminal artifact binding, and any OnDemand surface are blocked until the named record/contract questions are resolved.\\n\\n## 2. System Intent Summary\\n\\n**FACT:** Within the final 24-hour window for each scheduled MLB slate, ingest the slate and create a schema-enumerated framing snapshot; acquire evidence into an append-only provenance store; run five isolated, heterogeneous, persona-specific analysts; let each request and receive only its own evidence; continue each analyst in-session for re-analysis; validate forward-only through deterministic L1, pairwise different-family L2, and outside-pool L3; normalize from four preserved inputs; and seal an immutable nine-section SAP landscape.\\n\\nCadence is Overnight (framing/store population only), Morning (full analyst run), and Pre-Game (full analyst run; terminal). Prior snapshots remain records and are never delivered. Market-class evidence is exclusive to Persona D. Missing data remains explicit. Retries, exclusions, effective-N, integrity, provenance, and provider/token cost are recorded. Pilot scope is one scheduled MLB slate, N=5, full validation, and four seeded failures. No consensus, EV engine, human arbitration, trigger reruns, or pilot OnDemand.\\n\\n## 3. Methodology -> Architecture Traceability\\n\\n| Methodology requirement | Source | Architecture contract | Status | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Five independent personas; no peer context | Methodology §§1, 3.2, 5; prompts 02-06 | I2, EX-1, EX-6 | Exact | Architecture adds process/container/network/env isolation and canaries. |\\n| Analysts self-determine gaps | §§1.4 P2, Stage 2 | IF-3, DA-4 | Exact | Store may be broad; delivery is request-gated. |\\n| Package invariant | §§2.5, Stage 2 | I1, IF-2 | Exact | Single choke point and audit are machine-enforced. |\\n| Evidence identity and cumulative delivery | §2.5 | IF-2, DA-1/2/3 | Partial | `acquired_in_run` and complete status-map shape need schema binding. |\\n| Market evidence only Persona D | §4.3; prompt 05 | IF-2/3, SE-4 | Exact | Boundary and re-check are explicit. |\\n| Intra-run continuity; inter-run freshness | §2.6, Stage 3 | EX-3 | Exact | Retry also stays in same session per VL-6. |\\n| Heterogeneity | §3 Stage 1 | EX-2 | Partial | Architecture gives >=3 families and pairwise L2 rule; provider assignment/registry is not supplied. |\\n| Three validation layers; no skip | §4 | VL-1..7, I3/I5 | Exact | L1 semantic router is architecture completion under standing rulings. |\\n| G4 deterministic classification/retry | §7.1 | VL-2, VL-5, VL-6 | Exact | Observable classification tests are methodology-owned. |\\n| Forward-only validation | §4 | I3, VL-7 | Exact | Corrections are replacement evidence only. |\\n| Normalizer four inputs, neutral/stateless | §5, prompt 09 | NO-1..6 | Exact | Selection/reasoning/peers forbidden. |\\n| Confidence tiers and effective-N | §§5-6 | IF-4, NO-4/6 | Partial | Tier enum is methodology-owned; artifact schema version is architecture-owned and not yet pinned. |\\n| Integrity report | §3/Stage 6 | IF-4, I7 | Exact | Includes contamination, gates, anomalies, continuity. |\\n| Terminal SAP-PreGame; Morning retained | §2.3-2.4, §6 | IF-4 | Exact | Older source's SAP-OnDemand is stale for pilot. |\\n| Append-only evidence/provenance/replay | §§2, 6, 9 | DA-1..5, I4/I9 | Exact | Re-execution verifies process, not historical result. |\\n| Cost measurement at execution point | §9 | I10, OB-1..4 | Partial | Unit is fixed; 53-call decomposition and provider pricing binding are unresolved. |\\n| Failure behavior | §§7, 7.1 | §7 Failure Domains, checkpoints | Partial | Checkpoint/resume is architecture completion; acquisition threshold semantics remain underspecified. |\\n\\n## 4. Architecture -> Methodology Back-Trace\\n\\n| Architecture contract | Authorizing source | Classification | Trace / issue |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| I1/IF-2 package choke point | Methodology package invariant; CR-1 | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | Exact. |\\n| I2/EX-1 isolation and canaries | P1 and §5 controls | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | Container/process granularity is architecture-owned completion. |\\n| I3/VL-7 forward-only | Stage 4 forward-only rule | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | Exact. |\\n| I4 replay-as-record | Provenance/artifact requirements | REASONABLY DERIVED | Canonical replay semantics are architecture-owned completion; no methodology conflict found. |\\n| I6 machine-checkable gates | §7.1 G4 ruling | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | Exact. |\\n| IF-1 fixed `0.3-MLB`; no OnDemand | schema §3.1 plus accepted v0.3.1 scope | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | The `OnDemand` enum in older artifacts is stale. |\\n| IF-4 independent artifact schema and immutability | Stage 6 plus architecture ownership | ARCHITECTURE-OWNED COMPLETION | Binding version and store immutability require implementation contract. |\\n| VL-2 L1 semantic router | G4 determinism and gates-as-checkpoints standing rulings | ARCHITECTURE-OWNED COMPLETION | Explicitly flagged by Chiave; not a new methodology ruling. |\\n| Checkpoint/resume at each gate | gates-as-checkpoints standing ruling | ARCHITECTURE-OWNED COMPLETION | Requires persistence semantics and idempotency contract. |\\n| L3 fallback pre-approved/configured/exercised | methodology L3 fallback requirement | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | Operations coordination belongs to Talon; implementation must expose the hook. |\\n| SE-1..7 security boundaries | prompt/data isolation and trust requirements | REASONABLY DERIVED | Security implementation is Chiave-owned; OnDemand trust boundary is deferred. |\\n| OB-3 provider abstraction metering | methodology cost ledger | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | Exact provider/invoice integration is not specified. |\\n\\nNo supplied architecture contract was found to authorize a consensus engine, EV engine, trigger-based rerun, human arbitration, market access for non-D, or pilot OnDemand.\\n\\n## 5. Discrepancy Register\\n\\n| ID | Classification | Source A | Source B | Conflict / impact | Owner | Gate |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| D-01 | status drift | HANDOFF §1-2, §9 | Chiave v1.0 header/§10 | “Coder unblocked/ready” vs post-gate/pre-build and pending v0.3.2 fixes. | Coda | GOVERNANCE / DON DECISION |\\n| D-02 | stale handoff | HANDOFF §9 | Chiave v1.0 §0/§14 | Handoff says architecture brief does not exist; supplied canonical architecture does. | Coda | NON-BLOCKING RECORD FIX |\\n| D-03 | ruling-ID drift | methodology changelog; HANDOFF §4 | Chiave §12 | Same CR IDs carry different ruling names; traceability tests cannot bind safely. | Coda + Kimi + Chiave | GOVERNANCE / DON DECISION |\\n| D-04 | semantic conflict | old v0.3 / old architecture brief | accepted v0.3.1 + Chiave v1.0 | OnDemand and enum retained in old records but removed from pilot. | Coda | NON-BLOCKING RECORD FIX; pilot surface blocked |\\n| D-05 | version drift | Chiave §0/§14 | handoff title/status | Architecture v1.0 references methodology v0.3.1 pending v0.3.2 record fixes; handoff calls v0.3.1 complete. | Kimi + Coda | IMPLEMENTATION CLARIFICATION REQUIRED |\\n| D-06 | implementation ambiguity | methodology §2, §9 | Chiave OB-4 | 53 total / 26 full-run calls is not decomposed against three framing snapshots and all stages. | Kimi + Chiave | ARCHITECTURE GATE |\\n| D-07 | implementation ambiguity | methodology §2.1/§2.6 | Chiave IF-1/§7 | “Fresh framing snapshot” may imply a model invocation, but only Overnight=1 and full-run=26 are budgeted. | Kimi | METHODOLOGY GATE |\\n| D-08 | missing contract | Stage 2 G2 | Chiave §7 | `>threshold%` has no value, denominator, or action when unmet; partial mode is described but not parameterized. | Kimi | METHODOLOGY GATE |\\n| D-09 | missing contract | Stage 2/IF-3 | Chiave IF-3 | Semantic deduplication, requester-to-item mapping, and cumulative status-map schema are not specified enough for deterministic replay. | Kimi + Chiave | IMPLEMENTATION CLARIFICATION REQUIRED |\\n| D-10 | missing contract | prompts/README | EX-2 | “Different architecture family” registry and assignment algorithm are absent; normalization family constraints are absent. | Chiave | ARCHITECTURE GATE |\\n| D-11 | missing contract | Stage 6 | IF-4 | Artifact schema version and exact nine-section JSON contract are not supplied. | Chiave | ARCHITECTURE GATE |\\n| D-12 | textual drift | methodology versions | Chiave §14 | Pending six fixes include Stage 6 terminal line, ruling numbering, attribution, H1 version; source package does not include accepted v0.3.2. | Kimi | METHODOLOGY GATE |\\n| D-13 | scope ambiguity | methodology handoff | Chiave §11 | “one MLB slate” versus handoff definition of slate as one scheduled game; multi-game execution topology is unclear. | Don + Kimi | GOVERNANCE / DON DECISION |\\n| D-14 | operational boundary | Chiave §7/§13 | pilot/handoff | Checkpoint/resume and L3 fallback require deployment, persistence, and recovery behavior not owned by coder alone. | Talon + Chiave | IMPLEMENTATION CLARIFICATION REQUIRED |\\n\\n## 6. Version / Ruling Crosswalk\\n\\n| Subject | Safe binding now | Unsafe/stale reference |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Methodology | Accepted `EC8_AI_Convergence_v0.3.1.md` content as supplied, with v0.3.2 record fixes unresolved | `EC8_AI_Convergence_v0.3.md` as normative source |\\n| Architecture | `Architecture Specification v1.0` / `EC8_Architecure_Brief.txt` | Older `Chiave_Architecture_Brief.md` that still exposes OnDemand |\\n| Framing schema | `0.3-MLB`, `run_context ∈ {Overnight, Morning, PreGame}` | Any schema containing `OnDemand`; old schema text with divergent enum |\\n| Prompts | Fixed handoff prompts 01-09, prompt package v0.3 | Prompt copies without manifest/hash binding |\\n| Artifact | Nine sections; terminal `SAP-PreGame`; schema version must be assigned by Chiave | `SAP-OnDemand` for pilot; unversioned artifact JSON |\\n| Rulings | Content can be implemented only after a canonical ID map is issued | Binding tests to CR number alone |\\n\\n## 7. Implementation Contract By Pipeline Stage\\n\\nThe following is a translation of accepted contracts, not production code.\\n\\n| Stage | Inputs / outputs | Must never receive | State / session | Access / failure | Provenance / metering | Gate |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Acquisition | Raw slate/source requests -> immutable evidence items/status | Peer outputs, analyst reasoning; secrets in payloads | Persistent append-only store; acquisition execution ephemeral | Source failure => `unfilled(reason)`; no silent substitution | SHA-256 identity, source, time, reliability, run type, expiration; meter acquisition at execution | Source item valid and stored or explicit status |\\n| Framing | Raw slate + trusted structured inputs -> `0.3-MLB` snapshot | Analyst outputs, prose judgment, prior snapshot delivery | Snapshot persistent; framing call isolated | Invalid schema blocks G0; no OnDemand pilot context | model/prompt/params/runtime metadata; one ledger entry per actual call | G0 |\\n| Analyst first pass | Current framing snapshot + training knowledge -> structured preliminary analysis and gap requests | Peers, N, peer personas, divergence, prior runs, unrequested evidence, market data unless D | Fresh context per run; continuous into Stage 3 | Execution failure retry/exclude per slot; contamination recorded | analyst canary, model family, prompt/params, session ID; provider ledger | G1 |\\n| Gap-request router | Analyst-owned structured requests -> authorized acquisition work/status | Peer request content for delivery; market requests from non-D | Ephemeral routing plus persistent request lifecycle | Malformed => `unfilled(malformed_request)`; non-D market => `access_denied` + event | requester persona, request ID, policy decision, timestamps | Every request authorized and traceable |\\n| Evidence acquisition | Authorized requests/store -> immutable items | Analyst outputs and peer context | Persistent store; no analyst session | Partial mode; `unfilled` reason; never mutate item | Per-item lineage and acquisition ledger | G2 inputs available; unresolved threshold contract D-08 |\\n| Package assembler | Current snapshot + that analyst's requested/cumulative items + status map -> package | Peer items/reasoning/gaps, prior snapshots, non-D market | Single choke point; package ephemeral, audit persistent | Any invariant breach => G6-style failure/block | package hash, item IDs, disclosure line, audit record | I1/IF-2 audit passes |\\n| Analyst re-analysis | Same session + package -> final analysis | Validation reports, peer data, sealed corrections as commentary | Same session as first pass; retry same session; fresh next run | Incomplete/hallucination => G3 action; correction only as replacement evidence | session transcript sealed; all evidence IDs | G3 |\\n| L1 | Analysis + package + registries -> mechanical report / semantic classification event | Peer outputs; analyst raw confidence is not needed | Stateless per analysis; persisted report | Failure routes through L2 classification; never skip | test IDs, registry versions, timestamps; ledger only if model router invoked (L1 itself no model call) | VL-1/VL-2 |\\n| L2 | Analysis + evidence/package + L1 report -> pairwise validation | Raw analyst confidence; peer analysts; wrong-family validator | Independent validator context; report sealed | FAIL classified; correctable retry once, second FAIL exclude; execution failure blocks/retries | validator model family, report hash, class/test IDs, ledger | VL-3/VL-6 |\\n| L3 | Analysis + L1/L2 reports -> red-team report | Analyst pool identity/context beyond allowed input;