tion Contract by Pipeline Stage\\r\\n\\r\\n   Acquisition / overnight pre-fetch / Stage 2c — In: slate schedule,\\r\\n   proactive list, gap requests. Out: provenance-tagged immutable store\\r\\n   items. Never receives: analyst outputs, package destinies. State:\\r\\n   persistent append-only SHA-256 (DA-1/2). Session: none. Access: trust\\r\\n   boundary (SE-1), market-class tagging. Failure: partial-data mode,\\r\\n   unfilled(reason). Provenance: DA-3 mandatory. Metering: per-source log,\\r\\n   non-billable. Gate: schema + provenance complete before commit.\\r\\n\\r\\n   Framing — In: pre-fetched raw slate only (\\\"You do NOT fetch data…\\\").\\r\\n   Out: schema 0.3-MLB, null+reason-code. Never receives: analyst outputs,\\r\\n   evidence, prior snapshots. State: snapshot persisted as record; never\\r\\n   delivered to analysts (M28). Session: stateless, 1/run. Access: isolated\\r\\n   from analysts. Failure: malformed → anomaly re-run; structural → G0\\r\\n   reject. Provenance: schema_version, generated_at, per-field sources.\\r\\n   Metering: 1 billable request/run. Gate G0: resolvable matchups, valid\\r\\n   window, schema validates.\\r\\n\\r\\n   Analyst first pass — In: current framing snapshot only; gap statuses\\r\\n   null. Out: preliminary conviction, information_gaps[], calibration,\\r\\n   self-critique. Never receives: peers, evidence, N, personas, market\\r\\n   class (non-D). State: canary injected. Session: opens the one session.\\r\\n   Access: separate context, unique prompt/params. Failure: re-run or\\r\\n   exclude; contamination → G1 investigation. Provenance:\\r\\n   execution-metadata capture. Metering: 5/run. Gate G1: all 5 complete,\\r\\n   coherent gaps, canary clean.\\r\\n\\r\\n   Gap-request router — In: 5 gap lists. Out: structured requests {entity,\\r\\n   attribute, timeframe, granularity, data class}, dedup, feasibility\\r\\n   flags. Never receives: reasoning/selections. State: persistent\\r\\n   per-analyst request log. Session: code (DR-07 contract required).\\r\\n   Access: non-D market request → access_denied + event. Failure: malformed\\r\\n   → unfilled(malformed_request). Provenance: requester→request→outcome\\r\\n   map. Metering: non-billable (confirm). Gate: every item classified\\r\\n   before dispatch.\\r\\n\\r\\n   Evidence acquisition (Stage 2c) — as Acquisition, plus Gate G2 (DR-06:\\r\\n   threshold UNKNOWN — proceed with partial data, flag severe gaps until\\r\\n   Kimi pins it).\\r\\n\\r\\n   Package assembler (IF-2 choke point) — In: framing snapshot, store items\\r\\n   matching analyst request history, cumulative request_status map. Out:\\r\\n   snapshot + own requested evidence + status map — nothing else, ever\\r\\n   (I1). Never receives into package: peer evidence, market class for non-D\\r\\n   (except baseline lines — DR-18), prior snapshots, validation outputs.\\r\\n   State: ephemeral, logged, reconstructable. Access: single choke point;\\r\\n   role-keyed market filter (IF-3 + re-verified). Failure: any\\r\\n   un-reconstructable item = G6 failure. Provenance: disclosure line (M29).\\r\\n   Metering: n/a. Gate: package audit passes.\\r\\n\\r\\n   Analyst re-analysis (Stage 3) — In: same session; package; replacement\\r\\n   evidence items only on G4 retry. Out: final selection/Pass, raw\\r\\n   confidence, cited reasoning, key evidence, residual uncertainty,\\r\\n   self-critique; system-populated gap statuses. Never receives: 7.3's list\\r\\n   + sealed validation reports. State: transcript sealed at run end (EX-3).\\r\\n   Session: same session as Stage 1. Failure: incomplete → G3 re-run.\\r\\n   Metering: 5/run, token-heavy (full context). Gate G3: structured,\\r\\n   traceable, uncertainties flagged.\\r\\n\\r\\n   Validation L1 — In: analyst outputs, package, framing. Out:\\r\\n   PASS/FLAG/FAIL; mechanical classes decided here (CH-1/2/4/5, CO-1/2/4);\\r\\n   semantic FAILs routed to L2 (VL-2). State: deterministic,\\r\\n   replay-consistent. Session: none, no model call. Failure: blocks entry;\\r\\n   never skipped. Provenance: findings + routed classes logged. Metering:\\r\\n   none. Gate: every FAIL classified or routed.\\r\\n\\r\\n   Validation L2 — In: analyst output minus raw confidence, package,\\r\\n   framing; L1-routed FAILs. Out: PASS/FLAG/FAIL + failure_class, test_id,\\r\\n   classification_reason. Never receives: raw confidence, peers, normalized\\r\\n   tier. State: sealed on FAIL. Access: family ≠ analyst, per pair.\\r\\n   Failure: blocks entry; retry; never skipped. Metering: 5/run + retries.\\r\\n   Gate: every FAIL classified (no runtime judgment — CR-2).\\r\\n\\r\\n   Validation L3 — In: analyst output + L1 + L2 reports. Out: as L2 +\\r\\n   red-team opinion. Access: outside pool; fallback pre-approved,\\r\\n   configured, exercised before pilot. Failure: primary outage → fallback;\\r\\n   fallback outage → block, never bypass. Metering: 5/run + retries. Gate:\\r\\n   G4 action table executes deterministically.\\r\\n\\r\\n   Normalizer — In: exactly {self-assessment, sufficiency score\\r\\n   (deterministic: fill_rate × weighted_reliability × conflict_penalty ×\\r\\n   recency_decay), validation state, flags}. Out: tier + justification +\\r\\n   all four inputs preserved. Never receives: reasoning, selection, peers,\\r\\n   matchup context. State: stateless, per-analyst, no batching. Failure:\\r\\n   blocks whole artifact; never bypassed. Provenance: input-set version\\r\\n   (NO-3). Metering: 5/run. Gate G5: tiered + justified; FAIL analysts\\r\\n   never Conviction/Lean.\\r\\n\\r\\n   SAP assembler — In: all stage outputs, effective-N, integrity data. Out:\\r\\n   nine-section SAP; exclusions {analyst, layer, class, test_id, detail,\\r\\n   retry_number, action}. Must not synthesize a system pick or blend.\\r\\n   State: immutable after G6. Failure: re-assemble. Gate G6: nine sections,\\r\\n   effective-N, provenance, integrity report, no contamination.\\r\\n\\r\\n   Artifact store — In: G6-passed artifacts only. Out: immutable\\r\\n   retrievable artifacts; SAP-PreGame flagged terminal. State: persistent;\\r\\n   snapshots join backup set. Failure: abort + DA-5 restore; no artifact\\r\\n   preferable to a wrong artifact. Gate: G6 is the only write path.\\r\\n\\r\\n   ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\n   8. Decisions the Implementation Engineer Is Not Permitted to Make\\r\\n\\r\\n   N (=5); persona definitions/count; framing schema fields/enums/versions;\\r\\n   package contents (I1 — no \\\"helpful\\\" additions); evidence push (CR-1);\\r\\n   market-class scope and recipients (incl. not stripping baseline lines —\\r\\n   DR-18); validation layer count/order/skippability/blindness; G4\\r\\n   classes/tests/actions/retry counts (no second retry, no runtime-judgment\\r\\n   escapes); forward-only topology (corrections only as replacement\\r\\n   evidence); normalization inputs/blindness/tier enum; artifact\\r\\n   sections/terminal semantics/immutability; effective-N definitions\\r\\n   (retries → ledger, not ran_n); cadence/timing/new run types (no\\r\\n   on-demand surface, stubs, or \\\"temporary\\\" triggers); session semantics\\r\\n   (Stage 3 is continuation, not fresh); request_status enum/lifecycle;\\r\\n   cost caps (none exist — measure only); contamination methodology; slate\\r\\n   definition; isolation mechanisms; G4 exclusions are final (no\\r\\n   promote/revive).\\r\\n\\r\\n   Unresolved embedded choices — route before coding that surface: G2\\r\\n   threshold (DR-06); gap free-text→structured mapping (DR-07); artifact\\r\\n   schema version (DR-08); prompt \\\"lines\\\" sentence scope (DR-18);\\r\\n   normalization threshold normativity (DR-17).\\r\\n\\r\\n   Ordinary discretion allowed: vendor selection within EX-2;\\r\\n   language/framework; infrastructure; parser internals post-DR-07; tests;\\r\\n   dashboards.\\r\\n\\r\\n   ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\n   9. Routed Questions\\r\\n\\r\\n   ┌─────┬──────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┐\\r\\n   │ #   │ Question                         │ Seat                        │\\r\\n   ├─────┼──────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤\\r\\n   │ Q1  │ Canonical methodology stamp;     │ Kimi + Coda                 │\\r\\n   │     │ retire S2 (DR-03)                │                             │\\r\\n   ├─────┼──────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤\\r\\n   │ Q2  │ Ruling-ID crosswalk              │ Coda                        │\\r\\n   │     │ adjudication; interim            │                             │\\r\\n   │     │ content-keyed binding (DR-02)    │                             │\\r\\n   ├─────┼──────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤\\r\\n   │ Q3  │ G2 threshold                     │ Kimi (Don only if business) │\\r\\n   │     │ value/denominator/action (DR-06) │                             │\\r\\n   ├─────┼──────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤\\r\\n   │ Q4  │ Artifact schema version (DR-08)  │ Chiave                      │\\r\\n   ├─────┼──────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤\\r\\n   │ Q5  │ Gap free-text→IF-3 structured    │ Kimi + Chiave               │\\r\\n   │     │ mapping + dedup (DR-07)          │                             │\\r\\n   ├─────┼──────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤\\r\\n   │ Q6  │ Prompt \\\"no lines\\\" scope vs       │ Kimi                        │\\r\\n   │     │ baseline framing lines (DR-18)   │                             │\\r\\n   ├─────┼──────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤\\r\\n   │ Q7  │ Prompt 09 numeric thresholds     │ Kimi                        │\\r\\n   │     │ normative? (DR-17)               │                             │\\r\\n   ├─────┼──────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤\\r\\n   │ Q8  │ Refresh S4 §14; align I1         │ Chiave                      │\\r\\n   │     │ wording; fix filename typo       │                             │\\r\\n   │     │ (DR-04/12)                       │                             │\\r\\n   ├─────┼──────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤\\r\\n   │ Q9  │ On-demand revival policy lines — │ Don                         │\\r\\n   │     │ post-pilot only (CR-2)           │                             │\\r\\n   ├─────┼──────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤\\r\\n   │ Q10 │ Checkpoint/resume + L3 fallback  │ Talon + Chiave              │\\r\\n   │     │ ops contract (DR-15)             │                             │\\r\\n   ├─────┼──────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┤\\r\\n   │ Q11 │ Provider slot assignments        │ No ruling needed —          │\\r\\n   │     │                                  │ Implementation/Talon within │\\r\\n   │     │                                  │ EX-2; Luce verifies         │\\r\\n   └─────┴──────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────┘\\r\\n\\r\\n   ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\n   10. Implementation Readiness Verdict\\r\\n\\r\\n   PARTIALLY BLOCKED\\r\\n\\r\\n   READY WITH NON-BLOCKING FIXES (start now): Phase 0 (store DA-1..5,\\r\\n   secrets SE-5, schema); Phase 1 (provider abstraction, ledger hooks OB-3,\\r\\n   emit-points OB-5); non-semantic scaffolding. No blocked surface touches\\r\\n   these.\\r\\n\\r\\n   BLOCKED SURFACES: ① G2 gate assertions (DR-06) · ② artifact schema\\r\\n   binding (DR-08) · ③ gap-router semantics (DR-07) · ④ package-assembler\\r\\n   market-filter semantics (DR-18) · ⑤ ruling-keyed test traceability\\r\\n   pending CR crosswalk (DR-02).\\r\\n\\r\\n   Downgraded from v0.1 (now specified): framing scheduler/call-budget\\r\\n   tests; overnight model-call question; multi-game slate topology;\\r\\n   on-demand; evidence delivery model.\\r\\n\\r\\n   No execution evidence was supplied — all claims are\\r\\n   FACT/DERIVED/CONFLICT from records, not VERIFIED. This is translation,\\r\\n   not certification (Luce's seat).\\r\\n\\r\\n   ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\n   11. Recommended Next Handoff\\r\\n\\r\\n   1. Coda (one session): DR-01/02/03 — readiness contradiction, CR\\r\\n      crosswalk, canonical stamp. Unblocks the \\\"unblocked\\\" claim.\\r\\n   2. Kimi: v0.3.2 record stamp over S1; pin G2 (Q3); gap-mapping contract\\r\\n      (Q5); prompt wording fixes (Q6/DR-18); re-version prompts (DR-09);\\r\\n      correct S5 §9/§11 (DR-10/11).\\r\\n   3. Chiave: artifact schema version (Q4); refresh §14; align I1; rename\\r\\n      spec file per its own closing instruction.\\r\\n   4. Implementation (parallel, now): Phase 0 + Phase 1 against §7; bind\\r\\n      records by content hash.\\r\\n   5. Luce: verification evidence matrix for the four seeded pilot failures\\r\\n      so Phase 3 acceptance is checkable on arrival.\\r\\n   6. Talon: scheduling + L3-fallback operational contract in parallel —\\r\\n      needed by Phase 2, not Phase 0.\\r\\n\\r\\n   ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\n   Boundary note: this document reconciles and translates only. No\\r\\n   methodology, architecture, or governance rulings were made; every\\r\\n   recommendation is labeled PROPOSED, and every conflict is routed, not\\r\\n   harmonized. The strongest single finding for Don's attention: the\\r\\n   handoff says \\\"coder unblocked\\\" while Chiave's canonical spec says\\r\\n   \\\"post-gate, pre-build\\\" — the gap is now proven to be record-sized\\r\\n   (DR-01–DR-04), and closing it is a Coda session, not a redesign.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbDb_a_VcRXbmfD04q0Zl2QneWvY67RYtC1n8uZRMfs/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"EC8_Runtime_Design_GLM5.1_v1.0\",\"id\":\"1IbDb_a_VcRXbmfD04q0Zl2QneWvY67RYtC1n8uZRMfs\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"10093\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T15:52:56.904Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T15:52:58.752Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T15:52:58.752Z\",\"display_title\":\"EC8_Runtime_Design_GLM5.1_v1.0\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbDb_a_VcRXbmfD04q0Zl2QneWvY67RYtC1n8uZRMfs/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1-2XT7kaaOIIu8aqjcGFIPF_ktPF0N9vQ\"],\"shared\":true,\"content\":\"﻿# EC8 AI Convergence — Independent Runtime / Model Design Pass v1.0\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Seat**: GLM 5.1 — Independent Design & Build authority (not architecture governance, not methodology ownership)\\r\\n**Date**: 2026-09-06\\r\\n**Posture**: Convert methodology requirements + Chiave Architecture v1.1 constraints + K1–K9 handoff into a concrete, cost-aware runtime design. No methodology modified. No architecture modified. No governance decisions.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Claim tags**: GIVEN | DERIVED | PROPOSED | UNKNOWN | OUTSIDE AUTHORITY\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 0. Source Constraints (Read, Not Authored)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| Source | Key Constraints Extracted |\\r\\n|--------|--------------------------|\\r\\n| Methodology v0.3.1 (S1) | N=5 analysts; 3 scheduled runs/slate (Overnight=1 framing call, Morning=26, PreGame=26); 53 calls/slate; ~795 calls/15-game day; ≥3 model families; L1=deterministic code; L2≠analyst family per pair; L3 outside pool; normalization blind; no on-demand |\\r\\n| Chiave Architecture v1.1 | PR-1 family taxonomy = provider→lineage→model→version; PR-2 registry pre-flight check; EX-2 heterogeneity machine-checkable; FB-1/2 L3 fallback pre-approved; CK-3 crash-restart ≤2/analyst/run; I9 provenance from execution metadata only |\\r\\n| Reconciliation v0.2 | DR-14↑ family taxonomy undefined (blocks EX-2 machine-check); DR-22 G4 registries missing; DR-24 contamination mechanisms unspecified; Phase 0/1 startable, Phase 2 blocked |\\r\\n| Prompt package 01–09 | 9 distinct system prompts; structured JSON output required per prompt; temperature 0.3–0.7 range recommended per persona |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 1. Model-Family Taxonomy (PROPOSED — per PR-1, awaiting Chiave formal pin via DR-14↑)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHierarchy: `provider_org → foundation_lineage (family_id) → model → version`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| family_id | provider_org | Foundation Lineage | Bedrock Available |\\r\\n|-----------|-------------|-------------------|-------------------|\\r\\n| `anthropic-claude` | Anthropic | Claude (Transformer, RLHF/Constitutional) | YES |\\r\\n| `meta-llama` | Meta | Llama (Dense+MoE Transformer, open weights) | YES |\\r\\n| `mistral` | Mistral AI | Mistral (Sparse MoE Transformer) | YES |\\r\\n| `deepseek` | DeepSeek | DeepSeek (MoE Transformer, DeepSeek-specific) | YES |\\r\\n| `amazon-nova` | Amazon | Nova (Amazon-built Transformer) | YES |\\r\\n| `minimax` | MiniMax | MiniMax (MoE Transformer) | YES |\\r\\n| `google-gemma` | Google | Gemma (Dense Transformer, open weights) | YES |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Distinct orgs sharing a lineage do not satisfy EX-2** (PR-1). Same org with distinct lineages may. All seven families above are distinct lineages from distinct orgs — they satisfy EX-2 pairwise.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**UNKNOWN**: Whether Kimi/Chiave accept this exact taxonomy. DR-14↑ blocks the machine-check until formally pinned. This design proceeds against this proposed taxonomy as the compliance criterion.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 2. Bedrock Pricing Reference (GIVEN — us-east-1, standard tier, 2026-09-06)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| Model | family_id | Input/1M tok | Output/1M tok | Structured Output | Context Window |\\r\\n|-------|-----------|-------------|--------------|-------------------|---------------|\\r\\n| Claude 3.5 Sonnet v2 | anthropic-claude | $3.00 | $15.00 | JSON mode | 200K |\\r\\n| Claude 3 Haiku | anthropic-claude | $0.80 | $4.00 | JSON mode | 200K |\\r\\n| Llama 3.3 70B Instruct | meta-llama | $0.36 | $1.46 | Tool call | 128K |\\r\\n| Llama 3.1 8B Instruct | meta-llama | $0.12 | $0.24 | Tool call | 128K |\\r\\n| Mistral Small 24B | mistral | $0.08 | $0.24 | JSON mode | 32K |\\r\\n| Mistral Large 3 | mistral | $0.50 | $1.50 | JSON mode | 128K |\\r\\n| DeepSeek v3.2 | deepseek | $0.62 | $1.85 | JSON mode | 128K |\\r\\n| Amazon Nova Pro | amazon-nova | $0.80 | $3.20 | JSON mode | 300K |\\r\\n| Amazon Nova Lite | amazon-nova | $0.06 | $0.24 | JSON mode | 300K |\\r\\n| Amazon Nova Micro | amazon-nova | $0.035 | $0.14 | JSON mode | 128K |\\r\\n| MiniMax M2.5 | minimax | $0.30 | $1.20 | JSON mode | 1M |\\r\\n| Gemma 3 27B IT | google-gemma | $0.23 | $0.38 | JSON mode | 128K |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**UNKNOWN**: Exact Bedrock model IDs for some models (see §4 manifest). Claude 3.5 Sonnet v2 pricing shown is standard on-demand; extended-access variant is $6/$30. Llama 4 model IDs and pricing not yet confirmed on Bedrock (checked 2026-09-06 — Llama 4 section present but model rows not rendered in pricing page scrape). Pricing may have changed since scrape.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 3. Token Estimates (DERIVED — per-prompt, single-matchup slate)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| Stage | Prompt ID | Est. Input Tokens | Est. Output Tokens | Reasoning |\\r\\n|-------|-----------|------------------|-------------------|-----------|\\r\\n| Framing | P01 | 4,000 | 2,000 | Raw slate data → fixed schema. Input is pre-fetched data (~3K) + system prompt (~1K). Output is populated JSON. |\\r\\n| Analyst 1st pass | P02–P06 | 6,000 | 1,500 | System prompt (~2K) + framing schema (~2K) + gap status map (~2K). First pass: no evidence yet. |\\r\\n| Analyst re-analysis | P02–P06 | 20,000 | 2,000 | System prompt + framing + full evidence package (~10K cumulative) + first-pass context carried in session. This is the token-heavy call (OB-1). |\\r\\n| L2 Validation | P07 | 12,000 | 1,000 | System prompt (~2K) + analyst output (~2K) + evidence package (~6K) + framing (~2K). No raw confidence. |\\r\\n| L3 Validation | P08 | 16,000 | 1,500 | System prompt (~2K) + analyst output (~2K) + L1 report (~0.5K) + L2 report (~1K) + evidence (~8K) + framing (~2K). Red-team scope is broader. |\\r\\n| Normalization | P09 | 3,000 | 500 | System prompt (~2K) + 4 structured inputs (~1K). Tightly constrained. |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Note**: Analyst re-analysis carries the full first-pass context (EX-3: same session). The 20K input estimate accounts for evidence accumulation across runs (IF-2 cumulative delivery). Pre-Game runs may carry more accumulated evidence than Morning runs.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 4. Runtime Assignment Matrix — Profile A: Cost-Optimized\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Goal**: Minimum sufficient intelligence. Cheapest model that reliably satisfies the contract for each stage.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### 4.1 Primary Assignments\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| Stage | Prompt ID | Calls/Run | Required Capability | Proposed Model | family_id | Bedrock Model ID | Structured Output | Context Req | Reasoning Level | Temp | Timeout | Retry |\\r\\n|-------|-----------|-----------|--------------------|---------------|-----------|------------------|-------------------|-------------|----------------|------|---------|-------|\\r\\n| Framing | P01 | 1 | Schema fill, zero discretion | Amazon Nova Micro | amazon-nova | `amazon.nova-micro-v1:0` | JSON mode | 128K | Low | 0.1 | 30s | 1 |\\r\\n| Analyst A (Situational) | P02 | 1+1 | Contextual reasoning, evidence citation | DeepSeek v3.2 | deepseek | `deepseek.deepseek-v3:0` | JSON mode | 128K | Medium | 0.5 | 120s | 1 |\\r\\n| Analyst B (Form) | P03 | 1+1 | Trend/regression reasoning | Meta Llama 3.3 70B | meta-llama | `meta.llama3-3-70b-instruct-v1:0` | Tool call | 128K | Medium | 0.4 | 120s | 1 |\\r\\n| Analyst C (Structural) | P04 | 1+1 | Matchup/tactical reasoning | Mistral Small 24B | mistral | `mistral.mistral-small-2407-v1:0` | JSON mode | 32K | Medium | 0.3 | 120s | 1 |\\r\\n| Analyst D (Market) | P05 | 1+1 | Market/behavioral reasoning | MiniMax M2.5 | minimax | `minimax.m2-5-v1:0` | JSON mode | 1M | Medium | 0.6 | 120s | 1 |\\r\\n| Analyst E (Micro) | P06 | 1+1 | Process metrics, statistical reasoning | Amazon Nova Pro | amazon-nova | `amazon.nova-pro-v1:0` | JSON mode | 300K | Medium-High | 0.3 | 120s | 1 |\\r\\n| L2 Validation | P07 | 5 | Factual checking, classification | Per-analyst (see §4.2) | varies | varies | JSON mode | varies | Medium | 0.2 | 90s | 1 |\\r\\n| L3 Validation | P08 | 5 | Red-team, missed evidence | Google Gemma 3 27B IT | google-gemma | `google.gemma3-27b-it-v1:0` | JSON mode | 128K | Medium | 0.3 | 120s | 1 |\\r\\n| Normalization | P09 | 5 | 4-input→5-tier, constrained | Amazon Nova Micro | amazon-nova | `amazon.nova-micro-v1:0` | JSON mode | 128K | Low | 0.1 | 30s | 1 |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Calls/Run notation**: \\\"1+1\\\" = 1 first-pass + 1 re-analysis (same session, two provider requests per EX-3). L2/L3/Normalization = 5 calls per run (one per analyst).\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### 4.2 L2 Per-Analyst Assignment (EX-2: different family from target analyst)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| Validates Analyst | Target family_id | L2 Model | L2 family_id | Bedrock Model ID | Input/1M | Output/1M |\\r\\n|-------------------|-----------------|----------|-------------|------------------|----------|-----------|\\r\\n| A (Situational) | deepseek | Amazon Nova Lite | amazon-nova | `amazon.nova-lite-v1:0` | $0.06 | $0.24 |\\r\\n| B (Form) | meta-llama | Amazon Nova Lite | amazon-nova | `amazon.nova-lite-v1:0` | $0.06 | $0.24 |\\r\\n| C (Structural) | mistral | Amazon Nova Lite | amazon-nova | `amazon.nova-lite-v1:0` | $0.06 | $0.24 |\\r\\n| D (Market) | minimax | Amazon Nova Lite | amazon-nova | `amazon.nova-lite-v1:0` | $0.06 | $0.24 |\\r\\n| E (Micro) | amazon-nova | Mistral Small 24B | mistral | `mistral.mistral-small-2407-v1:0` | $0.08 | $0.24 |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Rationale**: Nova Lite ($0.06/$0.24) is the cheapest capable model