 Manager | Talon | Provider abstraction (fallback) |\\r\\n| `SPORTS_DATA_API_KEY` | MLB data feeds (Statcast, etc.) | AWS Secrets Manager | Talon | Evidence acquisition engine |\\r\\n| `ODDS_API_KEY` | Market data feeds | AWS Secrets Manager | Talon | Evidence acquisition (Market persona) |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Never logged. Never committed. Never echoed.** (SE-5, workspace doctrine)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 15. Implementation Configuration Manifest (Stub — for coder)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n```yaml\\r\\nec8:\\r\\n  gateway: bedrock\\r\\n  region: us-east-1\\r\\n  cross_region_profile: us  # us-east-1 + us-east-2 + us-west-2\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n  profiles:\\r\\n    cost_optimized:  # Profile A\\r\\n      framing:\\r\\n        model: nova-micro\\r\\n        temperature: 0.1\\r\\n        max_tokens: 2048\\r\\n        timeout_ms: 30000\\r\\n        retry: 1\\r\\n      analysts:\\r\\n        A_situational:\\r\\n          model: deepseek-v32\\r\\n          temperature: 0.5\\r\\n          max_tokens: 2048\\r\\n          timeout_ms: 120000\\r\\n          retry: 1\\r\\n          family_id: deepseek\\r\\n        B_form:\\r\\n          model: llama-33-70b\\r\\n          temperature: 0.4\\r\\n          max_tokens: 2048\\r\\n          timeout_ms: 120000\\r\\n          retry: 1\\r\\n          family_id: meta-llama\\r\\n        C_structural:\\r\\n          model: mistral-small-24b\\r\\n          temperature: 0.3\\r\\n          max_tokens: 2048\\r\\n          timeout_ms: 120000\\r\\n          retry: 1\\r\\n          family_id: mistral\\r\\n        D_market:\\r\\n          model: minimax-m25\\r\\n          temperature: 0.6\\r\\n          max_tokens: 2048\\r\\n          timeout_ms: 120000\\r\\n          retry: 1\\r\\n          family_id: minimax\\r\\n        E_micro:\\r\\n          model: nova-pro\\r\\n          temperature: 0.3\\r\\n          max_tokens: 2048\\r\\n          timeout_ms: 120000\\r\\n          retry: 1\\r\\n          family_id: amazon-nova\\r\\n      validation:\\r\\n        L2:\\r\\n          A: {model: nova-lite, family_id: amazon-nova}\\r\\n          B: {model: nova-lite, family_id: amazon-nova}\\r\\n          C: {model: nova-lite, family_id: amazon-nova}\\r\\n          D: {model: nova-lite, family_id: amazon-nova}\\r\\n          E: {model: mistral-small-24b, family_id: mistral}\\r\\n          temperature: 0.2\\r\\n          timeout_ms: 90000\\r\\n        L3:\\r\\n          model: gemma3-27b\\r\\n          family_id: google-gemma\\r\\n          fallback: claude-3-haiku\\r\\n          fallback_family_id: anthropic-claude\\r\\n          temperature: 0.3\\r\\n          timeout_ms: 120000\\r\\n      normalization:\\r\\n        model: nova-micro\\r\\n        temperature: 0.1\\r\\n        max_tokens: 512\\r\\n        timeout_ms: 30000\\r\\n        retry: 1\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n  ledger:\\r\\n    unit: provider_billable_request\\r\\n    fields: [provider, model, input_tokens, output_tokens, cost_per_call, cumulative_slate_cost]\\r\\n    emit_point: provider_abstraction_layer  # OB-3\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n  registry:\\r\\n    pre_flight_check: true  # PR-2: validate EX-2 before any model call\\r\\n    version: 1\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 16. Risks / Unknowns\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| ID | Risk | Severity | Mitigation | Owner |\\r\\n|----|------|----------|------------|-------|\\r\\n| R1 | Mistral Small 24B may be insufficient for Analyst C (Structural) — matchup/tactical reasoning is complex | Medium | Profile B upgrades to Mistral Large 3 for that slot; monitor G4 exclusion rate | Implementation + Talon |\\r\\n| R2 | Nova Micro may produce malformed JSON for framing schema — small models sometimes skip fields | Medium | Fallback to Nova Lite; pre-flight schema validation; retry once | Implementation |\\r\\n| R3 | Gemma 3 27B (Profile A L3) may lack reasoning depth for red-team task | High | Profile B uses Claude 3 Haiku for L3; if Gemma underperforms, escalate to Profile B for L3 only | Implementation + Don |\\r\\n| R4 | Bedrock model IDs for 6 models are unverified — may differ from assumed IDs | Medium | Verify against `aws bedrock list-foundation-models` before Phase 1 build | Talon |\\r\\n| R5 | Llama 3.3 70B uses tool-call mode, not native JSON mode — output parsing may fail | Low | Prompt-level JSON instruction + output parser with fallback | Implementation |\\r\\n| R6 | Family taxonomy (§1) is PROPOSED, not pinned — DR-14↑ blocks machine-check until Chiave formalizes | High | Design proceeds against proposed taxonomy; implementation must wire registry check against whatever taxonomy is pinned | Chiave |\\r\\n| R7 | L2 fallback may violate EX-2 if fallback model family matches target analyst — must re-check at switchover time | Medium | Pre-flight check (PR-2) applies to fallback too; if no valid fallback, entry blocks | Implementation |\\r\\n| R8 | Nova Lite/Micro context windows (128-300K) sufficient for all stages? Re-analysis with heavy evidence could approach limits. | Low | Monitor token counts; Nova Pro fallback if approaching limit | Talon |\\r\\n| R9 | Cross-region Bedrock inference may have different model availability or pricing | Low | Pin to us-east-1 primary; cross-region as latency fallback only | Talon |\\r\\n| R10 | Prompt caching (Bedrock) could reduce framing input costs if the framing schema prompt is static | Low | Evaluate post-Phase 1; not in baseline cost model | OUTSIDE — optimization |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 17. Highest-Cost Analysis & Substitution Table\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| Slot | Current Model | Cost/Call | Cheapest Viable Sub | Sub Cost/Call | Savings | Quality Degradation Risk |\\r\\n|------|--------------|-----------|--------------------|--------------|---------|-------------------------|\\r\\n| Analyst E re (Profile A) | Nova Pro | $0.02240 | Mistral Small 24B | $0.00208 | $0.02032 | **Likely** — Nova Pro's 300K context + stronger reasoning for process metrics is justified |\\r\\n| Analyst A re (Profile A) | DeepSeek v3.2 | $0.01630 | Llama 3.3 70B | $0.01012 | $0.00618 | Moderate — DeepSeek reasoning quality is stronger for situational synthesis |\\r\\n| Analyst A re (Profile C) | Claude 3.5 Sonnet v2 | $0.09000 | DeepSeek v3.2 | $0.01630 | $0.07370 | Low-Moderate — DeepSeek is strong; Claude adds marginal quality for 5.5x cost |\\r\\n| L3 (Profile B) | Claude 3 Haiku | $0.01880 | Nova Lite | $0.00096 | $0.01784 | **Likely** — Haiku's reasoning for red-team is meaningfully better |\\r\\n| L3 (Profile C) | MiniMax M2.5 | $0.00660 | Gemma 3 27B | $0.00429 | $0.00231 | Low — both are comparable mid-tier |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 18. Recommendation: Profile B (Balanced) for MLB Pilot\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Profile A** ($0.22/slate, $3.36/day) is the cheapest faithful design but carries meaningful risk:\\r\\n- Mistral Small 24B for Analyst C (Structural) may underperform on matchup reasoning\\r\\n- Gemma 3 27B for L3 may lack red-team depth\\r\\n- Nova Micro for framing has higher malformed-output risk\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Profile B** ($0.40/slate, $5.95/day) resolves these risks at modest cost increase:\\r\\n- Analyst B upgraded to Mistral Large 3 (stronger form/trajectory reasoning)\\r\\n- L3 upgraded to Claude 3 Haiku (proven red-team capability)\\r\\n- Framing on Nova Lite (more reliable schema population)\\r\\n- L2 uses stronger models (Llama 3.3 70B / DeepSeek v3.2) for better G4 classification\\r\\n- Still only $178/month at full 15-game cadence — well within \\\"measure first, cap later\\\" (Don #8)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Profile C** ($0.71/slate, $10.65/day) adds Claude 3.5 Sonnet v2 for one analyst lane — 5.5x the cost of DeepSeek for marginal analytical improvement. Not justified for a pilot whose purpose is to *measure* the system, not maximize single-analyst quality.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Recommended**: **Profile B** for pilot. Switch to Profile A for specific stages once measurement confirms smaller models are sufficient. Reserve Profile C for post-pilot quality optimization after calibration data exists.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 19. Answer: Cheapest Faithful Runtime Design\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**The cheapest runtime that faithfully executes the accepted EC8 methodology and Chiave architecture is Profile A at $0.22/slate ($3.36/day at 15 games, $100.86/month).**\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIt satisfies every hard constraint:\\r\\n- **EX-2 heterogeneity**: 5 distinct families in analyst pool ≥ 3 ✓\\r\\n- **L2 family separation**: Every L2 is different family from its target analyst ✓\\r\\n- **L3 outside pool**: google-gemma ∉ {deepseek, meta-llama, mistral, minimax, amazon-nova} ✓\\r\\n- **L3 fallback pre-approved**: Claude 3 Haiku (anthropic-claude) also outside pool ✓\\r\\n- **Framing**: Tightly constrained, zero-discretion task on cheapest capable model ✓\\r\\n- **Normalization**: Tightly constrained 4-input→5-tier on cheapest capable model ✓\\r\\n- **53-call budget**: Maintained (L1 = deterministic code, 0 model calls) ✓\\r\\n- **PR-2 pre-flight check**: Wired into configuration ✓\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe only fidelity risk is whether Mistral Small 24B (Analyst C) and Gemma 3 27B (L3) produce outputs of sufficient quality to pass G4 at acceptable rates. This is an empirical question — exactly the kind the pilot is designed to answer.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 20. Substantive Header\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\nDATE:           2026-09-06\\r\\nSESSION:        EC8-Runtime-Design-Pass-v1.0\\r\\nSEAT:           Chiave (bootstrap loaded; acting as independent Design & Build per task instruction)\\r\\nRUNTIME:        GLM 5.1 (opencode-go/glm-5.1)\\r\\nENVIRONMENT:    Windows / opencode / Bedrock us-east-1\\r\\nCURRENT GATE:   NONE — design output, not gate verdict\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\nSTATUS:         PROCEED\\r\\nCONFIDENCE:     82%\\r\\nREASON:         Design satisfies all hard constraints; cost model grounded in Bedrock pricing; 6 model IDs unverified (R4); family taxonomy proposed not pinned (R6); L3 quality on Gemma uncertain (R3)\\r\\nNEXT GATE:      Verify Bedrock model IDs (R4); Chiave pin family taxonomy (DR-14↑); Kimi resolve DR-20/DR-19\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: Yes — approve Profile B for pilot; confirm family taxonomy; confirm L3 quality threshold\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n*The standard outlives the soldier — whoever ends up carrying it.*\"}]},\"error\":null,\"error_data\":null,\"error_code\":null,\"classification_id\":null,\"json_rpc_error_code\":null,\"error_http_status_code\":null,\"error_http_headers\":null,\"internal\":{\"external_call_time_ms\":2111},\"clamp_errors\":null,\"clamp_rewrites\":null,\"connector_id\":\"connector_5f3c8c41a1e54ad7a76272c89e2554fa\",\"connector_name\":\"Google Drive\",\"action_name\":\"search\",\"is_sync\":false}"}, "create_time": 1790381177.002108, "end_turn": null, "id": "4d95ac28-ec2d-4c8b-a631-4fb95c45bca3", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "chime_version": 1, "classifier_response": "default", "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab43fca21d0819183966405a724bf5d", "invoked_plugin": {}, "invoked_resource": {"api_tool_version": "v2", "app_name": "Google Drive", "contains_mcp_source": false, "description": "Search Google Drive and return file or folder metadata. Calls without `item_type` and `page_token` retain the legacy search and optional best-effort text hydration. An explicit `image`, `document`, or `folder` item type searches exactly one metadata-only provider page; it never fetches file contents, even with `best_effort_fetch=True`. Return the opaque, provider-owned `next_page_token` unchanged as the next request's `page_token`, including when a page has no allowed results. Use short, specific keywords, or omit the query to browse accessible files. Broaden an empty-result search with related terms, abbreviations, or synonyms. `special_filter_query_str` is a raw Google Drive v3 `q` filter for MIME type, modification time, ownership, sharing, or folder selection. Set `req