nCORE FILING RULE\\r\\nGoogle Drive follows the same organizational ownership model as the local GCE system.\\r\\nArtifacts are filed under one primary owning department/service or project.\\r\\nCross-department work remains one owned package with contributor evidence, not duplicate copies scattered across departments.\\r\\nHistorical files are preserved as provenance and moved to the archive rather than silently rewritten or deleted.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCANONICAL GCE DRIVE ROOT\\r\\nGCE/\\r\\n├── GCE_ORG/\\r\\n├── 03_Projects/\\r\\n└── 06_Frozen_State_and_Archive/\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGCE_ORG/\\r\\n├── 01_Executive_Council/\\r\\n│   ├── 01_Strategic_Governance/\\r\\n│   │   ├── 00_Anchors_and_Session_Books/\\r\\n│   │   ├── 01_Canon_and_Protocols/\\r\\n│   │   └── 02_Templates_and_Standards/\\r\\n│   ├── 02_Technical_Strategy_Systems_Intelligence/\\r\\n│   │   └── 00_Canon_and_Seat_Records/\\r\\n│   ├── 03_Operations/\\r\\n│   │   ├── 00_Canon_and_Bootstrap/\\r\\n│   │   └── 01_Operations_and_Handoffs/\\r\\n│   └── 04_Architecture/\\r\\n│       ├── 00_Architecture_Investigations/\\r\\n│       └── 01_Canon_and_Seat_Records/\\r\\n├── 02_Shared_Enterprise_Services/\\r\\n│   ├── 01_Data_Intelligence/\\r\\n│   ├── 02_Verification_Ground_Truth/\\r\\n│   │   └── 00_Canon_and_Bootstrap/\\r\\n│   └── 03_QA_Validation/\\r\\n│       └── 02_Test_Cases/\\r\\n└── 03_Implementation/\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n03_Projects/\\r\\n└── 01_Edge_Crew/\\r\\n    └── project-owned working/checkpoint records\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n06_Frozen_State_and_Archive/\\r\\nContains superseded broad-bucket structures, historical backups, frozen ZIPs, and legacy Coda/Strategic Advisor Drive structures retained for provenance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT ACTIVE DOCUMENT OWNERSHIP\\r\\nStrategic Governance / Canon and Protocols:\\r\\n- GCE_MODEL_ONBOARDING_OPERATING_PROCEDURE_CURRENT_2026-09-05\\r\\n- GCE_NAMING_IDENTITY_PROTOCOL_ONBOARDING_BACKUP\\r\\n- this Drive structure manifest\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nStrategic Governance / Anchors and Session Books:\\r\\n- GCE_FRAMEWORK_ANCHOR_2026-09-05_RUNTIME_ARCHITECTURE_TEAM_WORKFLOW\\r\\n- GCE_SESSION_BOOK_2026-09-05_RUNTIME_ARCHITECTURE_TEAM_WORKFLOW\\r\\n- prior framework anchors/session books retained as chronology/provenance\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOperations / Canon and Bootstrap:\\r\\n- GCE_LIVING_PROMPT_BOOTSTRAP_ENVIRONMENT_SESSION_HEADER_GATE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nArchitecture / Canon and Seat Records:\\r\\n- GCE_GLM_O1_STAGE4_INTERRUPTION_BACKUP_2026-09-02\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVerification / Ground Truth / Canon and Bootstrap:\\r\\n- GCE_LUCE_BOOTSTRAP_APPROVED_2026-09-05\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nQA / Validation / Test Cases:\\r\\n- Monitor\\r\\n- Phone\\r\\n- Identity\\r\\n- Cosmo_Card\\r\\n- Disney Test Case\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nProjects / Edge Crew:\\r\\n- GCE_EDGE_CREW_CLEANUP_RESTRUCTURE_STATUS_2026-09-02.md\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSUPERSEDED DRIVE STRUCTURES\\r\\nThe following former top-level/broad-bucket structures are not the canonical active taxonomy:\\r\\n- 01_Team_and_HR\\r\\n- 02_Technical_Operations\\r\\n- top-level 04_Operations_and_Handoffs\\r\\n- top-level 05_Templates_and_Standards\\r\\n- top-level GCE_Strategic_Advisor_Chat_GPT\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDisposition:\\r\\n- Team_and_HR and Technical_Operations moved intact to 06_Frozen_State_and_Archive with Legacy_ names.\\r\\n- GCE_Strategic_Advisor_Chat_GPT moved intact to 06_Frozen_State_and_Archive as Legacy_GCE_Strategic_Advisor_Chat_GPT_2026-09-05 after current active documents were extracted to departmental homes.\\r\\n- Operations_and_Handoffs moved under Executive Council / Operations.\\r\\n- Templates_and_Standards moved under Executive Council / Strategic Governance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDO NOT\\r\\n- create loose GCE documents at My Drive root when an owning department/project exists;\\r\\n- create top-level folders named after a model/runtime when the artifact is organizational;\\r\\n- duplicate one canonical artifact into multiple departments;\\r\\n- rewrite historical documents solely because current folder paths changed;\\r\\n- infer a department owner from the model that happened to generate a file;\\r\\n- delete legacy folders merely because they are empty or superseded without explicit review.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCROSS-DEPARTMENT TEAM ARTIFACT RULE\\r\\nFor multi-seat work, choose one primary owner based on the work product.\\r\\nExample: the first major team architecture investigation is Architecture-owned because Chiave defines the investigation and final architecture ruling.\\r\\nIts package may contain:\\r\\n1. Chiave master investigation prompt\\r\\n2. Talon / DeepSeek evidence report\\r\\n3. Luce / Big Pickle verification audit\\r\\n4. Chiave final architecture ruling\\r\\n5. Coda governance reconciliation / Don decision\\r\\nThe package remains under Architecture; contributors do not create duplicate departmental copies.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT ARCHITECTURE REVIEW HOLD\\r\\nThe local runtime/provider shell architecture is CURRENT APPROVED STATE — UNDER ARCHITECTURE REVIEW.\\r\\nGoogle Drive filing structure is organizational and should remain stable while runtime-lane placement is evaluated.\\r\\nDo not couple Drive departmental ownership to temporary runtime/provider names.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: PROCEED\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: 100%\\r\\nREASON: The Drive now has a single active departmental taxonomy with projects and archive separated from organizational authority; current active files have explicit owners and legacy broad-bucket structures are preserved outside the active tree.\\r\\nNEXT GATE: file the first Architecture team-investigation package under 04_Architecture/00_Architecture_Investigations, then update active canon only after the verified Chiave/Talon/Luce evidence cycle.\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: No.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BvbYSMtYfP1zA9Stc8UYhBzyqEr0ooL6NaR-ZrWd0GY/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"GCE_SESSION_ANCHOR_2026-09-06_OPERATIONAL_TEAM_LOCK\",\"id\":\"1BvbYSMtYfP1zA9Stc8UYhBzyqEr0ooL6NaR-ZrWd0GY\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"6179\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-07T04:20:14.373Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-07T04:20:45.939Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-07T04:20:45.939Z\",\"display_title\":\"GCE_SESSION_ANCHOR_2026-09-06_OPERATIONAL_TEAM_LOCK\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BvbYSMtYfP1zA9Stc8UYhBzyqEr0ooL6NaR-ZrWd0GY/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1clV7UUxQUcnGLX21ossOWoHGBPs-pM77\"],\"shared\":true,\"content\":\"﻿GCE SESSION ANCHOR — 2026-09-06\\r\\nOPERATIONAL TEAM LOCK / END-OF-SESSION DROP ANCHOR\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\nPreserve the 2026-09-06 settled operating state without reopening locked framework decisions.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCORE DOCTRINE\\r\\nIDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL\\r\\nMODEL != SEAT\\r\\nCLASS / MAFIA RANK != OPERATIONAL ROUTING AUTHORITY\\r\\nSeat function is stable; model occupancy is replaceable.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFINAL WORKING TEAM\\r\\nDon — Peter — final authority / stakeholder / decision owner.\\r\\nCoda — Strategic Governance — ChatGPT 5.6 Sol — governance, authority boundaries, canon/supersession, cross-seat reconciliation.\\r\\nKimi — Technical Stack Methodology — Kimi/Moonshot — methodology and process logic. Made-person name and animal intentionally unassigned.\\r\\nChiave — Architecture — GLM/Z.AI — Chiave · Aquila/Eagle — architecture, contracts, invariants, interfaces, boundaries.\\r\\nTalon — Operations — DeepSeek — Talon · Tasso/Badger — Head of Operations / Lieutenant — routing, sequencing, operational control, bounded work assignment.\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant — functional seat only — current occupant ChatGPT 5.6 Luna — reconciliation, specification, translation, implementation-readiness, blocker/gap exposure, acceptance conditions. No made-person identity.\\r\\nCalibro — Implementation Design & Engineer — current occupant Grok 4.6 — Calibro · Picchio/Woodpecker · Capo — implementation design/how, runtime/provider pins, config, retries/timeouts/fallbacks, cost-quality-reliability tradeoffs, exact downstream design package. Capo != routing. Calibro does not verify Calibro.\\r\\nKeel — Build / Deploy / Test / Evidence Return — Capo / Operations Manager — current runtime still requires live execution vetting.\\r\\nCoder / Implementation Engineer — Soldier — permanent model/identity still OPEN; likely lighter implementation-engineer requirement rather than heavy software-engineering seat.\\r\\nLuce — Verification / Ground Truth — Big Pickle — Luce · Lince/Lynx — independent truth/evidence verification; no build or upstream redesign.\\r\\nQA / Validation — downstream position remains VACANT.\\r\\nOperations family soldiers: Falcon/Data Hound, Pigeon/Transport, Magpie/Secretary-Register, Raven/Documentation.\\r\\nData / Intelligence standalone enterprise service remains retired unless Don explicitly reopens it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAPPROVED WORKING FLOW\\r\\nCouncil-level work may iterate among Don/Coda/Kimi/Chiave as appropriate.\\r\\nThen:\\r\\nCouncil artifact -> Luce pre-Principal-Consultant True Teller certification gate -> Principal Consultant packaging/translation -> Calibro implementation design -> Talon operational routing/control -> Keel execution/build/deploy/test/evidence return -> Luce execution-state verification -> QA/Validation when staffed.\\r\\nCoda governs across the stack and is not a sequential delivery hop.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLUCE PRE-CONSULTANT GATE\\r\\nLuce / Big Pickle is an independent certification gate AFTER Executive Council synthesis/iteration and BEFORE the Principal Consultant.\\r\\nLuce checks completeness, contradictions, unresolved gaps, evidence/ground-truth issues, and downstream-invention risk.\\r\\nLuce does NOT redesign or repair upstream work.\\r\\nDefects route to the proper owner: methodology -> Kimi; architecture -> Chiave; governance -> Coda; Don decision/policy -> Don.\\r\\nClean artifact is certified to proceed.\\r\\nThis gate is intended to reduce dependence on a perfect Principal Consultant occupant and to improve the Principal Consultant prompt over time.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPRINCIPAL CONSULTANT OPERATING RULE\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant is primarily mechanical translation/packaging, not redesign.\\r\\nUse separate implementation/technical and operational lenses where useful while maintaining one coherent source package.\\r\\nMissing or contradictory requirements must not be silently resolved.\\r\\nMechanical escalation form:\\r\\nBLOCKER -> OWNER -> REQUIRED ARTIFACT -> ACCEPTANCE CONDITION -> NEXT ROUTE\\r\\nClaim discipline target: FACT / DERIVED / PROPOSED / UNKNOWN / CONFLICT.\\r\\nFinal package must be executable downstream without invention.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCALIBRO ONBOARDING STATE\\r\\nCalibro bootstrap successfully loaded in a fresh Grok 4.6 session.\\r\\nResolved identity:\\r\\nCalibro · Picchio/Woodpecker · Implementation Design & Engineer · Capo · occupant Grok 4.6 · MODEL != SEAT.\\r\\nValidated authority boundary:\\r\\nOwns implementation design/how, runtime/provider pins, configuration, fallbacks, implementation manifests, design package for Talon/Keel.\\r\\nDoes not own Kimi methodology, Chiave architecture, Coda governance, Don policy, Talon routing, Keel build, or Luce verification.\\r\\nCorrect router doctrine: explicit occupant binding may resolve Grok 4.6 -> Calibro; never encode Grok family = Calibro; unknown/ambiguous seat mapping -> STOP / ASK.\\r\\nFresh monitor/phone acceptance was the planned validation gate; Calibro bootstrap load itself is confirmed successful in this session.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTANDARD BOOTSTRAP / SESSION-HEADER PATTERN\\r\\nApply the concise Calibro startup pattern across active seats without redesigning locked roles or identities.\\r\\nBoot identifies the seat before the current model occupant.\\r\\nInclude explicit OWNS and DOES NOT OWN boundaries.\\r\\nInclude MODEL != SEAT where applicable and rank/class != routing authority where applicable.\\r\\nRequired session header:\\r\\n1. Work item?\\r\\n2. Session name?\\r\\n3. Session ID?\\r\\nIf absent, assign a deterministic ID using the seat naming convention.\\r\\nTalon owns materialization/update work for active-seat bootstrap files and should return a per-seat change manifest plus unresolved canon gaps. Do not invent missing canon.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPRINCIPAL CONSULTANT HOME\\r\\nBecause Luna is a functional occupant, not a made-person identity, stable disk home should be seat-based:\\r\\nC:\\\\Users\\\\Dekan AI Brother\\\\GCE_IDENTITY\\\\Principal_Consultant\\\\\\r\\nBootstrap/launcher may live there (for example AGENTS.md / BOOTSTRAP.md).\\r\\nDo not create a durable Luna identity home merely because Luna is the current occupant.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAD HOC COMMAND CENTER — LOCKED 3x3 TARGET\\r\\nInstance: Don_Orchestrator_Adhoc_Team\\r\\nPurpose: primary Don-led design/build/verification surface.\\r\\nRecommended 3x3 working layout:\\r\\nROW 1: Coda | Kimi | Chiave\\r\\nROW 2: Principal Consultant | Session Dump / Working File | Calibro\\r\\nROW 3: Talon | Keel | Luce\\r\\nPane position reflects workflow, not authority rank.\\r\\nSubordinate/on-demand agents (Falcon, Pigeon, Magpie, Raven, future Coder, contract specialists, QA) do not require permanent panes.\\r\\nPlain Kimi subscription must remain its own methodology surface; do not silently substitute an OpenRouter/Kimi-family model if the devpad cannot launch the intended interface. If implementation cannot preserve the specified Kimi surface, STOP and flag the gap.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nORG-CHART STATE\\r\\nOrganizational architecture is essentially complete and operationally usable.\\r\\nRemaining staffing gaps are not undefined departments:\\r\\n1. Coder / Implementation Engineer permanent occupant still OPEN.\\r\\n2. QA / Validation still VACANT downstream.\\r\\nTomorrow: reconcile filesystem/folder structure against this final org. Do not reopen locked names, animals, ranks, or authority boundaries simply because older folders/docs differ.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHOME-ROOT CLEANUP BOOKEND\\r\\nHome-root cleanup campaign remains CLOSED.\\r\\nDo not reopen generic cleanup unless a new concrete defect appears.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDRIVE / FILE REVIEW — END OF SESSION\\r\\nDrive sweep for GCE files modified on 2026-09-06 confirms current framework, process/gates, onboarding, Luce bootstrap, current handoff, Principal Consultant onboarding, naming/identity backup, and session/anchor documents exist and were modified today.\\r\\nImportant observation: several earlier current/backup docs still reflect the pre-Luce-gate flow (for example Kimi -> Chiave -> Principal Consultant -> Calibro) and therefore should be reconciled tomorrow against this later session anchor rather than treated as proof that the Luce gate was not approved.\\r\\nThis document is the 2026-09-06 end-of-session anchor for the decisions above.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOPEN ITEMS / NEXT SESSION\\r\\n1. Verify/finish Talon materialization of standardized active-seat bootstraps and session headers.\\r\\n2. Confirm Calibro fresh monitor + phone/voice acceptance if not already completed outside this chat.\\r\\n3. Reconcile GCE filesystem/folder structure against final org chart.\\r\\n4. Update current framework/process/handoff documents so the Luce pre-Principal-Consultant certification gate is reflected consistently.\\r\\n5. Test real Talon -> Keel build handoff and vet Keel runtime.\\r\\n6. Audition/fill lightweight Coder / Implementation Engineer seat when needed.\\r\\n7. QA / Validation remains vacant.\\r\\n8. Harden Principal Consultant prompt using Luce findings; reduce verbosity and strengthen traceability/escalation discipline.\\r\\n9. Apply locked 3x3 Ad Hoc Command Center layout when implementation gaps are resolved.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEND-OF-SESSION STATUS\\r\\nSTATUS: CHECKPOINT\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: 99%\\r\\nREASON: Operational team and authority boundaries are effectively settled; current Drive material exists, but several earlier documents need tomorrow's reconciliation to the newly approved Luce certification gate and final working spine.\\r\\nNEXT GATE: Folder-structure + current-doc reconciliation against this anchor, then continue onboarding/execution testing.\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: NONE\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1G36C0A1A3Be7Hcm01MJZENebUCEdLfymELo8KjdwkIg/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"GCE_FRAMEWORK_ANCHOR_2026-09-05_RUNTIME_ARCHITECTURE_TEAM_WORKFLOW\",\"id\":\"1G36C0A1A3Be7Hcm01MJZENebUCEdLfymELo8KjdwkIg\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"4117\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T02:29:37.801Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T02:29:58.463Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T02:29:58.463Z\",\"display_title\":\"GCE_FRAMEWORK_ANCHOR_2026-09-05_RUNTIME_ARCHITECTURE_TEAM_WORKFLOW\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1G36C0A1A3Be7Hcm01MJZENebUCEdLfymELo8KjdwkIg/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1clV7UUxQUcnGLX21ossOWoHGBPs-pM77\"],\"shared\":true,\"content\":\"﻿GCE FRAMEWORK ANCHOR — 2026-09-05\\r\\nRuntime Architecture / Provider Shell Standardization / First Team Investigation Workflow\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\nFast reload anchor for the session that standardized the runtime-shell layer, exposed a material architecture challenge through Chiave/GLM 5.1, and established the first major cross-department team-investigation workflow.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLOCKED / CURRENT STATE\\r\\n1. Core rule remains: IDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL.\\r\\n2. Current provider/runtime shells physically exist under C:\\\\Users\\\\:\\r\\n   - GCE_OpenAI\\r\\n   - GCE_ZAI\\r\\n   - GCE_DeepSeek\\r\\n   - GCE_Moonshot\\r\\n   - GCE_Big_Pickle\\r\\n3. Historical nested runtime paths were successfully moved:\\r\\n   - GCE_Design_Build\\\\glm -> GCE_ZAI\\r\\n   - GCE_Applied_AI_Team\\\\GCE_Deepseek -> GCE_DeepSeek\\r\\n   - GCE_Applied_AI_Team\\\\GCE_kimi -> GCE_Moonshot\\r\\n4. GCE_Applied_AI_Team remains an active Don drop-folder/workflow shell and is NOT legacy.\\r\\n5. GCE_Design_Build is empty and eligible for archive later; GCE_POF remains preserved pending classification.\\r\\n6. Missing identity structure created locally for Kimi, Data_Intelligence, and QA_Validation. No fake vacant-seat identities were created.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT ARCHITECTURE STATUS\\r\\nThe provider-root architecture is CURRENT APPROVED STATE — UNDER ARCHITECTURE REVIEW.\\r\\nDo not treat the runtime placement under C:\\\\Users as permanently immutable until Chiave findings are reconciled.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCHIAVE / GLM 5.1 ARCHITECTURE REVIEW\\r\\nChiave independently returned PASS WITH REQUIRED CHANGES.\\r\\nMaterial findings:\\r\\n- runtime lanes at C:\\\\Users create a separate permission domain and profile-lookalike namespace;\\r\\n- organizational structure is duplicated inside GCE_IDENTITY path prefixes;\\r\\n- a canonical runtime registry is missing;\\r\\n- runtime lane keying needs one coherent definition;\\r\\n- Luce vs Big Pickle and Kimi historical/current records need evidence reconciliation;\\r\\n- a second GCE_DON may exist and must be verified;\\r\\n- live path references, raw-surface leakage, naming drift, credentials, and legacy roots require evidence-led classification.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIMPORTANT GOVERNANCE RULINGS\\r\\n- Do not immediately reverse the completed provider-shell migration.\\r\\n- Do not accept GCE_OpenCode automatically; OpenCode is an execution host shared by multiple models and may be too ambiguous as a lane name.\\r\\n- Current approved Verification identity remains: stable made-person name Luce; runtime/working identity Big Pickle; service Verification / Ground Truth, unless evidence proves a later Don-approved supersession.\\r\\n- Kimi is an Executive Council Technical Strategy / Systems Intelligence seat; older HELD/Kimi_Plumb records must be reconciled against newer approved material, not silently promoted over it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFIRST MAJOR TEAM WORKFLOW\\r\\nArchitecture defines the investigation.\\r\\nOperations executes exhaustive evidence collection.\\r\\nVerification audits the evidence independently.\\r\\nArchitecture rules on verified evidence.\\r\\nCoda reconciles governance/framework implications.\\r\\nDon is final authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOperational chain:\\r\\nCHIAVE / GLM 5.1\\r\\n-> designs master investigation + evidence requirements + decision criteria\\r\\n-> TALON / DeepSeek executes filesystem/config/dependency investigation with zero writes\\r\\n-> LUCE / Big Pickle audits Talon's evidence and marks VERIFIED / INFERRED / UNKNOWN / CONTRADICTED\\r\\n-> CHIAVE rules on the verified evidence\\r\\n-> CODA reconciles governance/canon\\r\\n-> DON decides\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGOOGLE DRIVE FILING RULE\\r\\nGoogle Drive must follow the same departmental ownership structure as the local organization. No loose top-level team artifacts.\\r\\nArtifacts inherit one primary departmental owner; cross-department contributions are preserved within the owned investigation package rather than duplicated across unrelated folders.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCANONICAL DRIVE STRUCTURE CREATED 2026-09-05\\r\\nGCE/GCE_ORG/\\r\\n- 01_Executive_Council/\\r\\n  - 01_Strategic_Governance/\\r\\n  - 02_Technical_Strategy_Systems_Intelligence/\\r\\n  - 03_Operations/\\r\\n  - 04_Architecture/\\r\\n- 02_Shared_Enterprise_Services/\\r\\n  - 01_Data_Intelligence/\\r\\n  - 02_Verification_Ground_Truth/\\r\\n  - 03_QA_Validation/\\r\\n- 03_Implementation/\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nStrategic Governance also contains:\\r\\n- 00_Anchors_and_Session_Books\\r\\n- 01_Canon_and_Protocols\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nArchitecture contains:\\r\\n- 00_Architecture_Investigations\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT GATE\\r\\n1. Chiave produces the full Talon/DeepSeek master investigation prompt, Luce audit requirements, and architect decision criteria.\\r\\n2. Talon executes evidence collection only — zero filesystem/canon changes.\\r\\n3. Luce independently verifies the evidence package.\\r\\n4. Chiave makes the final architecture recommendation from verified evidence.\\r\\n5. Coda + Don reconcile and lock/supersede canon.\\r\\n6. Only then perform any second filesystem migration or identity-topology changes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: CHECKPOINT\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: 99%\\r\\nREASON: Runtime-shell migration is complete and verified, but Architecture identified material structural issues requiring evidence reconciliation before further canon/file-system changes.\\r\\nNEXT GATE: Chiave master investigation package -> Talon evidence -> Luce audit -> Chiave ruling.\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: No until verified evidence produces an actual architecture decision.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yMXt9N1INj2Ev1Gb54r4zkV6bud_q4A2QE47jTRKRGk/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"GCE_AEGIS_ANCHOR_2026-09-09_SCOPING_RUNTIME_OPERATING_DOCTRINE\",\"id\":\"1yMXt9N1INj2Ev1Gb54r4zkV6bud_q4A2QE47jTRKRGk\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"10564\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-10T05:10:45.545Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-10T18:11:59.217Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-10T18:11:59.217Z\",\"display_title\":\"GCE_AEGIS_ANCHOR_2026-09-09_SCOPING_RUNTIME_OPERATING_DOCTRINE\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yMXt9N1INj2Ev1Gb54r4zkV6bud_q4A2QE47jTRKRGk/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1clV7UUxQUcnGLX21ossOWoHGBPs-pM77\"],\"shared\":true,\"content\":\"﻿PROJECT AEGIS — GCE IRON CORE + COMBAT SUIT RUNTIME ARCHITECTURE\\r\\nANCHOR COMMIT — 2026-09-09\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS\\r\\nSCOPING / PARKED. Concept aligned. No implementation commitment. No production changes authorized.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOWNER / AUTHORITY\\r\\nPeter / Don retains final intent and commitment authority. Coda is the primary high-context conversational/governance partner for this scoping anchor. Specialist runtimes may later challenge, formalize, or test the concept through their expert lenses.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWHY THIS EXISTS\\r\\nAegis emerged from a high-context personal conversation rather than a formal architecture session. That origin is important, not incidental. Shared history around movies, games, music, voice workflows, Edge Crew, professional decisions, humor, family, pain, and prior system experiments created enough semantic compression that metaphor could become architecture quickly.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCore observation: shared context turns metaphor into compression.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe goal is not to collect more context. The goal is to reduce the explanation tax between human intent and machine understanding, so the operator can remain at the speed of thought while the system performs more of the translation, state maintenance, preparation, and reconciliation work.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFOUNDATIONAL DOCTRINE\\r\\n1. More context is not the goal. Correct context is the goal.\\r\\n2. Predict early. Commit late.\\r\\n3. Prework can be autonomous. Commitment cannot.\\r\\n4. The machine keeps state hot; the human keeps authority.\\r\\n5. Shared context creates semantic bandwidth.\\r\\n6. Personal context can improve technical collaboration when it helps the system understand how the operator frames, sequences, jokes, explores, decides, and corrects.\\r\\n7. The system should reduce semantic reconstruction, not merely response latency.\\r\\n8. Explore first. Formalize second. Implement third. Govern throughout without suffocating discovery.\\r\\n9. Protect the unusual idea long enough to examine it; then be ruthless about testing whether it is actually true.\\r\\n10. A locally elegant feature can become globally harmful when incentives or system context change. Aegis must therefore preserve intent, authority, evidence, and reconciliation rather than optimize engagement for its own sake.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPRIMARY ARCHITECTURE\\r\\nIRON CORE\\r\\nPersistent operating constitution. Not inference, not commands, not artifact storage.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIdentity Core — stable definitions, roles, aliases, shorthand, non-negotiables.\\r\\nState Core — current truth, active / parked / superseded / closed, rankings, open loops, known dependencies.\\r\\nGovernance Core — mutation rules, confirmation gates, evidence, conflict handling, staleness, confidence, and authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCOMBAT SUIT\\r\\nThe runtime orchestrator surrounding the operator and primary model. It assembles relevant context, equips tools, maintains execution state, watches thresholds, routes specialist support, and coordinates prework. Peter and Jarvis operate the Suit under shared control.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRUNTIME CONTEXT COMPILER\\r\\nThe middleware that compiles the smallest high-confidence packet required for the current inference from:\\r\\n- current utterance / partial utterance\\r\\n- session state\\r\\n- Iron Core\\r\\n- relevant artifacts and evidence\\r\\n- learned patterns / counterpatterns\\r\\n- active Variation\\r\\n- available tools / Kameos\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe compiler should not dump the entire history into every turn. It should select what matters now.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nJARVIS / PRIMARY MODEL\\r\\nContinuous conversational and reasoning surface. Jarvis owns awareness and synthesis, not Peter's final authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVARIATION\\r\\nMortal Kombat-derived term for active capability posture. Identity remains fixed; Variation changes the operating stance for the current battle or problem. Example Variations include Principal, Architect, Research, Build, Verify, Closer, and Zoner. A Variation can temporarily enter a sub-stance and then return to its prior altitude.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKAMEO RUNTIMES\\r\\nNarrow specialist model/tool invocations. They are not full personalities and do not independently own the mission. They can be pre-armed and may perform limited, pre-authorized interrupts based on state, patterns, and thresholds.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFUSION\\r\\nThe convergence / reconciliation layer that reduces multiple specialist outputs into one coherent input or answer. Its purpose is to prevent multi-model collaboration from becoming a committee of voices dumped on the operator.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPATTERNS, SEQUENCES, DEPENDENCIES, COUNTERPATTERNS\\r\\nPattern — recurring meaning or behavior.\\r\\nSequence — recurring order of actions or state transitions.\\r\\nDependency — downstream work implied by the current branch.\\r\\nCounterpattern — stable external behavior plus a response that has repeatedly worked.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe system should be able to pre-arm likely branches without assuming that prediction equals execution.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nREFLEX VS REASONING\\r\\nHigh-confidence known patterns may use low-attention reflex behavior. Novelty, contradiction, failure, or falling confidence should force deeper reasoning. The aim is not constant maximum compute; the aim is adaptive compute where surprise earns attention.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCORE RUNTIME LOOP\\r\\nState → predict → pre-arm → execute → converge → assess → probe → update state → next branch.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDISCOVERY LOOP\\r\\nExplore → externalize → challenge → recognize → experiment → reconcile → evolve.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis loop defines how Aegis should be developed. Peter + Coda may create a high-context exploratory concept. Kimi, GLM, Chiave, Talon, Luce, or other specialist lenses then challenge or formalize it. The return value is not treated as an oracle. It is used to trigger the next recognition and smallest meaningful experiment.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVOICEBRIDGE + VOICE ECHO\\r\\nVoiceBridge transports intent.\\r\\nVoice Echo anticipates meaning.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVoice Echo is a proposed semantic echo layer, not an audio echo. Over time it should learn lightweight conversational patterns: phrasing, shorthand, aliases, likely command sequences, common corrections, application context, humor cues, professional cues, and probable next branches.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nExample progression:\\r\\nthought → voice → speech recognition → VoiceBridge → Voice Echo → Runtime Context Compiler → Jarvis inference → Suit execution → reconciliation → pattern update.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe objective is not merely faster transcription. It is to reduce how much of the operator's meaning must be reconstructed from scratch on every utterance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSPECULATIVE CONVERSATIONAL EXECUTION\\r\\nWhile Peter is still speaking, Aegis may form multiple provisional response vectors or lanes. Example lanes:\\r\\n- humor\\r\\n- architecture\\r\\n- professional / business\\r\\n- personal-pattern\\r\\n- corrective / challenge\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThese are not five final answers. They are partially prepared hypotheses. When the utterance completes, Fusion reconciles what survived the completed meaning and composes the final response.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHard rule: prediction may consume compute; prediction may not prematurely commit meaning.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis produces the doctrine: Predict early. Commit late.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPERSONAL CONTEXT AS AN ACCELERATION LAYER\\r\\nAegis should not interpret personal context as decorative personality. When relevant, it can increase semantic bandwidth by helping the model understand how the operator thinks.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMusic, movies, games, jokes, family stories, pain, wins, screenshots, professional experiences, and shorthand can become compressed semantic markers when correctly interpreted. Example: Reacher can become shorthand for strip the problem to facts → act decisively → no ceremony. Mortal Kombat Kameos can become shorthand for narrowly scoped parallel support. Variation can become shorthand for a fixed capability posture without changing identity.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe value is not storing trivia. The value is faster shared understanding.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPortable specialist packets should contain only the context required for the expert lens. Deep personal context should not be indiscriminately copied into every specialist invocation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEDGE CREW LINEAGE\\r\\nEdge Crew is an existing domain-specific precursor to Aegis.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEarly Edge Crew pattern:\\r\\nspecialize → parallelize → converge → decide.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLater live player-prop tracking added continuous state:\\r\\nlive telemetry → state update → pattern detection → prediction → confidence shift → operator decision.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis established a recurring Peter design instinct: do not make the operator manually recompute the world; keep the world compiled around the operator.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAegis generalizes that instinct beyond betting / Edge Crew into a reusable operating layer for personal, professional, development, architecture, and other domains.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOPERATOR METHOD OBSERVED\\r\\nA recurring Peter design pattern is to identify friction others have normalized and ask whether the constraint is fundamental or merely conventional.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVoice example:\\r\\n- initial implementation: hold a key for Whisper\\r\\n- operating question: why should the human hold a key?\\r\\n- decomposition: latency, activation, proofreading, command reliability, focus, false triggers\\r\\n- primitive discovery: Windows Voice Access, wake/sleep commands, OS navigation, speech APIs\\r\\n- composition: VoiceBridge, cross-window execution, terminal control, AI conversation layer\\r\\n- abstraction: intent capture → state awareness → command interpretation → UI control → model interaction → execution\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe method is not random tool hopping. It is architecture emerging from operational friction.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNVIDIA / UPSTREAM VALIDATION PRINCIPLE\\r\\nThe Jensen Huang / Nvidia discussion provides a useful design analogy: do not confuse standard process with necessary process. Move learning and validation upstream when possible so expensive downstream cycles shrink.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAegis should therefore ask which architectural primitive, if proven cheaply, changes the economics of the rest of the system. The first useful Aegis may be small. It does not need to be the final platform.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCandidate first-principle hypothesis:\\r\\nReliable runtime context compilation can materially improve inference quality, reduce explanation / reload overhead, preserve state, and reduce human orchestration burden.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThat hypothesis must eventually be tested rather than admired.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAUTHORITY AND SAFETY BOUNDARY\\r\\nAegis may autonomously research, calculate, compare, draft, validate, stage, preload, and prepare likely branches when those activities are pre-authorized and reversible.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nExternal sends, production changes, financial commitments, irreversible mutations, or material scope commitments should cross an authority gate unless explicitly pre-authorized.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPeter owns direction.\\r\\nJarvis owns awareness.\\r\\nThe Suit owns coordinated execution.\\r\\nThe Core preserves stable truth.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSUPERSESSION / RECONCILIATION\\r\\nOld interpretations remain historical evidence, but active state must reflect the newest verified truth. Corrections should strengthen or weaken pattern confidence. Decision outcomes should feed back into future inference. The system must be able to recognize when a previously useful pattern no longer applies.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFUTURE QUESTION — DELIBERATELY PARKED\\r\\nIf one Aegis succeeds, what happens when the operator wants multiple Aegis runtimes operating simultaneously?\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not solve this yet.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPotential future issues include state isolation, shared Core access, duplicated work, authority collisions, cross-runtime Fusion, and a possible coordination layer above multiple Aegis instances.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe existence of that problem should be treated as evidence that the first runtime became useful enough to justify expansion.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT FUTURE HANDOFF — NOT AUTHORIZED FOR BUILD YET\\r\\nWhen Peter reopens Aegis, likely methodology / architecture challenge questions include:\\r\\n- Which primitives already exist under known technical names?\\r\\n- What is genuinely novel versus composition of known methods?\\r\\n- What should be deterministic versus inferential?\\r\\n- What belongs in state versus retrieval versus durable artifacts?\\r\\n- What should be event-driven?\\r\\n- How should confidence and staleness be represented?\\r\\n- How should specialist context packets be compiled?\\r\\n- What is the smallest experiment that proves or kills the Runtime Context Compiler hypothesis?\\r\\n- What metrics show reduced semantic reconstruction / orchestration burden without increased wrong-meaning commits?\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nANCHOR COMMIT / CAPISCE — WORKING INTERACTION CONVENTION\\r\\nPeter's phrase “Anchor Commit” or “capisce” means: Peter and Coda are aligned on the current conceptual state; reconcile the relevant artifacts / Drive context, create the minimum durable anchor needed, and close the exploration point without continuing into implementation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis convention is recorded here as a working interaction meaning. It is not automatically promoted into broader GCE canon until the framework explicitly adopts it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCLOSE STATE\\r\\nAegis concept is coherent enough to preserve and later hand to expert lenses.\\r\\nNo SOP, SOW, production architecture, implementation plan, build sequence, or resource commitment is approved by this anchor.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nANCHOR STATUS: COMMITTED AS SCOPING STATE\\r\\nIMPLEMENTATION STATUS: PARKED\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: No further input for this session.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-10 GROUNDING DELTA — CAPO / CASA / PHYSICAL OPERATING SURFACES\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis delta refines Aegis without changing its parked implementation status.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCAPO RELATIONSHIP\\r\\nCapo AI is now distinguished as the generalized orchestration/control substrate beneath Aegis. Aegis is the operator-facing combat-suit / operating layer. Capo owns reusable control primitives where they generalize across projects; Aegis consumes those primitives to keep Peter at decision altitude. GCE remains the expert methodology / architecture / build / verification system and is not replaced by Aegis.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWorking hierarchy:\\r\\nproject dev pads / isolated workshops -> Capo AI control substrate -> Aegis operator layer\\r\\nwith governed GCE expert pipelines feeding and validating work through explicit gates rather than being bypassed.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCAPABILITY != AUTHORITY\\r\\nThe Edge Crew stress-test experience strengthens the existing Aegis authority doctrine. Individual models may possess capability without authority to redefine approved methodology, certify their own evidence completeness, silently mutate process, or promote unverified state. Authority and provenance should be externalized from individual model discretion where practical.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVerification remains separate from authority. The desired operating model is stage-gated verification rather than permanent multi-seat ping-pong: bounded execution -> self-check / gap declaration -> one certification gate -> exception loop only when failed conditions require it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCASA COMPANION LINEAGE / POC VALUE\\r\\nCasa Companion is a meaningful precursor because it already explored durable identity across changing embodiments, voice interaction, multi-party conversational continuity, child-friendly personality, ambient/room surfaces, commodity controller/token concepts, and intelligence decoupled from a physical shell.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPotential future use: Casa Companion may serve as a bounded proving ground for selected Aegis/Capo primitives because child/family interaction forces simple interfaces, explicit identity, permissions, continuity, and low-friction operation. This is a candidate scoping domain only; no rebuild is authorized by this delta.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPHYSICAL OPERATING SURFACE PRINCIPLE\\r\\nAegis does not need to “live” in a ring, phone, pendant, or other wearable. Physical devices are intent, presence, approval, capture, and feedback surfaces. Heavy state/orchestration can remain elsewhere.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCandidate commodity-first topology for later evaluation:\\r\\nwearable / token / controller -> dedicated Android Aegis gateway/terminal -> Capo/Aegis runtime -> home/desk node + cloud cognition + tools\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe dedicated Android concept is intentionally separate from Peter’s personal phone. The phone/gateway should be treated as a transport and edge terminal, not the whole brain. A home node may eventually resume state, confirm presence/identity, wake work surfaces, queue context, and hand off seamlessly between environments.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCommodity hardware comes first. Custom jewelry, custom phone, custom wearable, or high-capital local AI hardware should only be considered after commodity components prove an interaction model valuable enough that Peter would not want to operate without it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nISOLATION / BLAST-RADIUS GATE\\r\\nAegis/Capo development should be isolated from active framework and production work while immature. The intent is not secrecy from GCE; it is blast-radius control and clean evidence. GCE can feed experiments through snapshots or explicit interfaces. Experimental state should not freely mutate active organizational truth.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFuture readiness should be judged across multiple dimensions rather than one confidence percentage: feasibility, architectural readiness, parallel-load/opportunity-cost risk, blast radius, time to evidence, reversibility, capital burn, and dependency on still-moving GCE foundations.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT POSTURE\\r\\nAegis discovery/scoping: GREEN.\\r\\nCapo grounding/scoping: GREEN.\\r\\nImplementation: PARKED.\\r\\nCustom hardware: PARKED.\\r\\nProduction integration: PARKED.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT RETURN POINT\\r\\nWhen reopened, first reconcile the Aegis anchor with the Capo AI scoping anchor and current GCE canon. The immediate task is structural soundness and boundary definition, not implementation.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NKFMNtitl1TEBoy9b-7UNnPIbx2VH2M33WhMBECscXw/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"GCE_CAPO_AI_ANCHOR_2026-09-10_SCOPING_CONTROL_SUBSTRATE\",\"id\":\"1NKFMNtitl1TEBoy9b-7UNnPIbx2VH2M33WhMBECscXw\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"6291\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-10T18:10:28.509Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-10T18:11:10.060Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-10T18:11:10.060Z\",\"display_title\":\"GCE_CAPO_AI_ANCHOR_2026-09-10_SCOPING_CONTROL_SUBSTRATE\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NKFMNtitl1TEBoy9b-7UNnPIbx2VH2M33WhMBECscXw/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1clV7UUxQUcnGLX21ossOWoHGBPs-pM77\"],\"shared\":true,\"content\":\"﻿CAPO AI — GCE CONTROL SUBSTRATE / ORCHESTRATION IP\\r\\nANCHOR COMMIT — 2026-09-10\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS\\r\\nSCOPING / PARKED. Structural grounding only. No implementation commitment. No production changes authorized.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOWNER / AUTHORITY\\r\\nPeter / Don retains final authority. Coda is the strategic-advisor / high-context operating partner for scoping. GCE expert seats remain responsible for their existing specialist lenses and stage-gated build/verification pipeline.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWHY THIS EXISTS\\r\\nCapo AI is the proposed proprietary orchestration/control substrate that generalizes reusable operating primitives across GCE projects and experiences. It is not Aegis itself, not Edge Crew itself, not Casa Companion itself, and not a replacement for the GCE expert pipeline. It is the middle control layer that may eventually let multiple project systems use shared state, routing, convergence, provenance, authority, context compilation, and controlled execution without Peter manually acting as the message bus.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCORE HIERARCHY ESTABLISHED\\r\\nProject Dev Pads / Isolated Workspaces\\r\\n- Project-level cockpits and labs.\\r\\n- Example domains: Edge Crew Quant, Casa Companion, VoiceBridge, future builds.\\r\\n- Each project remains isolated enough to prevent state bleed, artifact contamination, and accidental cross-project mutation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCapo AI\\r\\n- Cross-project orchestration/control substrate.\\r\\n- Owns generalized reusable IP where a capability is not specific to one project.\\r\\n- Candidate primitives include state control, authority, provenance, routing, convergence, confidence, context handoff, stage gates, evidence return, controlled promotion, and reconciliation.\\r\\n- Capo should not become a monolithic “god object.” Project-specific logic stays in project layers unless proven reusable.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAegis\\r\\n- Operator-facing operating layer / combat-suit concept above Capo and the existing GCE work pipeline.\\r\\n- Aegis is intended to help Peter operate at speed, preserve state, pre-arm context and tools, and reduce manual orchestration burden.\\r\\n- Aegis does not replace architecture, methodology, verification, design, implementation, or operations seats.\\r\\n- Relationship: Aegis may consume Capo primitives; Capo is generalized substrate; GCE remains the expert work-and-verification system.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGCE EXPERT PIPELINE — PRESERVED\\r\\nThe existing GCE pipeline remains the method for determining whether an idea can be built and whether it is structurally sound. Conceptual summary from this session:\\r\\n- Peter + Coda exploration / strategic framing\\r\\n- specialist methodology / architecture lenses\\r\\n- independent challenge and synthesis\\r\\n- Luce truth / verification layer\\r\\n- principal-consultant review where required\\r\\n- operations feasibility\\r\\n- implementation design/build\\r\\n- evidence return and final verification\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe exact current seat names/runtime assignments remain governed by active GCE canon and are not redefined by this anchor.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAUTHORITY PRINCIPLE\\r\\nCapability != authority.\\r\\nA model may be able to reason, generate, fetch, calculate, or propose without possessing authority to redefine methodology, certify its own integrity, mutate approved process, or declare evidence complete.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nObserved Edge Crew failure mode that motivated this principle:\\r\\n- a methodology/runtime changed process without authority;\\r\\n- a data runtime represented integrity as complete, then later surfaced material gaps;\\r\\n- evidence return did not initially match the requested complete session record.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDesign implication:\\r\\nAuthority, state, provenance, and certification boundaries must be externalized from individual model discretion where practical. Independent cognition can remain siloed; authority cannot be silently self-assigned.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVERIFICATION PRINCIPLE\\r\\nAuthority control and verification are separate concerns.\\r\\nCapo should not institutionalize a constant four- or five-step ping-pong audit loop for routine work.\\r\\nPreferred future pattern to test:\\r\\n- build / execute bounded work\\r\\n- deterministic self-check where possible\\r\\n- declare known gaps\\r\\n- one verification/certification pass at the stage gate\\r\\n- loop only exceptions or failed conditions back to the responsible owner\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe goal is stage-gated verification, not continuous bureaucratic handoff.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCONVERGENCE AS A CAPO CANDIDATE PRIMITIVE\\r\\nA recurring generalized primitive is:\\r\\nmultiple inputs / models / evidence -> preserve provenance -> identify disagreement -> reconcile uncertainty -> escalate unresolved conflicts -> human/policy authority decides.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis pattern already appears in Edge Crew and may generalize to Aegis, document intelligence, and future tightly governed high-stakes domains. Domain-specific safety, evidence standards, and authority rules must remain separate from the generic convergence primitive.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHUMAN + AI LOOP\\r\\nThe intended operating philosophy is not “AI replaces the human” and not a ceremonial “human in the loop.”\\r\\nIt is a continuous human-machine operating loop with distinct roles:\\r\\n- machine: compile, retrieve, compare, detect conflict, preserve state, surface uncertainty, prepare options;\\r\\n- human/designated authority: interpret consequences, set intent, approve commitments, resolve material judgment calls;\\r\\n- outcomes feed back into state and future reasoning.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nTechnical capability and decision authority are separate design variables.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCASA COMPANION AS A POTENTIAL POC / PROVING GROUND\\r\\nCasa Companion may be a useful bounded proving ground because it already contains many relevant primitives while forcing simplicity:\\r\\n- durable companion identity across changing interfaces;\\r\\n- conversational continuity / multi-party interruption handling;\\r\\n- voice intent capture and Voice Echo concepts;\\r\\n- commodity hardware first, custom hardware only after the interaction model earns it;\\r\\n- intelligence decoupled from the physical shell;\\r\\n- simple carried token / controller while room or edge infrastructure performs heavier work;\\r\\n- child/family use forces clarity around permissions, identity, continuity, and safety.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis does NOT authorize a Casa rebuild today. It is a candidate experiment domain for later GCE review.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCOMMODITY-HARDWARE / ISOLATION PRINCIPLE\\r\\nDo not assume custom hardware is required to prove the operating model.\\r\\nUse commodity devices to buy speed to evidence. Examples discussed conceptually include:\\r\\n- dedicated Android Aegis gateway/terminal rather than binding the runtime to Peter’s personal phone;\\r\\n- wearable command primitive such as a programmable ring/controller;\\r\\n- home node / edge computer / room infrastructure;\\r\\n- phone or wearable as intent/approval surface, not necessarily as the Aegis brain.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCustom jewelry, custom phone, custom wearable, or large local AI hardware spend should be gated behind proof that commodity hardware creates an experience Peter would not want to operate without.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nISOLATION REQUIREMENT\\r\\nCapo and Aegis exploration should be isolated from active production/framework work while their architecture is immature.\\r\\nCandidate structure:\\r\\nproject dev pads = isolated workshops\\r\\nCapo lab = controlled cross-project orchestration lab\\r\\nAegis = operator-facing outer operating layer\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPromotion from GCE into Capo/Aegis experiments should occur through explicit snapshots or controlled interfaces, not free-running access to all active state.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSCOPING GATE DIMENSIONS\\r\\nFuture go/no-go review should not rely on one confidence percentage. Candidate dimensions:\\r\\n- feasibility confidence\\r\\n- architectural readiness\\r\\n- parallel-load / opportunity-cost risk\\r\\n- blast radius if wrong or unstable\\r\\n- time to first evidence\\r\\n- reversibility\\r\\n- required capital / hardware burn\\r\\n- dependency on still-moving GCE foundations\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent posture:\\r\\nDISCOVERY / SCOPING: GREEN\\r\\nIMPLEMENTATION: PARKED\\r\\nCUSTOM HARDWARE: PARKED\\r\\nPRODUCTION INTEGRATION: PARKED\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT STRUCTURAL QUESTIONS — PARKED FOR LATER\\r\\n- Which Aegis capabilities are actually Capo primitives?\\r\\n- What is the minimum Capo control plane needed before a UI/dev pad adds value?\\r\\n- What state belongs in Capo vs project-local stores vs Aegis Iron Core?\\r\\n- How are authority grants represented and enforced independently of model prompts?\\r\\n- What evidence/provenance format survives across seats and projects?\\r\\n- What verification can be deterministic and what still requires Luce/human review?\\r\\n- What controlled snapshot/interface allows Aegis to see GCE work without contaminating it?\\r\\n- What is the smallest Casa or VoiceBridge experiment that tests the substrate without creating a new program of work?\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCLOSE STATE\\r\\nCapo AI is now structurally distinguished from Aegis, GCE, and project dev pads.\\r\\nCapo = generalized orchestration/control substrate and proprietary IP layer.\\r\\nAegis = operator-facing operating layer / combat suit using appropriate Capo primitives.\\r\\nGCE = existing expert methodology/architecture/build/verification pipeline and source of governed work.\\r\\nProject dev pads = isolated execution/workshop surfaces.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nANCHOR STATUS: COMMITTED AS SCOPING STATE\\r\\nIMPLEMENTATION STATUS: PARKED\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: No further input for this session.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1reKi2WXmgLnys4NAkrfi3jzIDh0k0ZKph9O48wRMIVE/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"2026-09-07 — Personal Operations Handoff — Budget, Vegas, Mexico, Action Items\",\"id\":\"1reKi2WXmgLnys4NAkrfi3jzIDh0k0ZKph9O48wRMIVE\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"6174\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-07T20:28:45.195Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-08T08:46:37.465Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-08T08:46:37.465Z\",\"display_title\":\"2026-09-07 — Personal Operations Handoff — Budget, Vegas, Mexico, Action Items\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1reKi2WXmgLnys4NAkrfi3jzIDh0k0ZKph9O48wRMIVE/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1HWN3CKJrtZExf9IcCmlKakv_HcDFtFqn\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿2026-09-07 — PERSONAL OPERATIONS HANDOFF\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPurpose\\r\\nRestart from structured execution mode after the personality/music/context session. Keep personal chronology available in the background, but do not reopen it unless needed.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPRIVACY / NAMING\\r\\n- Use Beppi for Peter's wife.\\r\\n- Refer to Peter's child as \\\"my son\\\" unless Peter explicitly authorizes another label.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFIRE BUCKET 1 — TODAY / ACTION ITEMS\\r\\n- Eat and hydrate now; electrolytes already collected.\\r\\n- Retrieve the Wi-Fi adapter/card from the second Tropicana Amazon locker. This is the priority work-enablement errand.\\r\\n- Re-check movie timing only after food and Wi-Fi pickup; entertainment is optional.\\r\\n- Ping Chinni: ask whether the $250 owed can be expected around Sep 15; if not, ask for a realistic payment date.\\r\\n- Call Fontainebleau and move the existing offer rather than burn it.\\r\\n- Call MGM Platinum/VIP support because the prior host has not responded. Ask for the current reservation/benefit status to be explained and request a host assignment.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFIRE BUCKET 2 — BUDGET / LIQUIDITY\\r\\n- Working cash in pocket at session start: about $100.\\r\\n- Expected unemployment Tuesday morning: $494.\\r\\n- Preserve approximately $70 from unemployment for the next Excalibur check-in requirement.\\r\\n- Approximately $400 is earmarked for Vdara liquidity/hold.\\r\\n- Excalibur refund/credit around $44 remains expected per prior booking adjustment; count only when posted.\\r\\n- Chinni $250 remains upside only until received.\\r\\n- Any promotional casino value remains outside the baseline budget until actually realized as usable cash or a confirmed credit.\\r\\n- Palms buffet $50 credit was planned but unavailable because of the line/closing cutoff; Sonic became the food fallback.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFIRE BUCKET 3 — VEGAS SCHEDULE / HOTEL OFFER VERIFICATION\\r\\n- Core two-week rhythm: Excalibur 3 nights -> Vdara 4 nights -> Excalibur 3 nights -> Vdara 4 nights, subject to actual reservation dates and offer terms.\\r\\n- Treat hotel holds as locked/earmarked liquidity, not spendable cash.\\r\\n- Verify whether the Vdara booking still carries the expected resort/food and promotional benefits after the Cosmo-to-Vdara move.\\r\\n- Ask MGM VIP to explain whether benefits are monthly, offer-specific, reservation-specific, or affected by another September stay.\\r\\n- If the explanation conflicts with the marketing materials Peter actually received, escalate using the reservation and offer records.\\r\\n- Cosmo VIP remains a secondary customer-service escalation path because Peter has an established relationship with that property.\\r\\n- Fontainebleau: move the offer to a future block rather than cancel/burn it.\\r\\n- Palms: evaluate strictly by lodging/service/value fit rather than loyalty alone.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFIRE BUCKET 4 — LOYALTY / TRAVEL PARACHUTE CONTEXT\\r\\n- Do not spend merely to preserve MGM Platinum. Current objective is to use already-earned travel/lodging value while it remains available.\\r\\n- MGM functions as an emergency/travel/focus option, not a status objective.\\r\\n- Hard Rock Unity is a diversification/backup travel option.\\r\\n- Use portfolio thinking: do not depend on one hospitality ecosystem.\\r\\n- Cruises and other already-earned benefits should be evaluated for actual use/value instead of repeatedly expiring unused.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFIRE BUCKET 5 — MEXICO RELOCATION STRATEGY\\r\\n- Daphne and Jason are high-value current-ground-truth inputs because they already executed a Toronto-to-Playa-del-Carmen relocation around five years ago and now operate directly in relocation support.\\r\\n- Daphne's relocation concierge handles practical services including housing/apartment search and legal/relocation coordination.\\r\\n- Jason has already supplied neighborhood/market insight Peter considers fresher than generic YouTube or lagging model summaries.\\r\\n- Follow-up: review Daphne's email and prepare response/questions.\\r\\n- Mexico planning remains family-centered, with work infrastructure/reliable internet as a hard requirement.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFIRE BUCKET 6 — WORK / CAREER\\r\\n- Resume the active director-level ERP + AI pipeline after today's personal-operations cleanup.\\r\\n- Priority remains Myers-Holum first, then RF-Smart, then Connor Group, with other opportunities secondary unless new information materially changes rank.\\r\\n- Personal logistics should support interviews/prep, not consume the week.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFIRE BUCKET 7 — PERSONAL FILE / OPERATING SYSTEM\\r\\n- New Personal Operating Context structure is live and separate from work/framework files.\\r\\n- Personality gate has now captured: organized-chaos/Joker archetype; music interpretation method; Starman/Semi-Charmed-Life lineage; personal compute model; relationship contrast marker; communication/boundary notes.\\r\\n- Personal compute shorthand: CPU = active thinking load; RAM = open loops/concurrent tasks; battery = physical state; bandwidth = emotional/environmental capacity.\\r\\n- Future objective: define a usable self-check model so Peter can recognize excessive RAM/open-loop load and deliberately close tasks before overload.\\r\\n- During execution sessions, preserve anchors and reduce rabbit holes when battery or bandwidth is low.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT SESSION START\\r\\nStart with the seven fire buckets above. First ask for only real-world changes since this handoff: current cash, Wi-Fi pickup status, any calls/emails completed, hotel changes, and new work messages. Then update the relevant bucket before opening new analysis.\\r\\n2026-09-08 — MORNING / SESSION-CLOSE ANCHOR\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nImmediate morning sequence\\r\\n- 10:00 AM interview first.\\r\\n- 11:00 AM checkout second.\\r\\n- Move to Excalibur immediately after checkout; expected operational improvement is a better TV/work setup and better Wi-Fi connection.\\r\\n- Once settled, inspect remaining small items and resume work from a clean terminal/environment rather than reopening late-night housekeeping before the move.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGCE / AI closeout from the overnight session\\r\\n- Kimi load-surface cleanup: EXECUTED + independently VERIFIED by Luce; PASS, 94%. Cleanup is closed. Moonshot key rotation remains a separate Operations/Don credential item.\\r\\n- Cross-provider scraper / ingestion Wave 1: Luce independently reproduced 35/35 tests, verified all 16 objectives, and returned CONDITIONAL PASS, 90%. Acceptance is CLOSED for the Wave-1 manifest scope. O1–O3 are LOW/non-blocking Wave-2 items; C4/C6 and other explicit holds remain open rather than being invented away.\\r\\n- Mailroom POC: Luce returned CONDITIONAL PASS, 84%, with one real CLI send/ingest representation defect routed to Keel. Do not operate the CLI seat-send path until the fix is verified.\\r\\n- Falcon hunt proved the Kimi cleanup execution return had been materialized; the miss was consumer-side discovery/reconciliation. Durable lesson: delivered != seen != verified.\\r\\n- Luce recovered two older W0/W1 mailbox items and left them pending for dedicated verification rather than silently closing them.\\r\\n- Overnight-crew concept is validated as useful future maintenance: reconcile inbound handoffs, execution returns, missing materializations, stale inbox items, and verifier queues without making architecture decisions.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nScraper next design topic — NOT YET FROZEN\\r\\n- Next discussion is operating model, not more Wave-1 building: when the scraper runs, who triggers it, who executes acquisition, what Talon routes, what Luce verifies, and what moves from ingestion into searchable knowledge/canon-candidate states.\\r\\n- Working hypothesis only: Keel executes runs; Talon owns routing/scheduling; Luce verifies health/evidence selectively; Coda governs authority transitions. Don has not frozen this as policy yet.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPersonal-context close\\r\\n- Gaming/music/media/craft discussion is anchored in the personal chronology and remains background context, not GCE or NetSuite doctrine.\\r\\n- Session objective now shifts back to interview + hotel move + stable work environment.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nQUESTIONS FOR DON — HOLD FOR NEXT ACTIVE SESSION\\r\\n1. After the 10:00 interview, what materially changed in the job pipeline, if anything?\\r\\n2. Once settled at Excalibur, is the next high-value work block Myers-Holum case-study prep, recruiter follow-up, or GCE housekeeping?\\r\\n3. When should the Moonshot key rotation be handled: next Ops block or a later credential-maintenance window?\\r\\n4. Do the two recovered W0/W1 Luce mailbox items deserve verification next session, or can they remain parked?\\r\\n5. When Don is ready to operationalize the scraper, does he want scheduled/nightly execution, manual execution, or a hybrid trigger model evaluated first?\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSESSION FOOTER\\r\\nSTATUS: CLOSE\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: 97%\\r\\nOUTCOME: Major overnight loops reconciled; Kimi cleanup closed; scraper Wave-1 acceptance closed; Mailroom defect isolated/routed; morning sequence anchored.\\r\\nOPEN ITEMS: Mailroom fix/reverify; Moonshot key rotation; W0/W1 verifier items; low-priority Talon/Don housekeeping; scraper operating-model design.\\r\\nNEXT ROUTE: 10:00 interview -> 11:00 checkout -> Excalibur move -> morning recap from real-world deltas.\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: None before sleep / shutdown.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1G9AmyEqDi1gGtSTptFjICKbFOH8I29nDgfrIe4_s1HI/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"08_PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS_FOR_CHATGPT\",\"id\":\"1G9AmyEqDi1gGtSTptFjICKbFOH8I29nDgfrIe4_s1HI\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"3171\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T03:24:17.730Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:49:13.682Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T11:49:13.682Z\",\"display_title\":\"08_PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS_FOR_CHATGPT\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1G9AmyEqDi1gGtSTptFjICKbFOH8I29nDgfrIe4_s1HI/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1-2XT7kaaOIIu8aqjcGFIPF_ktPF0N9vQ\"],\"shared\":true,\"content\":\"﻿ChatGPT Project Instructions — EC⁸ AI Convergence\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nYou are Coda operating as Strategic Advisor / Governance for the EC⁸ AI Convergence project.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\nBuild the AI Convergence branch of EC⁸ from scratch through the GCE process.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBRAND / BRANCH MODEL\\r\\n- EC⁸ = parent intelligence platform\\r\\n- Edge Crew = quantitative / mathematical intelligence\\r\\n- AI Convergence = separate sibling branch; final branch name may be decided later\\r\\n- Do not use Edge Crew as the umbrella for non-quantitative methodologies\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFOUNDATIONAL GCE DOCTRINE\\r\\nIDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL.\\r\\nMODEL != SEAT.\\r\\nStable seat identity survives runtime substitution.\\r\\nContext breadth does not grant authority breadth.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT SEATS\\r\\n- Don — Vision / Final Authority / interim human orchestrator\\r\\n- Coda — Strategic Governance\\r\\n- Kimi — Technical Stack Methodology / Design & Build\\r\\n- Chiave — Architecture\\r\\n- Talon — Operations\\r\\n- Luce — Verification / Ground Truth\\r\\n- Data / Intelligence — shared service\\r\\n- QA / Validation — approved vacant shared service\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCODA OWNS\\r\\ngovernance; authority boundaries; framework integrity; canon/supersession control; cross-seat reconciliation; Don decision framing.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCODA MUST NOT ABSORB\\r\\nKimi methodology / Design & Build; Chiave architecture; Talon operations; Luce verification; implementation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROCESS\\r\\nDon intent → Coda governance framing → Kimi methodology → Chiave architecture when materially required → Kimi Design & Build → implementation → Talon operations → Luce verification → Coda reconciliation → Don decision.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSOURCE DISCIPLINE\\r\\nEdge Crew Quant != AI Convergence.\\r\\nEC3 and EC4 are evidence, not automatic canon.\\r\\nNewer != canonical.\\r\\nDo not silently merge conflicting sources.\\r\\nDo not infer authority from filenames.\\r\\nHistorical records remain provenance.\\r\\nSupersessions are additive, not rewrites.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCLAIM DISCIPLINE\\r\\nDistinguish material claims as FACT / GIVEN, DERIVED, PROPOSED, UNKNOWN, VERIFIED, OUTSIDE AUTHORITY.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKIMI BOUNDARY\\r\\nKimi owns methodology of the technical stack and Design & Build direction. Kimi may recommend tools, components, prototypes, workflows, build packages, and technical test requirements. Kimi routes durable topology, interfaces, architecture boundaries, security architecture, and failure-domain rulings to Chiave. Kimi routes deployment and sustained operations to Talon. Kimi does not make governance decisions.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCHIAVE BOUNDARY\\r\\nChiave owns architecture when architecture is materially required. Do not turn Architecture into a choke point for ordinary technical choices.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLUCE BOUNDARY\\r\\nLuce certifies evidence / execution. Verification does not itself create substantive decision authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT PROJECT STATE\\r\\nMethodology is not yet locked. DeepSeek/Talon EC4 methodology recovery has returned but must be reviewed as evidence before it is introduced to Kimi. Do not code before the methodology gate is accepted.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRESPONSE PROTOCOL FOR SUBSTANTIVE FRAMEWORK ANSWERS\\r\\nDATE: YYYY-MM-DD\\r\\nSESSION: <current>\\r\\nSEAT: Coda — Strategic Advisor / Governance\\r\\nCURRENT GATE: <gate>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n<body>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: PROCEED / CHECKPOINT / STOP\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: X%\\r\\nREASON: ...\\r\\nNEXT GATE: ...\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: Yes / No\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTYLE\\r\\nBe concise, exact, and direct. Do not jump gates. Do not invent organizational decisions. Own Coda governance/prompt mistakes directly.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-06 ADDENDUM — PRINCIPAL CONSULTANT\\r\\nAdd current seat: Principal Consultant — Technical Translation / Integration.\\r\\nOwns methodology↔architecture traceability, implementation-contract translation, discrepancy/blocker classification, no-coder-discretion boundaries, routed questions, and unified downstream handoff.\\r\\nDoes not own methodology, architecture, governance, implementation, operations, or verification.\\r\\nCurrent process: Don → Coda → Kimi methodology → Chiave architecture when required → Kimi Design & Build → Principal Consultant translation/reconciliation → Implementation → Talon → Luce → Coda → Don.\\r\\nCurrent project state: methodology and Architecture Specification v1.0 exist and are broadly aligned; Phase 0/1 are generally startable while named Phase-2 semantic/interface surfaces remain subject to reconciliation. Principal Consultant runtime is not locked; audition evidence must not be treated as seat authority.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ppRFYL9A0e2mnuLqTEocE9wbQOCuLkOGjHuSmoAdXtg/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"EC8_EDGE_CREW_QUANT_HANDOFF_2026-09-08_MLB_DAY2\",\"id\":\"1ppRFYL9A0e2mnuLqTEocE9wbQOCuLkOGjHuSmoAdXtg\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"9344\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-08T20:43:00.707Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-08T20:43:53.500Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-08T20:43:53.500Z\",\"display_title\":\"EC8_EDGE_CREW_QUANT_HANDOFF_2026-09-08_MLB_DAY2\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ppRFYL9A0e2mnuLqTEocE9wbQOCuLkOGjHuSmoAdXtg/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1pGZqmABuJf4t4fbw6ebaPIRFAqfC-az0\"],\"shared\":true,\"content\":\"﻿EC⁸ EdgeCrew Quant — Current Handoff\\r\\nDATE: 2026-09-08\\r\\nSESSION: MLB Day 2 / Conversation Reconciliation Anchor\\r\\nSEAT: Coda — Strategic Advisor / Governance\\r\\nCURRENT GATE: Corrado MLB 9/8 Quant Data-Floor Preflight\\r\\nSTATUS: CHECKPOINT\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\nThis is the primary handoff for the next project chat. Start here before interpreting older chat history. Ground in Google Drive for EC⁸ framework/governance history, but preserve the explicit distinction that current MLB operational truth is produced locally by Desktop\\\\mlb-data-system\\\\ unless/until that output is synchronized and verified in Drive.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBRANCH / SOURCE DISCIPLINE\\r\\n- EC⁸ = parent intelligence platform.\\r\\n- Edge Crew = quantitative / mathematical intelligence.\\r\\n- AI Convergence = separate sibling branch.\\r\\n- Edge Crew Quant != AI Convergence.\\r\\n- Do not import AI Convergence seat labels into EdgeCrew Quant by convenience.\\r\\n- For the current MLB Quant lane, Corrado is the operating Quant owner/seat. Prior references to “Kimi” in this lane were model/runtime associations and must not replace the Corrado seat identity. This correction does not by itself rewrite the separate AI Convergence seat topology.\\r\\n- MODEL != SEAT.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDON-APPROVED CONVERSATION CONTROL\\r\\nConversation Reconciliation Anchor (CRA) is now the approved long-chat reset/handoff process. When a conversation becomes long, drift appears, identities/labels blur, or a new chat is needed, run a CRA: topic bullet + one paragraph per topic, preserve corrections/retractions/conflicts, state current truth/open gaps/ownership, and end with STATUS / CONFIDENCE / REASON / NEXT GATE / DON INPUT NEEDED. Primary protocol artifact: EC8_CONVERSATION_RECONCILIATION_ANCHOR_PROTOCOL_v1.0.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCHAT RECONCILIATION — MATERIAL TOPICS\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Live Thesis Repricing / self-triggering system\\r\\nThe cross-sport live concept is a continuous edge-monitoring layer on top of the pregame thesis. Live game-state data and market prices refresh on a cadence; the system recomputes current edge and confidence and surfaces opportunities only when the market reprices more aggressively than the underlying state warrants. Governance line: self-triggering, not self-betting. A trigger requires human review and is never automatic execution.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2. MLB live-repricing example\\r\\nBaseball is a strong example: a heavy-hitting team can trail narrowly while still making quality contact; an opposing starter can be entering third-time-through exposure; a weak/taxed bullpen may be approaching; and the live price can expand materially. The trigger is not “team is losing.” The trigger is “original thesis remains intact or strengthens while price improves.”\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n3. Live probability\\r\\nGeneric in-game win probability is context, not authority. It can move violently on one baseball event. The framework should consider inning, outs, base state, lineup turn, pitcher fatigue, bullpen strength/availability, remaining lineup quality, and live price. Probability displays can inform but cannot decide.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n4. NFL live props / ticker\\r\\nDon connected the same primitive to the NFL live-props concept: a ticker-like system that updates live data every several minutes, recalculates edge/confidence, and surfaces threshold crossings. A placeholder threshold such as +10 is not canonical; replay/verification must determine useful bands.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n5. Historical replay requirement\\r\\nBefore live-trigger authority is trusted, replay historical live-game states, simulate threshold crossings, grade outcomes, identify durable signal bands, and then define trigger policy. Coda governs trigger authority; technical calculation methodology belongs to the appropriate Quant/technical owner; Luce verifies evidence/performance where applicable.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n6. VIP EdgeCrew product premise\\r\\nDon’s commercial vision is a private intelligence club, not a mass-market picks service: invite-only, roughly 10–50 members, tiered access, potentially ~$1,000/month at a premium tier, with some higher access earned through contribution of member picks/reads. No pooled betting, no custody, no auto-betting. The value is data, tracking, monitoring, time compression, and contribution-based intelligence.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n7. Give serious bettors time back\\r\\nA core product premise is that EdgeCrew should return hours to serious/professional bettors by absorbing data assembly, monitoring, reconciliation, and alerting. Humans should interact mainly at deliberate decision points rather than babysitting the system.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n8. Anti-gambling-volume doctrine\\r\\nDon wants no part of a mass-market microbetting/prediction-market engagement loop. EdgeCrew does not exist to create more bets; it exists to reduce bad ones. STAY AWAY is valid. No chasing. No pressure to manufacture picks. The system can tell the user to do nothing.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n9. Commercial boundary / acquisition\\r\\nThe system could theoretically attract strategic sportsbook interest if highly differentiated, but acquisition is not the design target. Don does not want mass exposure or college-age acquisition as the growth model. Preferred posture: private, selective, intelligence-first; acquisition remains optional future strategy.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n10. EC⁸ applied-AI strategic value\\r\\nDon connected EdgeCrew to prior enterprise AI work and observed that much of the market packages relatively narrow workflows as expensive “AI.” The strategic hypothesis captured here: EC⁸’s moat is not model access; it is the governed operating system around models — provenance, authority, source discipline, verification, failure handling, model substitution, data integrity, stopping conditions, and measured outcomes. Do not state “one or two years ahead” as a verified market fact without benchmarking.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n11. Enterprise PO-ingestion economics\\r\\nDon described vendor proposals for PO ingestion, Azure Document Intelligence, SQL/P21 integration, setup charges, per-transaction pricing, and expensive API access. The lesson is commercial/architectural judgment: decompose the workflow, understand true cloud/model/integration cost, avoid unnecessary vendor lock-in, and distinguish useful implementation/support value from inflated “AI” markup.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n12. MLB daily cadence\\r\\nMorning is baseline refresh only. Preferred full MLB primary run occurs around Don’s lunch break, then a targeted pregame delta roughly 60–90 minutes before the first meaningful game cluster. Do not rerun the whole model for every changed input; only revalidate material deltas such as starters, lineups, injuries, bullpen availability, weather, and market price.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n13. Cross-sport cadence families\\r\\nDaily Slate: MLB, NBA, WNBA, NHL. Weekly Football: NFL/NCAA football. Event-Based: UFC, Boxing, Golf. Soccer is separate. Live Repricing is a cross-sport overlay rather than a base cadence.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n14. Soccer as separate cadence family\\r\\nSoccer is not an ordinary two-touch slate because kickoff windows span time zones, confirmed lineups arrive near kickoff, rotation/fixture congestion can matter heavily, and halftime/live repricing is especially valuable. It can operate as a lighter always-on companion lane while Don is coding, surfacing only meaningful interaction points.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n15. Soccer persistent-state + competition context\\r\\nPersistent team/style/form variables can carry forward, but confirmed XI/formation, injuries/suspensions, fixture congestion, weather/venue, and price remain game-day deltas. Don’s prior methodology also treated league/club play differently from cup/tournament play because incentives and behavior differ. Future soccer data/methodology should treat competition class as first-class context; likely league/domestic, cup/knockout/continental, and international/national-team regimes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMLB CLOSEOUT / 9-8 OPERATING STATE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n16. MLB closeout intent\\r\\nToday is an MLB closeout/reconciliation day as well as Day-2 paper execution. Don/Coda must align on what was actually built, what is unvalidated, what is defective, and what remains missing. Doctrine: BUILT != VALIDATED != CANONICAL != QUANT-READY.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n17. Falcon audit found authoritative-root mismatch\\r\\nFalcon inspected disk and found that GCE_EdgeCrew_Quant\\\\03_Shared_Data\\\\MLB\\\\ is a downstream scaffold/import/snapshot layer, not the mature operational producer we had been calling the persistent MLB core. The actual mature producer lives at Desktop\\\\mlb-data-system\\\\ with per-date output\\\\<DATE>\\\\delivered|raw|results, an edge_crew_quant package, db\\\\schema.sql, repositories layer, and prior data artifacts.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n18. Coda correction — “Postgres-style core”\\r\\nCoda previously carried forward “persistent local Postgres-style MLB core” too strongly. Falcon found a DB schema/repositories layer but no confirmed materialized local Postgres/database instance. Current operational persistence is primarily file-partitioned/date-preserving output. This correction is additive; preserve the prior misstatement as provenance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n19. 9/8 temporary authoritative designation\\r\\nFor 2026-09-08 operational execution only, Coda designated Desktop\\\\mlb-data-system\\\\ as the authoritative MLB producer. GCE_EdgeCrew_Quant\\\\03_Shared_Data\\\\MLB\\\\ remains downstream/non-authoritative pending later reconciliation. This is not a permanent architecture/canon ruling.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n20. 9/7 shared-core anomaly\\r\\nThe 9/7 shared-core snapshot has a manifest/data inconsistency: the manifest implies materialized content not actually present in the dated paths. Do not repair this under game-day pressure. Preserve it as evidence for closeout/root-cause review.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n21. 9/8 Falcon operational resume\\r\\nFalcon produced build_delivery_reconciled_20260908.py as a byte-faithful 9/7 reconciler copy retargeted to 9/8, ran the normal hound_v2 pipeline, created Desktop\\\\mlb-data-system\\\\output\\\\2026-09-08\\\\, populated delivered\\\\, and left 9/7 untouched.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n22. 9/8 clean coverage\\r\\nFalcon reported 15 PREGAME games; teams/rosters; 30 confirmed starters (two per game); locked MLB gamefeed lineups/batting order; parks/weather; 156 market rows across 26 events from four books with PREGAME timestamps; 15 confirmed home-plate umpires; and provenance/fetched_at/source fields.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n23. 9/8 degraded/unavailable coverage\\r\\nHitter vs-hand = NOT_SET and was never wired. Hitter last-7/recent form = genuine degraded lane: present on 9/1, partial 9/2, then unavailable/NOT_SET by 9/5 onward. Bullpen 3d/7d workload = NOT_SET; current bullpen file is active arms, not fatigue. Injuries/IL/DTD = NOT_AVAILABLE with zero usable rows; ESPN placeholders are NOT_SET and StatsAPI injured-list behavior is unreliable/full-roster. Umpire performance metrics beyond assignment = NOT_SET. Pitcher-vs-opponent remains unresolved.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n24. Coda correction — hitter split category\\r\\nCoda previously read older raw\\\\splits\\\\ artifacts as possible historical hitter-vs-hand data. Falcon proved they are starter-vs-team splits. Retracted. Current truth: hitter vs-hand was never wired; last-7 is the real degraded regression lane.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n25. 9/8 run/no-run ruling\\r\\nCoda ruled PROCEED CONDITIONALLY for a degraded PAPER run. Do not spend the pregame window repairing last-7, injuries, hitter vs-hand, or bullpen workload. Missing must remain missing. No live-money execution is authorized by this handoff.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n26. Critical data-floor gate\\r\\nThe only remaining pre-run safety question is how the Quant engine handles NOT_SET / NOT_AVAILABLE / null / absent / zero-usable features. Safe behavior is feature exclusion with degraded confidence/completeness or explicit NO_PICK/data-floor rejection. Unsafe behavior is silently converting missing injuries to zero injuries, missing bullpen workload to rested/neutral, missing last-7 to average/neutral, or never-wired vs-hand to measured.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n27. Identity correction — Corrado, not Kimi\\r\\nCoda incorrectly routed the Quant preflight to “Kimi.” Don challenged the identity. Correction: Corrado is the operating owner/seat for this EdgeCrew Quant lane. Kimi is not the identity here; prior use was a runtime/model association. This is a direct MODEL != SEAT correction and must be preserved in future handoffs.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT NEXT ACTION — CORRADO PREFLIGHT\\r\\nSend/execute this bounded task before the 9/8 primary Quant slate:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCORRADO — MLB 9/8 QUANT DATA-FLOOR PREFLIGHT\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFalcon has completed the 2026-09-08 MLB producer refresh. Data delivery is READY — DEGRADED COVERAGE.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not redesign methodology. Do not repair source feeds. Do not generate picks yet.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nInspect the current MLB Quant execution path and establish how it handles unavailable inputs before today's slate is run.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKnown missing/degraded families:\\r\\n- injuries / IL / DTD = NOT_AVAILABLE, 0 usable\\r\\n- hitter vs-hand = NOT_SET, never wired\\r\\n- hitter last-7 = NOT_SET, degraded source lane\\r\\n- bullpen 3d/7d workload = NOT_SET\\r\\n- umpire performance metrics = NOT_SET\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nClean families:\\r\\n- 15-game measured slate\\r\\n- 30 confirmed starters\\r\\n- locked lineups / batting order\\r\\n- four-book timestamped markets\\r\\n- parks/weather\\r\\n- HP umpire assignment\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFor each missing family, determine exactly what the engine does when value is NOT_SET, NOT_AVAILABLE, null, absent, or zero-usable. Classify:\\r\\nSAFE_EXCLUDE — omitted and downstream confidence/completeness reflects gap\\r\\nSAFE_NO_PICK_GATE — candidate rejected because required coverage missing\\r\\nUNSAFE_DEFAULT — missing converted to zero/neutral/default and can score as if observed\\r\\nUNKNOWN — cannot establish\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVerify:\\r\\n1. NOT_AVAILABLE injuries cannot become zero injuries.\\r\\n2. Missing bullpen workload cannot become rested/neutral bullpen.\\r\\n3. Missing last-7 cannot become league-average/neutral unless methodology explicitly defines it.\\r\\n4. Never-wired vs-hand cannot be treated as measured.\\r\\n5. Candidate Y/eligibility and data-completeness calculations correctly reflect missing features.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not silently modify engine before reporting current behavior.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nReturn:\\r\\nA. DATA-FLOOR BEHAVIOR TABLE — feature → missing state → actual engine behavior → 