id": "51fafd6d-6902-444e-aa0b-aaaed40d77a1"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790381907.054459, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yes. This should be **derived from V3, not a second competing framework**.\n\nI’d call it:\n\n# GCE MID-FLIGHT FRAME — V1\n\nIts job is simply:\n\n> **Re-ground the active session without creating a new daily anchor, new thread, or new lifecycle.**\n\nIt inherits everything durable from the current V3 anchor unless explicitly changed.\n\n## Mid-Flight Header\n\n```text\n==================================================\nGCE MID-FLIGHT HEADER — V1\n==================================================\n\nTIMESTAMP:            <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM TZ>\n\nPARENT ANCHOR:        <current V3 daily anchor>\nAUTHORITY:            Don\nPRIMARY SEAT:         <seat>\nOCCUPANT / MODEL:     <model/runtime>\n\nMODE:                 <current operating mode>\nCURRENT THREAD:       <stable thread name>\nPROMOTED / CURRENT:   <what we are working on right now>\n\nPRIORITY:             <HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW>\nSTATUS:               <ACTIVE | CHECKPOINT | BLOCKED | PARKED>\nCONFIDENCE:           <0–100%>\n\nCURRENT CONTEXT:\n<maximum 1–2 lines: exactly where we are right now>\n\nCURRENT ANCHOR:\n<authoritative state/artifact currently governing the work>\n```\n\nThat is it. No `STARTED`, `DAYS RUNNING`, `ACTIVE DAYS`, maturity detail, giant roster, Cable Car state, etc.\n\nThose already exist above us in the daily anchor.\n\n---\n\n## Header Appendix — Mid-Flight Intent Delta\n\nThis is the lightweight version of the Don Intent Snapshot.\n\n```text\n--------------------------------------------------\nMID-FLIGHT APPENDIX — INTENT DELTA\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nDON INTENT:\n<what Don wants right now>\n\nIMMEDIATE OBJECTIVE:\n<what this specific run should accomplish>\n\nCONTEXT CHANGE:\n<NONE or what changed since the parent anchor>\n```\n\nThat last field matters.\n\nMost of the time:\n\n```text\nCONTEXT CHANGE: NONE\n```\n\nBut if you say:\n\n> \"Taxonomy is parked. We're doing Cable Car now.\"\n\nthen it records exactly that change.\n\n---\n\n# Mid-Flight Footer\n\nThis closes **only the mid-flight run**, not the daily session.\n\n```text\n==================================================\nGCE MID-FLIGHT FOOTER — V1\n==================================================\n\nSTATUS:               <PROCEED | CHECKPOINT | BLOCKED | PARKED>\n\nRESULT:\n<1–2 lines: what materially happened in this run>\n\nCONFIDENCE:           <0–100%>\n\nCHANGED SINCE ENTRY:\n- <material change>\n- <material change>\n- NONE\n\nBLOCKER:\n<NONE or one actual blocker>\n\nNEXT MOVE:\n<one immediate action>\n\nRETURN STATE:\n<CONTINUE CURRENT | PROMOTE <item> | PARK CURRENT | DROP ANCHOR>\n```\n\n### And yes — **confidence is mandatory.**\n\nI agree with you on that. It should never disappear.\n\nFor me, confidence is one of the most useful at-a-glance controls in the whole framework.\n\n---\n\n# Footer Appendix — Continuity Delta\n\nThis is the tiny machine/context appendix.\n\n```text\n--------------------------------------------------\nMID-FLIGHT APPENDIX — CONTINUITY DELTA\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nPARENT ANCHOR:        <same daily anchor>\nCURRENT SEAT:         <seat>\nNEXT ROUTE:           <seat / Don / NONE>\n\nPROMOTED / CURRENT:\n<current item>\n\nPARKED CHANGES:\n<NONE or changed parked item>\n\nANCHOR IMPACT:\n<NONE | UPDATE REQUIRED>\n\nHANDOFF CREATED:\n<NONE | handoff ID>\n```\n\nNotice `ANCHOR IMPACT`.\n\nThat's important.\n\nA mid-flight run can finish and say:\n\n```text\nANCHOR IMPACT: NONE\n```\n\nMeaning we learned/worked on something, but nothing durable enough happened to alter our daily anchor.\n\nOr:\n\n```text\nANCHOR IMPACT: UPDATE REQUIRED\n```\n\nThat tells us:\n\n> \"Okay, this became meaningful. Drop an anchor.\"\n\n---\n\n# Full lightweight example\n\nUsing what we're doing right now:\n\n```text\n==================================================\nGCE MID-FLIGHT HEADER — V1\n==================================================\n\nTIMESTAMP:            2026-09-25 <time> PT\n\nPARENT ANCHOR:        GCE_FRAMEWORK_RECON_ANCHOR_2026-09-25_V3_TAXONOMY_CONTINUATION\nAUTHORITY:            Don\nPRIMARY SEAT:         Coda\nOCCUPANT / MODEL:     GPT-5.6 Sol\n\nMODE:                 DESIGN\nCURRENT THREAD:       GCE Session Control Framework\nPROMOTED / CURRENT:   Mid-Flight Frame Design\n\nPRIORITY:             MEDIUM\nSTATUS:               ACTIVE\nCONFIDENCE:           98%\n\nCURRENT CONTEXT:\nDesigning the lightweight in-session grounding frame derived from the\ncanonical V3 daily Session Frame.\n\nCURRENT ANCHOR:\nGCE_SESSION_FRAME_V3_CURRENT_2026-09-25\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nMID-FLIGHT APPENDIX — INTENT DELTA\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nDON INTENT:\nCreate the smallest useful in-session header/footer for re-grounding\nwithout triggering a full daily anchor.\n\nIMMEDIATE OBJECTIVE:\nDefine the Mid-Flight Header, Footer, and lightweight appendices.\n\nCONTEXT CHANGE:\nSession Frame V3 remains canonical; this adds a subordinate runtime control.\n```\n\nAnd when we finish:\n\n```text\n==================================================\nGCE MID-FLIGHT FOOTER — V1\n==================================================\n\nSTATUS:               PROCEED\n\nRESULT:\nMid-Flight Frame V1 defined as a lightweight subordinate control\nunder the daily V3 Session Frame.\n\nCONFIDENCE:           98%\n\nCHANGED SINCE ENTRY:\n- Defined Mid-Flight Header.\n- Defined Mid-Flight Footer.\n- Defined intent and continuity delta appendices.\n\nBLOCKER:\nNONE\n\nNEXT MOVE:\nDon reviews and adjusts before canonicalization.\n\nRETURN STATE:\nCONTINUE CURRENT\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nMID-FLIGHT APPENDIX — CONTINUITY DELTA\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nPARENT ANCHOR:\nGCE_FRAMEWORK_RECON_ANCHOR_2026-09-25_V3_TAXONOMY_CONTINUATION\n\nCURRENT SEAT:         Coda\nNEXT ROUTE:           Don\n\nPROMOTED / CURRENT:\nMid-Flight Frame Design\n\nPARKED CHANGES:\nNONE\n\nANCHOR IMPACT:\nUPDATE REQUIRED\n\nHANDOFF CREATED:\nNONE\n```\n\n## The hierarchy becomes very clean\n\n```text\nDAILY ANCHOR / SESSION FRAME V3\n        │\n        ├── MID-FLIGHT\n        │      ├── header\n        │      └── footer\n        │\n        ├── MID-FLIGHT\n        │      ├── header\n        │      └── footer\n        │\n        └── CHECKPOINT\n```\n\nAnd I would make this distinction hard:\n\n**Anchor = durable daily grounding.**  \n**Mid-Flight = lightweight re-grounding while moving.**  \n**Checkpoint = capture exactly what has been accomplished and preserve a resumable state.**\n\nAnd **CONFIDENCE stays mandatory in all three.** That's non-negotiable in my view."]}, "create_time": 1790381907.057508, "end_turn": true, "id": "49f8a4e4-052a-4d12-b664-7e41ade8eb5c", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "h7fqub", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id": "uggpv7", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "2": {"edited": false, "id": "p0nl0b", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "3": {"edited": false, "id": "rxaopz", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "4": {"edited": false, "id": "pkjp8a", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "5": {"edited": false, "id": "w05to3", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "6": {"edited": false, "id": "7u3inl", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "7": {"edited": false, "id": "mx6pp1", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "8": {"edited": false, "id": "g7wvbt", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "9": {"edited": false, "id": "rbc7iv", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}}, "con