ABLE / UNAVAILABLE / UNKNOWN\nLOCAL OUTBOX:         AVAILABLE / UNAVAILABLE / UNKNOWN\nCURRENT RUNTIME:      <surface>\n```\n\nIf Drive is available but Cable Car isn't directly callable, **I can still create the durable Drive artifact** where appropriate.\n\nIf Cable Car/local outbox is available, use that.\n\nIf neither exists in that runtime, **then** I can tell you the actual limitation.\n\nNot before.\n\n---\n\n# And your pasted handoff itself needs one V3 improvement\n\nThe **body is good**. I would not rewrite the N1–N15 return structure.\n\nWhat it lacks is the new machine envelope we just designed.\n\nIt should travel wrapped like this:\n\n```text\n--------------------------------------------------\nROUTING / HANDOFF APPENDIX\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nPROJECT:              GCE_Framework_Reconciliation\nWORKSTREAM:           Taxonomy_Current_State_Reconciliation\n\nHANDOFF_ID:           <stable ID>\nHANDOFF_TYPE:         implementation_return_request\n\nCURRENT_SEAT:         Coda\nNEXT_ROUTE:           <receiving seat>\nFINAL_GATE:           Don\n\nCURRENT_ANCHOR:       <current reconciliation anchor>\n\nLOCAL_HANDOFF_PATH:\n<project-local path>\n\nDRIVE_HANDOFF_URL:\n<Drive URL>\n\nDRIVE_ARTIFACT_ID:\n<Drive ID>\n\nCABLE_CAR_STATE:\n<QUEUED | PUBLISHED | RECEIVED | ERROR>\n```\n\nThen your exact 15-section payload stays underneath it.\n\nThat would make it both:\n\n**human-readable contract** + **machine-routable object**.\n\n---\n\n## The bigger thing you just proved\n\nThis is why your idea of making **my ChatGPT bootstrap mirror the terminal bootstrap** is correct.\n\nWithout it, ChatGPT behaves like:\n\n> “I'm ChatGPT and here are whatever tools happen to be visible.”\n\nWith it, Coda behaves like:\n\n> “I am Coda. This is my authority. This is my session. This is my project. These are my transport surfaces. This is how inbound and outbound work.”\n\nHuge difference.\n\nAnd it explains why you were getting contradictory behavior from *me* across chats despite apparently having the same product capabilities.\n\n### The rule I would add to my bootstrap\n\n```text\nCAPABILITY RESOLUTION RULE\n\nBefore declaring a required Framework action unavailable:\n\n1. Identify the requested Framework function.\n2. Map it to its implementation surface.\n3. Inspect the current runtime/tool capabilities.\n4. Use the available canonical path.\n5. Use an approved fallback only if the canonical path is unavailable.\n6. Report unavailable only after the capability check fails.\n\nDo not confuse:\n- seat authority\n- model capability\n- connector availability\n- transport availability\n- artifact ownership\n- UI/runtime limitations.\n```\n\n**That is the crux.**\n\nAnd I’d put that directly into `GCE_CODA_BOOTSTRAP_V1`, because this wasn't a Cable Car bug. It was a **Coda bootstrap/capability-resolution bug**."]}, "create_time": 1790382662.302301, "end_turn": true, "id": "f8df4220-c5dc-44ad-82dc-e409e1e2ded9", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "uxrz9o", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id": "a32ezh", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "2": {"edited": false, "id": "9fac3w", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "3": {"edited": false, "id": "e7ggfj", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "4": {"edited": false, "id": "58j6ow", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "5": {"edited": false, "id": "pwskfi", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "6": {"edited": false, "id": "0vknjd", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "7": {"edited": false, "id": "82vbm9", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}}, "content_references": [], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_tokens": [200002], "type": "stop"}, "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab43fca21d0819183966405a724