" (\\\"APPROVED — Phase 0 design begins\\\") | S5 §4 and all other artifacts: seat = Chiave | Same seat, two names in one document | Identity confusion in routing | Kimi (record fix in S5) | **NBRF** |\\n| **DR-12** | textual drift | S4 I1: package = \\\"requested evidence\\\" | S1 §2.5: \\\"all evidence ever acquired for this analyst across all runs\\\" | Wording implies delta vs. cumulative | IF-2's cumulative clause resolves it; I1 wording should align to prevent coder misreading | Chiave (wording fix at next revision) | **NBRF** — contract follows IF-2 |\\n| **DR-13** (D-13) — **RESOLVED** | — | S1 §2.1 Slate Definition | S5 pilot scope | Slate = one scheduled MLB game; multi-game days = independent slates | None | — | Closed |\\n| **DR-14** (D-10, downgraded) | implementation ambiguity | \\\"Different architecture family\\\" (S1) / provider registry check (S4 EX-2) | No vendor registry or assignment algorithm supplied | Who fills which slot is unspecified | None — this is an ordinary implementation choice *constrained* by EX-2 (≥3 families, pairwise L2, L3 outside pool) | Implementation + Talon within EX-2; Luce verifies | **Not a gate** |\\n| **DR-15** (D-14, downgraded) | implementation ambiguity | S4 §7: checkpoint/resume at gates; L3 fallback coordination | S1 §8: Talon owns scheduling/fallback coordination | Operational contract not yet written | Blocks Phase 2/3 ops readiness, not code | Talon + Chiave | **ICR** — schedule before Phase 2 |\\n| **DR-16** | textual drift | README version line: \\\"effective-N accounting\\\" | No prompt body defines effective-N (it is system-side artifact accounting) | Dangling version claim | None; prompts don't need it | Kimi (README wording) | **NBRF** |\\n| **DR-17** | implementation ambiguity | S1 Stage 5 tier conditions marked \\\"Typical\\\" | Prompt 09 encodes numeric thresholds (composite >0.75 etc.) | Which is normative? | Normalizer coder must know whether prompt numbers are the contract | Kimi | **ICR** — small; 