\\n| G4 protocol | S1 §7.1 table (14 tests; retry once, Correctable only) | the old \\\"isolated and correctable\\\" runtime-judgment language (dead) |\\n| Cost baseline | 53/slate budget reference; ledger = truth (S4 OB-4) | any cost cap (none exists) |\\n| Artifact schema | nine sections per S1 Stage 6 + IF-4 fields | a version number (none exists — DR-08) |\\n| Cadence | Overnight(1 call)/Morning(26)/PreGame(26); framing ×3 | S2's framing-2 row (arithmetically inconsistent) |\\n| Ruling references | ruling **content** strings | bare CR numbers (DR-02) |\\n\\n### 6.3 \\\"Build-ready\\\" translation (brief §8.5)\\n\\n| Phrase | Where | Precise gate state |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| \\\"Methodology Complete / Ready for Coder / Coder UNBLOCKED\\\" | S5 header, §2 | Overclaim relative to S4 (DR-01) |\\n| \\\"Post-gate, pre-build\\\" | S4 header | Accurate for the full build; gate = architecture gate passed, build phases 0–3 not started |\\n| \\\"All contracts pinned. No deferred blockers for pilot design.\\\" | S1 §Exec 10 | Mostly true; G2 threshold and artifact schema version are unpinned (DR-06/DR-08) |\\n| Phase 0 design | S5 §2 (GLM/Chiave), S4 §10 | Design-owned by Chiave; build-owned by Implementation |\\n\\n**Translation (DERIVED):** the system is *post-architecture-gate, pre-implementation*, with Phase 0–1 unblocked, and a short list of record fixes that must land before the coder handoff is re-issued as \\\"unblocked\\\" for semantic surfaces.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Implementation Contract by Pipeline Stage\\n\\nDerived from S1 + S4 + handoff-copy prompts. \\\"Gate\\\" = machine-checkable condition to progress. Claims are FACT where both S1/S4 agree, DERIVED where assembled.\\n\\n### 7.1 Acquisition (overnight pre-fetch + Stage 2c)\\n- **Inputs**: slate schedule; gap requests (Stage 2c); proactive list (pitcher profiles, batter splits, form, weather, injuries, market lines — S1 §2.2).\\n- **Outputs**: evidence items in the shared store, tagged (timestamp, source, reliability tier, run type, expiration).\\n- **Must never receive**: analyst outputs; anything destined for a specific analyst's package (acquisition is analyst-blind; delivery is a separate contract).\\n- **State**: persistent, append-only, SHA-256 content-addressed (DA-1). Identity = (entity, attribute, snapshot-time); time-variant data creates new items, never mutates (DA-2).\\n- **Session**: none (no model).\\n- **Access**: acquisition engine = trust boundary (SE-1); untrusted text marked/sanitized (SE-3); market-class items tagged `market` (IF-3).\\n- **Failure**: source outage → partial-data mode; requesting analysts get `unfilled(reason)`; severe gaps flagged (S4 §7). No analyst impact beyond unfilled statuses.\\n- **Provenance**: DA-3 tags mandatory per item.\\n- **Metering**: every acquisition logged (count + source); not provider-billable (OB-2 granularity by source).\\n- **Gate**: item passes schema + provenance completeness before store commit.\\n\\n### 7.2 Framing\\n- **Inputs**: pre-fetched raw slate data from the ingestion layer (prompt 01-B: \\\"You do NOT fetch data, verify sources, query APIs, or make external calls\\\").\\n- **Outputs**: populated Framing Schema `0.3-MLB` instance; `null`+reason-code for unavailable fields (enum: `not_yet_released|source_unreliable|not_applicable|timeout|error`).\\n- **Must never receive**: analyst outputs; evidence items; prior run's framing snapshot.\\n- **State**: ephemeral per invocation; snapshot persisted as record; **prior snapshots never delivered to analysts** (M28).\\n- **Session**: stateless; one invocation per run (3/slate).\\n- **Access**: architecturally isolated from analysts (S1 Stage 0 controls).\\n- **Failure**: malformed output → anomaly-tracked re-run (S1 §9.1 note); structural errors → G0 reject slate.\\n- **Provenance**: `schema_version`, `generated_at`, per-field sources; run captured in execution metadata (I9).\\n- **Metering**: 1 provider-billable request per run; tokens counted (OB-1).\\n- **Gate (G0)**: matchups resolvable; temporal window valid; schema validates structurally.\\n\\n### 7.3 Analyst first pass (Stage 1)\\n- **Inputs**: current pass's framing snapshot only (+ training knowledge). No evidence yet; Stage 1 gap statuses are `null` (prompts 02–06-B).\\n- **Outputs**: preliminary conviction per matchup; `information_gaps[]` (free-text `requested` today — DR-07); meta-cognitive calibration; self-critique; first-pass selection/confidence.\\n- **Must never receive**: peer outputs/reasoning/gap requests; evidence; N; peer personas; divergence knowledge; market-class evidence (non-D; D has exclusive market access).\\n- **State**: none persistent from the analyst's side; canary token injected per analyst per run (EX-6).\\n- **Session**: opens the run's single analyst session (EX-3: two provider requests, one session).\\n- **Access**: separate execution context per analyst; unique prompt + sampling parameters (EX-1).\\n- **Failure**: execution error → re-run or exclude; contamination indicator → G1 investigation (never proceed silently).\\n- **Provenance**: model version, prompt hash, parameters captured from execution metadata (I9/EX-5).\\n- **Metering**: 5 requests/run; tokens per analyst (OB-2).\\n- **Gate (G1)**: all 5 complete; coherent gap requests; canary/fingerprint clean.\\n\\n### 7.4 Gap-request router (Stage 2a/2b + IF-3)\\n- **Inputs**: 5 analysts' `information_gaps[]`.\\n- **Outputs**: structured requests {entity, attribute, timeframe, granularity, data class}; semantic dedup; feasibility flags (`unacquirable|too_expensive`).\\n- **Must never receive**: analyst reasoning/selections (gap items only — otherwise bias channel).\\n- **State**: persistent request log per analyst per slate (feeds cumulative request_status map).\\n- **Session**: n/a (deterministic code + parsing; DR-07 mapping contract required before coding semantics).\\n- **Access**: market-class request from non-D persona → `access_denied` + `market_data_request_rate` event (expected 0% non-D) (IF-3).\\n- **Failure**: malformed → `unfilled(malformed_request)`; no blocking.\\n- **Provenance**: requester → request → outcome mapping retained for status replay.\\n- **Metering**: router is code, not model (DERIVED from L1-analogous determinism; confirm with Chiave — no model call is budgeted for it in the 53).\\n- **Gate**: every gap item classified (structured class or malformed) before acquisition dispatch.\\n\\n### 7.5 Evidence acquisition (Stage 2c)\\nSame contract as 7.1, scoped to requested items; additionally:\\n- **Gate (G2 — DR-06)**: threshold % filled — **value UNKNOWN; gate cannot be made machine-checkable until Kimi pins it**. Interim behavior per S1: proceed with partial data, flag severe gaps.\\n\\n### 7.6 Package assembler (IF-2 choke point — the single most security-sensitive component)\\n- **Inputs**: current framing snapshot; store items matching the analyst's request history; request_status map (cumulative, with `acquired_in_run`).\\n- **Outputs**: per-analyst package = framing snapshot + own requested evidence (cumulative) + request_status map. **Nothing else, ever (I1).**\\n- **Must never receive into a package**: peer-requested evidence; market-class evidence for non-D personas (except framing-schema baseline lines — DR-18); prior framing snapshots; validation outputs; system commentary about the analyst.\\n- **State**: ephemeral assembly; every assembly logged and reconstructable post-hoc (IF-2).\\n- **Session**: n/a.\\n- **Access**: single choke-point function; role-keyed market filter enforced here AND at IF-3 (defense in depth).\\n- **Failure**: any package item not reconstructable as {schema field | fulfilled request | status entry} = G6 failure (IF-2 Verify).\\n- **Provenance**: disclosure line included (M29); assembly logged.\\n- **Metering**: n/a (code).\\n- **Gate**: package audit passes before delivery.\\n\\n### 7.7 Analyst re-analysis (Stage 3)\\n- **Inputs**: same session continues; package from 7.6; replacement evidence items only if G4 retry (VL-6 — corrections arrive as evidence, never as commentary).\\n- **Outputs**: final selection (or Pass), raw confidence, reasoning with citations, key evidence, residual uncertainty, self-critique; gap items with system-populated `status/reason_if_unfilled/acquired_in_run`.\\n- **Must never receive**: everything in 7.3's forbidden list, plus validation reports (sealed).\\n- **State**: session transcript sealed into provenance at run end (EX-3).\\n- **Session**: **same session as Stage 1** — continuation, not fresh context (M19/EX-3).\\n- **Access**: same as 7.3.\\n- **Failure**: incomplete → G3 re-run.\\n- **Provenance**: as 7.3.\\n- **Metering**: 5 requests/run (full first-pass context carried — token-heavy; OB-1).\\n- **Gate (G3)**: structured outputs; reasoning traceable to evidence; residual uncertainties flagged.\\n\\n### 7.8 Validation L1\\n- **Inputs**: analyst final outputs; evidence package; framing schema.\\n- **Outputs**: PASS|FLAG|FAIL + mechanical findings; FAILs needing semantic classification (CO-3/5, UC-1..4) routed to L2 (VL-2); mechanical classes (CH-1/2/4/5, CO-1/2/4) decided here (VL-1).\\n- **Must never receive**: nothing forbidden — L1 sees what the analyst saw.\\n- **State**: deterministic code; replay-consistent.\\n- **Session**: n/a. **No model call** (S1 Stage 4; DERIVED that no ledger entry accrues).\\n- **Access**: read-only.\\n- **Failure**: L1 execution failure blocks the entry; never skipped (I5).\\n- **Provenance**: findings + routed classifications logged per analysis (VL-2).\\n- **Metering**: none (code).\\n- **Gate**: every FAIL carries a class or a routed classification before G4.\\n\\n### 7.9 Validation L2\\n- **Inputs**: analyst output (minus raw confidence), evidence package, framing schema; L1-routed semantic FAILs.\\n- **Outputs**: PASS|FLAG|FAIL + `failure_class` (`critical_hallucination|uncorrectable|correctable|null`), `test_id` (CH/UC/CO-n), `classification_reason` (prompts 07/08-B).\\n- **Must never receive**: analyst raw confidence; peer outputs; normalized tier.\\n- **State**: report sealed on FAIL (VL-6).\\n- **Session**: one invocation per analyst per layer.\\n- **Access**: model family ≠ analyst family, per pair (EX-2/VL-3).\\n- **Failure**: execution failure blocks that entry; retry; never skipped.\\n- **Provenance**: validator model/version captured.\\n- **Metering**: 5/run baseline + retries in ledger.\\n- **Gate**: every FAIL classified (no runtime judgment — CR-2).\\n\\n### 7.10 Validation L3\\n- **Inputs**: analyst output + L1 + L2 reports; framing schema.\\n- **Outputs**: as L2 + red-team opinion (quality score, calibration, missed evidence, alternatives).\\n- **Must never receive**: peer outputs; normalized tier.\\n- **State**: sealed reports.\\n- **Session**: one per analyst.\\n- **Access**: model outside analyst pool; **pre-approved fallback provider configured and exercised before pilot** (EX-2/VL-4).\\n- **Failure**: primary outage → fallback activates; fallback outage → entries blocked, never bypassed (S4 §7).\\n- **Provenance**: as L2.\\n- **Metering**: 5/run + retries.\\n- **Gate**: as L2; then G4 action table executes deterministically.\\n\\n### 7.11 Normalizer\\n- **Inputs**: exactly {analyst self-assessment, evidence sufficiency score (deterministic code: `fill_rate × weighted_reliability × conflict_penalty × recency_decay` — NO-5), validation state (L1/L2/L3), validation flags}.\\n- **Outputs**: tier ∈ {Conviction, Lean, Tentative, Pass, Contradicted} + justification + all four inputs preserved (NO-4).\\n- **Must never receive**: reasoning; selection; peers; matchup context (\\\"blind to the conclusion\\\").\\n- **State**: stateless, per-analyst, no batching (NO-2).\\n- **Session**: one invocation per included analyst.\\n- **Access**: neutral model; any capable family (README).\\n- **Failure**: failure blocks the whole artifact; retry; never bypassed (S4 §7).\\n- **Provenance**: input-set version recorded (NO-3 — version-gated changes).\\n- **Metering**: 5/run.\\n- **Gate (G5)**: every included analysis tiered + justified; FAIL analysts never receive Conviction/Lean.\\n\\n### 7.12 SAP assembler\\n- **Inputs**: all stage outputs; effective-N accounting; integrity report data (canaries, fingerprints, gate outcomes, anomalies, session-continuity verification).\\n- **Outputs**: nine-section SAP (S1 Stage 6); exclusions with `{analyst, layer, class, test_id, detail, retry_number, action}`.\\n- **Must never receive**: nothing beyond stage outputs; must not synthesize a system pick or blended score (Don #17).\\n- **State**: artifact immutable after G6 (IF-4).\\n- **Session**: n/a.\\n- **Access**: assembler is code; divergence matrix computed here.\\n- **Failure**: assembly failure → re-assemble (G6); structural incompleteness blocks.\\n- **Provenance**: full §8 chain; model/prompt versions from execution metadata only (I9).\\n- **Metering**: n/a.\\n- **Gate (G6)**: nine sections complete; effective-N present; provenance intact; integrity report present; no contamination evidence.\\n\\n### 7.13 Artifact store\\n- **Inputs**: G6-passed artifacts.\\n- **Outputs**: retrievable immutable artifacts; SAP-PreGame flagged terminal per slate.\\n- **Must never receive**: mutated artifacts (store enforces immutability — IF-4).\\n- **State**: persistent; store snapshots join the §0 backup set post-build.\\n- **Session/Access**: n/a; store-level immutability enforcement.\\n- **Failure**: whole-store failure → abort; restore from DA-5; no artifact preferable to a wrong artifact.\\n- **Provenance**: artifact-level chain complete.\\n- **Metering**: n/a.\\n- **Gate**: G6 pass is the only write path.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Decisions the Implementation Engineer Is Not Permitted to Make\\n\\n1. **N** (configured analysts) — pinned at 5 (M11/Don #11).\\n2. **Persona definitions, lenses, or count** — M3, S1 §4.\\n3. **Framing schema fields, enums, or versions** — M2/IF-1; changes are versioned methodology decisions.\\n4. **Package contents** — I1/IF-2: snapshot + requested evidence + request_status map, nothing else, ever. No \\\"helpful\\\" additions.\\n5. **Evidence push** — nothing enters a package unrequested (CR-1/DA-4), including overnight pre-fetch.\\n6. **Market-class scope decisions** — which classes are `market` and who receives them (Persona D only) — §4.3/IF-3. Baseline framing lines are NOT market-class evidence (IF-2); do not strip them (DR-18 pending Kimi confirmation).\\n7. **Validation layer count, order, skippability, or blindness rules** — P4/VL-1..8. L2 never sees raw confidence; L3 outside pool.\\n8. **G4 classes, tests, actions, or retry counts** — S1 §7.1/M30. No new failure classes; no second retry; no runtime-judgment escapes (CR-2).\\n9. **Forward-only topology** — no path from validation outputs to analyst context (I3/VL-7). Corrections only as replacement evidence items.\\n10. **Normalization inputs, blindness, or tier enum** — NO-1..6/M8. Contradicted is system-assignable only.\\n11. **Artifact sections, terminal semantics, or immutability** — M10/IF-4. SAP-PreGame is terminal; no system pick, no blended score (Don #17).\\n12. **Effective-N definitions** — configured/ran/included/excluded semantics; retries count in ledger, not ran_n (VL-8).\\n13. **Cadence, timing windows, or new run types** — S1 §2; on-demand is out of pilot scope (Don #18) — do not build the surface, stubs, or \\\"temporary\\\" triggers.\\n14. **Session semantics** — intra-run continuation, inter-run fresh context (M19/EX-3). Do not implement Stage 3 as a fresh call.\\n15. **request_status reason enum or gap lifecycle states** — M23/IF-2/IF-3.\\n16. **Cost caps or budget enforcement** — none exist; measure only (Don #8/D5). Budget 53 is reference, ledger is truth (OB-4).\\n17. **Contamination methodology** — canary injection, fingerprinting, pairwise sampling (EX-6/M7).\\n18. **Slate definition** — one MLB game per slate (S1 §2.1).\\n19. **Isolation mechanisms** — separate contexts, no shared memory/fs/netns/env (EX-1).\\n20. **Kill-switch-equivalents** — G4 exclusions are final; there is no promote/revive path (analogous to standing workspace doctrine; here explicit in §7.1).\\n\\n**Unresolved choices embedded in the package (route before coding that surface):** G2 threshold (DR-06); free-text→structured gap mapping (DR-07); artifact schema version (DR-08); prompt isolation sentence scope (DR-18); normalization numeric-threshold normativity (DR-17).\\n\\nOrdinary implementation discretion (allowed): vendor/provider selection within EX-2 constraints; language/framework; infrastructure; parser internals once DR-07 contract lands; test harness design; monitoring dashboards.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Routed Questions\\n\\n| # | Question | Seat | Why that seat |\\n|---|----------|------|---------------|\\n| Q1 | Confirm canonical methodology: stamp S1 content as v0.3.2 (or declare it canonical v0.3.1) and retire S2 to provenance (DR-03) | **Kimi** (record), **Coda** (canon confirm) | Methodology owner + supersession control |\\n| Q2 | Adjudicate ruling-ID crosswalk; declare content-keyed binding interim (DR-02) | **Coda** | Canon/supersession; cross-seat conflict |\\n| Q3 | Pin G2 threshold: value, denominator, action when unmet (DR-06) | **Kimi** (methodology gate); **Don** only if it's a business threshold | Gate criteria are methodology-owned |\\n| Q4 | Assign artifact schema version; publish versioned artifact contract (DR-08) | **Chiave** | Artifact interface owner |\\n| Q5 | Specify free-text gap → IF-3 structured form mapping + semantic dedup contract (DR-07) | **Kimi + Chiave** jointly | Splits methodology semantics / interface form |\\n| Q6 | Confirm scope of prompt sentence \\\"system will not deliver lines to you\\\" vs baseline framing lines delivered to all (DR-18) | **Kimi** (prompt wording) | Prompts are methodology-owned |\\n| Q7 | Confirm prompt 09 numeric thresholds are the normative tier contract vs S1's \\\"Typical\\\" (DR-17) | **Kimi** | Same |\\n| Q8 | Refresh S4 §14 pending list (3 of 6 landed); align I1 wording with IF-2 (DR-04/DR-12); rename artifact file (typo \\\"Architecure\\\"; S4 itself instructs `EC8_Architecture_v1.0.md`) | **Chiave** (own document) | Architecture records |\\n| Q9 | On-demand revival policy lines (who may trigger; quota) — needed only when the surface is revived, post-pilot (S4 CR-2) | **Don** | Policy lines; deliberately deferred |\\n| Q10 | Checkpoint/resume operational contract + L3 fallback coordination before Phase 2/3 (DR-15) | **Talon + Chiave** | Operations + failure semantics |\\n| Q11 | Provider/vendor slot assignments | **No ruling needed** — Implementation + Talon within EX-2; Luce verifies | Ordinary constrained choice (DR-14) |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Implementation Readiness Verdict\\n\\n### PARTIALLY BLOCKED\\n\\n**READY WITH NON-BLOCKING FIXES (can start immediately):**\\n- **Phase 0 — Foundation**: evidence store (DA-1..5: append-only, SHA-256, identity, provenance, backup), secrets (SE-5), data-layer schema. No blocked surface touches this.\\n- **Phase 1 — Orchestration**: provider abstraction with ledger hooks (OB-3) and observability emit-points (OB-5). The 53/26/1 budget is now decomposable and testable (DR-05 closed).\\n- Non-semantic scaffolding: run IDs, scheduling skeletons, store round-trips.\\n\\n**BLOCKED SURFACES (named):**\\n1. **G2 gate assertions** — threshold value absent (DR-06, Q3 → Kimi).\\n2. **Artifact schema binding** — no version exists for downstream/test pinning (DR-08, Q4 → Chiave).\\n3. **Gap-request router semantics** — free-text→structured mapping and dedup contract unspecified (DR-07, Q5 → Kimi+Chiave).\\n4. **Package-assembler market-filter semantics** — prompt wording vs baseline-lines delivery (DR-18, Q6 → Kimi).\\n5. **Ruling-keyed traceability in tests/docs** — bind to ruling content, not CR IDs, until DR-02 is adjudicated (Q2 → Coda).\\n\\n**NOT BLOCKED (downgraded from v0.1):** framing scheduler + call-budget assertions (now specified: 3 framing/slate); overnight model-call question (closed: 1 framing call); multi-game slate topology (closed: independent slates); on-demand (settled: excluded); evidence delivery model (aligned: request-gated store-only).\\n\\n**Note on evidence:** no execution evidence was supplied; every claim above is FACT/DERIVED/CONFLICT from records, not VERIFIED. This is a translation document, not a correctness certification (Luce's seat).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Recommended Next Handoff\\n\\n1. **To Coda** (single session): adjudicate DR-01/DR-02/DR-03 — readiness-state contradiction, ruling-ID crosswalk, canonical methodology stamp. This unblocks the \\\"unblocked\\\" claim in S5.\\n2. **To Kimi**: issue the v0.3.2 record stamp (or canonical declaration) over S1 content; pin G2 (Q3); specify the gap-mapping contract (Q5); fix prompt wording (Q6, Q18) and re-version prompts (DR-09); correct S5 §9/§11 (DR-10/DR-11).\\n3. **To Chiave**: assign artifact schema version (Q4); refresh §14; align I1 wording; rename the spec file per its own closing instruction.\\n4. **To Implementation (parallel, now)**: begin Phase 0 + Phase 1 against §7 contracts of this document; bind records by content hash.\\n5. **To Luce**: define the verification evidence matrix for the four seeded pilot failures (S4 §11) so Phase 3 acceptance is checkable on arrival.\\n6. **To Talon**: draft the scheduling + L3-fallback operational contract (Q10) in parallel; needed by Phase 2, not Phase 0.\\n\\n*Prior-handoff continuity: this document supersedes `EC8_Methodology_Architecture_Reconciliation_v0.1.md` — it resolves D-05/D-06/D-07/D-13, narrows D-01, retains D-08 (as DR-06) and D-11 (as DR-08), and adds the ruling-ID crosswalk (DR-02), the dual-v0.3.1 finding (DR-03), and the prompt/baseline market wording conflict (DR-18).*\\n\"},{\"url\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1oprgQ1DkAfDeg-AS3njg_YBcmCLOYoaI/view?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"EC8_Methodology_Architecture_Reconciliation_v0.1.md\",\"id\":\"1oprgQ1DkAfDeg-AS3njg_YBcmCLOYoaI\",\"mime_type\":\"text/markdown\",\"size\":\"22033\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:47:12.335Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:47:12.335Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":null,\"display_title\":\"EC8_Methodology_Architecture_Reconciliation_v0.1.md\",\"display_url\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1oprgQ1DkAfDeg-AS3njg_YBcmCLOYoaI/view?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1EXzOuIyaLkTFB0pL6g5xXTWddHcbjN3O\"],\"shared\":true,\"content\":\"# EC8 Methodology <-> Architecture Implementation Reconciliation\\n\\n**Prepared by:** Principal Consultant — Technical Translation / Integration  \\n**Status:** Reconciliation of supplied package; not a methodology or architecture amendment  \\n**Sources:** Kimi methodology `v0.3.1` in both archives; fixed `HANDOFF_v0.3.1`; Chiave `Architecture Specification v1.0` / `EC8_Architecure_Brief.txt`; production prompts 01-09.\\n\\nClaim labels used below: **FACT**, **DERIVED**, **PROPOSED**, **UNKNOWN**, **CONFLICT**, **OUTSIDE AUTHORITY**.\\n\\n## 1. Executive Reconciliation\\n\\n**FACT:** The intended system is a scheduled MLB Sovereign Analysis Pipeline. It creates five independent analyst landscapes, not a consensus pick, validates each analysis through L1/L2/L3, normalizes confidence, and emits immutable SAP artifacts.\\n\\n**FACT:** The accepted architecture is structurally aligned with the accepted methodology on isolation, request-gated evidence delivery, market-persona exclusivity, forward-only validation, deterministic G4, effective-N, provenance, metering, and terminal `SAP-PreGame`.\\n\\n**CONFLICT / record defect:** The fixed handoff declares “Ready for Coder,” while Chiave v1.0 declares “Post-gate, pre-build,” companion methodology pending six v0.3.2 record fixes, and Phase 0 still has exit criteria. This is a status contradiction, not permission to choose a side.\\n\\n**CONFLICT:** The package's older architecture brief and v0.3 source retain OnDemand and an `OnDemand` framing enum; the accepted v0.3.1 methodology and Chiave v1.0 remove OnDemand from pilot scope and bind the build to the corrected enum. The old artifacts are provenance only.\\n\\n**CONFLICT:** Ruling IDs drift. In the handoff, CR-1..CR-4 are evidence gating, deterministic G4, cost, and framing. In Chiave v1.0, CR-1 is evidence gating, CR-2 is OnDemand scope/revival conditions, CR-3 is cost, CR-4 is G4, and CR-5 is framing. The fixed methodology text also assigns differing names to CR-2/CR-4 in places.\\n\\n**IMPLEMENTATION CLARIFICATION REQUIRED:** “53 calls/slate” is a budget fact, but the supplied documents do not provide a machine-checkable call decomposition. Fresh framing is required for Overnight, Morning, and Pre-Game, yet Overnight is described as one call and full runs as 26. The ledger must count actual calls; Kimi/Chiave must document the intended baseline decomposition before budget assertions become tests.\\n\\n**VERDICT:** **PARTIALLY BLOCKED.** Phase 0 store/secrets design and non-semantic orchestration scaffolding can proceed. Framing scheduler, call-budget assertions, ruling-keyed traceability, terminal artifact binding, and any OnDemand surface are blocked until the named record/contract questions are resolved.\\n\\n## 2. System Intent Summary\\n\\n**FACT:** Within the final 24-hour window for each scheduled MLB slate, ingest the slate and create a schema-enumerated framing snapshot; acquire evidence into an append-only provenance store; run five isolated, heterogeneous, persona-specific analysts; let each request and receive only its own evidence; continue each analyst in-session for re-analysis; validate forward-only through deterministic L1, pairwise different-family L2, and outside-pool L3; normalize from four preserved inputs; and seal an immutable nine-section SAP landscape.\\n\\nCadence is Overnight (framing/store population only), Morning (full analyst run), and Pre-Game (full analyst run; terminal). Prior snapshots remain records and are never delivered. Market-class evidence is exclusive to Persona D. Missing data remains explicit. Retries, exclusions, effective-N, integrity, provenance, and provider/token cost are recorded. Pilot scope is one scheduled MLB slate, N=5, full validation, and four seeded failures. No consensus, EV engine, human arbitration, trigger reruns, or pilot OnDemand.\\n\\n## 3. Methodology -> Architecture Traceability\\n\\n| Methodology requirement | Source | Architecture contract | Status | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Five independent personas; no peer context | Methodology §§1, 3.2, 5; prompts 02-06 | I2, EX-1, EX-6 | Exact | Architecture adds process/container/network/env isolation and canaries. |\\n| Analysts self-determine gaps | §§1.4 P2, Stage 2 | IF-3, DA-4 | Exact | Store may be broad; delivery is request-gated. |\\n| Package invariant | §§2.5, Stage 2 | I1, IF-2 | Exact | Single choke point and audit are machine-enforced. |\\n| Evidence identity and cumulative delivery | §2.5 | IF-2, DA-1/2/3 | Partial | `acquired_in_run` and complete status-map shape need schema binding. |\\n| Market evidence only Persona D | §4.3; prompt 05 | IF-2/3, SE-4 | Exact | Boundary and re-check are explicit. |\\n| Intra-run continuity; inter-run freshness | §2.6, Stage 3 | EX-3 | Exact | Retry also stays in same session per VL-6. |\\n| Heterogeneity | §3 Stage 1 | EX-2 | Partial | Architecture gives >=3 families and pairwise L2 rule; provider assignment/registry is not supplied. |\\n| Three validation layers; no skip | §4 | VL-1..7, I3/I5 | Exact | L1 semantic router is architecture completion under standing rulings. |\\n| G4 deterministic classification/retry | §7.1 | VL-2, VL-5, VL-6 | Exact | Observable classification tests are methodology-owned. |\\n| Forward-only validation | §4 | I3, VL-7 | Exact | Corrections are replacement evidence only. |\\n| Normalizer four inputs, neutral/stateless | §5, prompt 09 | NO-1..6 | Exact | Selection/reasoning/peers forbidden. |\\n| Confidence tiers and effective-N | §§5-6 | IF-4, NO-4/6 | Partial | Tier enum is methodology-owned; artifact schema version is architecture-owned and not yet pinned. |\\n| Integrity report | §3/Stage 6 | IF-4, I7 | Exact | Includes contamination, gates, anomalies, continuity. |\\n| Terminal SAP-PreGame; Morning retained | §2.3-2.4, §6 | IF-4 | Exact | Older source's SAP-OnDemand is stale for pilot. |\\n| Append-only evidence/provenance/replay | §§2, 6, 9 | DA-1..5, I4/I9 | Exact | Re-execution verifies process, not historical result. |\\n| Cost measurement at execution point | §9 | I10, OB-1..4 | Partial | Unit is fixed; 53-call decomposition and provider pricing binding are unresolved. |\\n| Failure behavior | §§7, 7.1 | §7 Failure Domains, checkpoints | Partial | Checkpoint/resume is architecture completion; acquisition threshold semantics remain underspecified. |\\n\\n## 4. Architecture -> Methodology Back-Trace\\n\\n| Architecture contract | Authorizing source | Classification | Trace / issue |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| I1/IF-2 package choke point | Methodology package invariant; CR-1 | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | Exact. |\\n| I2/EX-1 isolation and canaries | P1 and §5 controls | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | Container/process granularity is architecture-owned completion. |\\n| I3/VL-7 forward-only | Stage 4 forward-only rule | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | Exact. |\\n| I4 replay-as-record | Provenance/artifact requirements | REASONABLY DERIVED | Canonical replay semantics are architecture-owned completion; no methodology conflict found. |\\n| I6 machine-checkable gates | §7.1 G4 ruling | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | Exact. |\\n| IF-1 fixed `0.3-MLB`; no OnDemand | schema §3.1 plus accepted v0.3.1 scope | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | The `OnDemand` enum in older artifacts is stale. |\\n| IF-4 independent artifact schema and immutability | Stage 6 plus architecture ownership | ARCHITECTURE-OWNED COMPLETION | Binding version and store immutability require implementation contract. |\\n| VL-2 L1 semantic router | G4 determinism and gates-as-checkpoints standing rulings | ARCHITECTURE-OWNED COMPLETION | Explicitly flagged by Chiave; not a new methodology ruling. |\\n| Checkpoint/resume at each gate | gates-as-checkpoints standing ruling | ARCHITECTURE-OWNED COMPLETION | Requires persistence semantics and idempotency contract. |\\n| L3 fallback pre-approved/configured/exercised | methodology L3 fallback requirement | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | Operations coordination belongs to Talon; implementation must expose the hook. |\\n| SE-1..7 security boundaries | prompt/data isolation and trust requirements | REASONABLY DERIVED | Security implementation is Chiave-owned; OnDemand trust boundary is deferred. |\\n| OB-3 provider abstraction metering | methodology cost ledger | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | Exact provider/invoice integration is not specified. |\\n\\nNo supplied architecture contract was found to authorize a consensus engine, EV engine, trigger-based rerun, human arbitration, market access for non-D, or pilot OnDemand.\\n\\n## 5. Discrepancy Register\\n\\n| ID | Classification | Source A | Source B | Conflict / impact | Owner | Gate |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| D-01 | status drift | HANDOFF §1-2, §9 | Chiave v1.0 header/§10 | “Coder unblocked/ready” vs post-gate/pre-build and pending v0.3.2 fixes. | Coda | GOVERNANCE / DON DECISION |\\n| D-02 | stale handoff | HANDOFF §9 | Chiave v1.0 §0/§14 | Handoff says architecture brief does not exist; supplied canonical architecture does. | Coda | NON-BLOCKING RECORD FIX |\\n| D-03 | ruling-ID drift | methodology changelog; HANDOFF §4 | Chiave §12 | Same CR IDs carry different ruling names; traceability tests cannot bind safely. | Coda + Kimi + Chiave | GOVERNANCE / DON DECISION |\\n| D-04 | semantic conflict | old v0.3 / old architecture brief | accepted v0.3.1 + Chiave v1.0 | OnDemand and enum retained in old records but removed from pilot. | Coda | NON-BLOCKING RECORD FIX; pilot surface blocked |\\n| D-05 | version drift | Chiave §0/§14 | handoff title/status | Architecture v1.0 references methodology v0.3.1 pending v0.3.2 record fixes; handoff calls v0.3.1 complete. | Kimi + Coda | IMPLEMENTATION CLARIFICATION REQUIRED |\\n| D-06 | implementation ambiguity | methodology §2, §9 | Chiave OB-4 | 53 total / 26 full-run calls is not decomposed against three framing snapshots and all stages. | Kimi + Chiave | ARCHITECTURE GATE |\\n| D-07 | implementation ambiguity | methodology §2.1/§2.6 | Chiave IF-1/§7 | “Fresh framing snapshot” may imply a model invocation, but only Overnight=1 and full-run=26 are budgeted. | Kimi | METHODOLOGY GATE |\\n| D-08 | missing contract | Stage 2 G2 | Chiave §7 | `>threshold%` has no value, denominator, or action when unmet; partial mode is described but not parameterized. | Kimi | METHODOLOGY GATE |\\n| D-09 | missing contract | Stage 2/IF-3 | Chiave IF-3 | Semantic deduplication, requester-to-item mapping, and cumulative status-map schema are not specified enough for deterministic replay. | Kimi + Chiave | IMPLEMENTATION CLARIFICATION REQUIRED |\\n| D-10 | missing contract | prompts/README | EX-2 | “Different architecture family” registry and assignment algorithm are absent; normalization family constraints are absent. | Chiave | ARCHITECTURE GATE |\\n| D-11 | missing contract | Stage 6 | IF-4 | Artifact schema version and exact nine-section JSON contract are not supplied. | Chiave | ARCHITECTURE GATE |\\n| D-12 | textual drift | methodology versions | Chiave §14 | Pending six fixes include Stage 6 terminal line, ruling numbering, attribution, H1 version; source package does not include accepted v0.3.2. | Kimi | METHODOLOGY GATE |\\n| D-13 | scope ambiguity | methodology handoff | Chiave §11 | “one MLB slate” versus handoff definition of slate as one scheduled game; multi-game execution topology is unclear. | Don + Kimi | GOVERNANCE / DON DECISION |\\n| D-14 | operational boundary | Chiave §7/§13 | pilot/handoff | Checkpoint/resume and L3 fallback require deployment, persistence, and recovery behavior not owned by coder alone. | Talon + Chiave | IMPLEMENTATION CLARIFICATION REQUIRED |\\n\\n## 6. Version / Ruling Crosswalk\\n\\n| Subject | Safe binding now | Unsafe/stale reference |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Methodology | Accepted `EC8_AI_Convergence_v0.3.1.md` content as supplied, with v0.3.2 record fixes unresolved | `EC8_AI_Convergence_v0.3.md` as normative source |\\n| Architecture | `Architecture Specification v1.0` / `EC8_Architecure_Brief.txt` | Older `Chiave_Architecture_Brief.md` that still exposes OnDemand |\\n| Framing schema | `0.3-MLB`, `run_context ∈ {Overnight, Morning, PreGame}` | Any schema containing `OnDemand`; old schema text with divergent enum |\\n| Prompts | Fixed handoff prompts 01-09, prompt package v0.3 | Prompt copies without manifest/hash binding |\\n| Artifact | Nine sections; terminal `SAP-PreGame`; schema version must be assigned by Chiave | `SAP-OnDemand` for pilot; unversioned artifact JSON |\\n| Rulings | Content can be implemented only after a canonical ID map is issued | Binding tests to CR number alone |\\n\\n## 7. Implementation Contract By Pipeline Stage\\n\\nThe following is a translation of accepted contracts, not production code.\\n\\n| Stage | Inputs / outputs | Must never receive | State / session | Access / failure | Provenance / metering | Gate |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Acquisition | Raw slate/source requests -> immutable evidence items/status | Peer outputs, analyst reasoning; secrets in payloads | Persistent append-only store; acquisition execution ephemeral | Source failure => `unfilled(reason)`; no silent substitution | SHA-256 identity, source, time, reliability, run type, expiration; meter acquisition at execution | Source item valid and stored or explicit status |\\n| Framing | Raw slate + trusted structured inputs -> `0.3-MLB` snapshot | Analyst outputs, prose judgment, prior snapshot delivery | Snapshot persistent; framing call isolated | Invalid schema blocks G0; no OnDemand pilot context | model/prompt/params/runtime metadata; one ledger entry per actual call | G0 |\\n| Analyst first pass | Current framing snapshot + training knowledge -> structured preliminary analysis and gap requests | Peers, N, peer personas, divergence, prior runs, unrequested evidence, market data unless D | Fresh context per run; continuous into Stage 3 | Execution failure retry/exclude per slot; contamination recorded | analyst canary, model family, prompt/params, session ID; provider ledger | G1 |\\n| Gap-request router | Analyst-owned structured requests -> authorized acquisition work/status | Peer request content for delivery; market requests from non-D | Ephemeral routing plus persistent request lifecycle | Malformed => `unfilled(malformed_request)`; non-D market => `access_denied` + event | requester persona, request ID, policy decision, timestamps | Every request authorized and traceable |\\n| Evidence acquisition | Authorized requests/store -> immutable items | Analyst outputs and peer context | Persistent store; no analyst session | Partial mode; `unfilled` reason; never mutate item | Per-item lineage and acquisition ledger | G2 inputs available; unresolved threshold contract D-08 |\\n| Package assembler | Current snapshot + that analyst's requested/cumulative items + status map -> package | Peer items/reasoning/gaps, prior snapshots, non-D market | Single choke point; package ephemeral, audit persistent | Any invariant breach => G6-style failure/block | package hash, item IDs, disclosure line, audit record | I1/IF-2 audit passes |\\n| Analyst re-analysis | Same session + package -> final analysis | Validation reports, peer data, sealed corrections as commentary | Same session as first pass; retry same session; fresh next run | Incomplete/hallucination => G3 action; correction only as replacement evidence | session transcript sealed; all evidence IDs | G3 |\\n| L1 | Analysis + package + registries -> mechanical report / semantic classification event | Peer outputs; analyst raw confidence is not needed | Stateless per analysis; persisted report | Failure routes through L2 classification; never skip | test IDs, registry versions, timestamps; ledger only if model router invoked (L1 itself no model call) | VL-1/VL-2 |\\n| L2 | Analysis + evidence/package + L1 report -> pairwise validation | Raw analyst confidence; peer analysts; wrong-family validator | Independent validator context; report sealed | FAIL classified; correctable retry once, second FAIL exclude; execution failure blocks/retries | validator model family, report hash, class/test IDs, ledger | VL-3/VL-6 |\\n| L3 | Analysis + L1/L2 reports -> red-team report | Analyst pool identity/context beyond allowed input; no bypass | Outside-pool context; fallback preconfigured | Primary outage -> fallback; both unavailable blocks, never skip | provider/fallback identity, report lineage, ledger | VL-4/VL-6 |\\n| Normalizer | Exactly self-assessment, sufficiency score, validation state, flags -> tier + justification | Reasoning, selection, peer outputs, raw package | Stateless per analyst; no batching | Failure blocks artifact and retries; `Contradicted` system-assigned only | formula/version, model metadata, four inputs preserved; meter model call | NO-1..6 / G5 |\\n| SAP assembler | Framing, included analyses, validation, divergence, sufficiency, provenance, integrity -> nine-section artifact | Mutable post-G6 inputs; hidden smoothing; unrecorded exclusions | Persistent immutable artifact; checkpointed orchestration | Missing section/gate/provenance blocks; no artifact preferred to wrong artifact | full chain, effective-N, integrity, cost ledger reconciliation | G6 |\\n| Artifact store | Validated artifact + manifest -> immutable retrievable terminal | Mutation, overwrite, unbound schema | Write-once persistent store; backup snapshots | Store failure aborts/recovery from DA-5 | artifact hash, schema/method/prompt versions, run ID | Immutability and restore test |\\n\\n## 8. Decisions the Implementation Engineer Is Not Permitted to Make\\n\\n- Choose between conflicting methodology or architecture versions.\\n- Treat the handoff's “coder unblocked” wording as authority to bypass the architecture gate.\\n- Reintroduce OnDemand, trigger reruns, consensus, EV scoring, or human arbitration.\\n- Decide whether fresh framing means a model call, or alter the 53/26 budget decomposition.\\n- Define a slate as one game or a multi-game slate.\\n- Alter the framing schema, enum, null/reason-code behavior, or artifact section semantics.\\n- Deliver prior snapshots, peer outputs, peer requests, peer personas, or non-D market evidence.\\n- Share analyst filesystem, network namespace, memory, environment, prompt template, or secrets.\\n- Select model families, L2 pairings, L3 provider/fallback, or normalization visibility in a way that changes heterogeneity/isolation.\\n- Convert a validation report into analyst-visible instructions or feed validation backward.\\n- Replace evidence items in place, hide missing evidence, or invent a fallback source/status.\\n- Change G4 tests, classes, retry count, retry session, exclusion behavior, or effective-N accounting.\\n- Define the G2 threshold, reliability formula, sufficiency formula, tier conditions, or `Contradicted` semantics.\\n- Assign artifact schema version, terminal pointer behavior, or post-G6 mutability without Chiave.\\n- Claim cost truth from configured intent, call counts alone, or a reconstructed ledger.\\n- Decide security boundaries, credential placement, retention, replay semantics, or checkpoint idempotency.\\n\\nOrdinary choices such as language, library, queue implementation, serialization library, and non-semantic naming are permitted only if all above contracts remain unchanged and tests expose the contract.\\n\\n## 9. Routed Questions\\n\\n1. **Kimi:** Is the normative implementation source v0.3.1 pending v0.3.2, and what exact six record fixes comprise v0.3.2? Provide canonical ruling IDs and the H1/version crosswalk.\\n2. **Kimi:** Does “fresh framing snapshot” require a new framing model invocation for Morning and Pre-Game? Publish the exact 53-call decomposition, including framing, analyst, validation, normalization, and retry exclusions.\\n3. **Kimi:** What is the numeric G2 threshold, denominator, freshness window, and action when the threshold is not met?\\n4. **Kimi + Chiave:** Define deterministic request deduplication, cumulative `request_status` schema, `acquired_in_run`, and requester-to-evidence authorization mapping.\\n5. **Chiave:** Issue a canonical ruling-ID map and artifact schema version/JSON contract, including exact nine sections and schema compatibility rules.\\n6. **Chiave:** Publish the provider-family registry, analyst-to-family assignment, pairwise L2 constraint, L3 outside-pool constraint, and normalization provider rule.\\n7. **Don + Kimi:** Resolve whether “slate” means one scheduled MLB game or a multi-game unit; specify run and artifact identity for a multi-game day.\\n8. **Chiave + Talon:** Define checkpoint persistence, resume idempotency, L3 fallback activation, operator ownership, and recovery evidence for the pilot.\\n9. **Coda:** Rule which older package artifacts are provenance-only and issue the status wording that replaces “ready for coder/unblocked.”\\n10. **Luce:** Confirm the machine-checkable verification evidence required for isolation, invoice reconciliation, classification reliability, and checkpoint/replay claims.\\n\\n## 10. Implementation Readiness Verdict\\n\\n### PARTIALLY BLOCKED\\n\\n**Can proceed:** Phase 0 append-only evidence store foundation, secret isolation skeleton, provider abstraction interfaces, execution-point ledger hooks, test harnesses, and non-semantic orchestration scaffolding.\\n\\n**Blocked:** framing scheduler and call-budget assertions; canonical ruling-keyed traceability; artifact schema binding and terminal pointer; G2 threshold behavior; semantic request deduplication/status replay; provider-family assignments; checkpoint/resume behavior; any OnDemand surface; multi-game slate topology.\\n\\nThis is not a correctness certification. No execution evidence was supplied, so all claims remain FACT/DERIVED/CONFLICT rather than VERIFIED.\\n\\n## 11. Recommended Next Handoff\\n\\nRoute this reconciliation to **Coda** for the status/ruling provenance decision, then to **Kimi and Chiave jointly** for the call-budget, G2, request lifecycle, provider registry, artifact schema, and slate-identity contracts. After those answers are recorded in the owned sources and the stale package is marked provenance-only, hand **Phase 0** to Implementation with Luce's acceptance evidence matrix and Talon's checkpoint/fallback operational contract.\\n\"},{\"url\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FHXcC5DKiLLIQROsHo5_0t9faw0GlVv5/view?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"EC8_Architecture_Specification_v1.0_Chiave_source.md\",\"id\":\"1FHXcC5DKiLLIQROsHo5_0t9faw0GlVv5\",\"mime_type\":\"text/markdown\",\"size\":\"20212\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:47:30.362Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:47:30.362Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":null,\"display_title\":\"EC8_Architecture_Specification_v1.0_Chiave_source.md\",\"display_url\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FHXcC5DKiLLIQROsHo5_0t9faw0GlVv5/view?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1EXzOuIyaLkTFB0pL6g5xXTWddHcbjN3O\"],\"shared\":true,\"content\":\"**Chiave — architecture documentation, hardened.**\\r\\n\\r\\nHere is the durable document. One design choice up front, made deliberately: **this spec references the methodology by version and pin rather than duplicating its content.** The framing schema JSON, the G4 test tables, the tier definitions — those live in Kimi's document, versioned. Duplicating them here would create exactly the two-write-path problem P7 exists to kill (and the stale-brief failure we just caught). What this document owns: the invariants, the interface contracts in checkable form, failure domains, security boundaries, instrumentation, the build plan, and the ruling register — including content the methodology has *not yet preserved*, which is the real backup value.\\r\\n\\r\\nTwo specifications in here are completions rather than consolidations — the L1 semantic-classification router and checkpoint/resume semantics — both flowing from standing rulings (G4 determinism, gates-as-checkpoints), exercised under normal design authority, flagged as such in the register. No new rulings were issued.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n# EC⁸ AI Convergence — Architecture Specification v1.0\\r\\n\\r\\n**Owner**: Chiave (Architecture) · **Status**: Post-gate, pre-build · **Companion**: Methodology v0.3.1 (Kimi, pending v0.3.2 record fixes)\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §0 — Document Authority\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is the canonical record of the architecture layer: structure, interfaces, failure behavior, instrumentation, and invariants. Methodology v0.3.1 governs process; this governs structure. Where this document's interface contracts and the methodology describe the same surface, they are the same ruling recorded twice — any divergence is a record error to be corrected at source, not adjudicated.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Governance**: versioned independently of the methodology; changes land here at adoption; every version diffs against the ruling register (§12). Build commits record actuals (chosen providers, infrastructure) in v1.1+ — this document is design-of-record until then.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Reference discipline**: methodology content is referenced by section and version, never copied. The normative framing schema text is methodology §3.1 @ v0.3.2 (enum fix pending); the G4 classification protocol is methodology §7.1 @ v0.3.1.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Backup set** (version-locked): `{this spec, methodology v0.3.x, prompts/01–09, governance changelog}` + manifest with SHA-256 per file. Post-build, evidence-store snapshots join the set. With these artifacts, the system is re-derivable.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §1 — System Invariants\\r\\n\\r\\nThe constitution. Violation of any invariant means the system is no longer what it claims to be, regardless of output quality.\\r\\n\\r\\n| ID | Invariant | Enforcement |\\r\\n|---|---|---|\\r\\n| **I1** | Analyst evidence package = current framing snapshot + requested evidence + request_status map. **Nothing else, ever.** | Single choke-point assembly function (IF-2); post-hoc package audit every run |\\r\\n| **I2** | No analyst context contains peer outputs, peer reasoning, peer gap requests, N, peer personas, or divergence measurement | Canaries, fingerprinting, package audit, isolation checks (EX-6) |\\r\\n| **I3** | Validation flow is forward-only: validation outputs feed normalizer and artifact; no path to analyst context exists | Topology constraint (VL-7); corrections reach analysts only as replacement evidence items |\\r\\n| **I4** | Replay-as-record: complete state capture; the stored artifact is canonical, re-execution verifies process, not results | Provenance chain (DA-3), evidence hashes, execution metadata (EX-5) |\\r\\n| **I5** | No validation layer is skipped; execution failure blocks, never bypasses | Layer scheduler (VL-4); G4 |\\r\\n| **I6** | Gates evaluate machine-checkable criteria only; no runtime judgment | G4 deterministic action table (VL-5); semantic classification is recorded and measured, never judged |\\r\\n| **I7** | Fail-transparent: partials, exclusions, and unfilled gaps are recorded, never smoothed | request_status, effective-N, integrity report are mandatory artifact sections |\\r\\n| **I8** | Every input shared by all analysts is a versioned constant, never per-run curation | Framing schema (IF-1) + disclosure set; store-vs-delivery separation (DA-4) |\\r\\n| **I9** | Provenance records model/prompt/parameter versions from execution metadata — never from configuration intent or org charts | Runtime capture at provider abstraction (EX-5) |\\r\\n| **I10** | Every model call and acquisition is metered at its execution point; the ledger is the only source of cost truth | Instrumentation at provider/acquisition layers (OB-3) |\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §2 — Interface Contracts\\r\\n\\r\\nThe four cross-seat interfaces. These are what other seats build against and what downstream binds to.\\r\\n\\r\\n### IF-1 — Framing Schema Interface\\r\\n- Output is a populated instance of framing schema **0.3-MLB** (methodology §3.1; v0.3.2 removes `OnDemand` from `run_context` — build commits to the fixed enum). Enumerated fields only; `null`-with-reason-code; no free-text fields; form-filler regime; **prior snapshots retained as record, never delivered** (M29).\\r\\n- **Verify**: schema validator rejects non-conforming output at G0; delivery log shows no analyst receiving more than one snapshot per run.\\r\\n\\r\\n### IF-2 — Evidence Package Interface\\r\\n- Contents per I1. `request_status`: `filled` | `unfilled` + reason (`unacquirable` | `source_unreliable` | `too_expensive` | `timeout` | `not_applicable`) | `pending`.\\r\\n- **Evidence identity**: (entity, attribute, snapshot-time) — each a distinct immutable store item. Time-variant data (lines, weather, injuries) never mutates a record; it creates a new one.\\r\\n- **Cumulative re-delivery** per run (M18/M30), with the disclosure line present in packaging.\\r\\n- **Market policy enforcement**: market-class evidence (movements, current lines at non-baseline times, public %, sharp indicators, volume) deliverable to Persona D only. Baseline line fields from the framing schema ride the shared baseline to all. Enforced role-keyed at the gap-request boundary (IF-3) and re-verified at the choke point.\\r\\n- **Assembly via a single choke-point function**; every package assembly logged and reconstructable post-hoc.\\r\\n- **Verify**: package audit reconstructs every delivered item as {schema field | fulfilled request | status entry}; any exception is a G6 failure.\\r\\n\\r\\n### IF-3 — Gap Request Interface\\r\\n- Structured form: entity, attribute, timeframe, granularity, data class. Lifecycle: `requested → filled | unfilled(reason) | pending`.\\r\\n- Access policy: data class `market` → Persona D only; all other classes → any persona.\\r\\n- **Verify**: malformed requests return `unfilled(malformed_request)`; market-class request from a non-D persona returns `access_denied` and emits a `market_data_request_rate` event (expected: 0% non-D).\\r\\n\\r\\n### IF-4 — Terminal Artifact Interface\\r\\n- Nine sections per methodology Stage 6. Effective-N fields: `configured_n, ran_n, included_n, excluded_n, exclusions[{analyst, reason, layer, class, test_id, detail}]`. Integrity report houses contamination results, gate outcomes, anomalies, session-continuity verification.\\r\\n- **Canonical terminal: SAP-PreGame** (scheduled scope only). SAP-Morning retained for trajectory, non-terminal. Artifacts immutable after G6. **Artifact schema versioned independently of methodology version; downstream binds to artifact schema version.**\\r\\n- **Verify**: G6 structural validation; immutability enforced at store level.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §3 — Execution Contracts\\r\\n\\r\\n| ID | Contract | Verify |\\r\\n|---|---|---|\\r\\n| **EX-1** | Separate execution context per analyst (process/container): no shared memory, filesystem, network namespace, or env vars. Per-persona prompts; unique sampling parameters per analyst per run | Isolation check per run; canary uniqueness |\\r\\n| **EX-2** | Heterogeneity: ≥3 model families across 5 analysts; L2 validator family ≠ analyst family **per pair**; L3 outside the analyst pool; L3 fallback pre-approved, configured, and exercised before pilot | Provider registry check at orchestration; fallback test (§11) |\\r\\n| **EX-3** | Continuity: intra-run = same session (Stage 1→3, two provider requests, one session); inter-run = fresh context; session transcript sealed into provenance at run end | Session-continuity verification in integrity report |\\r\\n| **EX-4** | Concurrency: analysts sequential or parallel, no ordering-dependent state; run IDs globally unique | Orchestration test |\\r\\n| **EX-5** | Version pinning: model versions, prompts, parameters pinned per run, captured from execution metadata (I9) | Provenance audit |\\r\\n| **EX-6** | Contamination detection: canary tokens unique per analyst per run; output fingerprinting; post-hoc pairwise sampling; all results → integrity report | Canary cross-appearance scan; fingerprint pass |\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §4 — Data Contracts\\r\\n\\r\\n| ID | Contract |\\r\\n|---|---|\\r\\n| **DA-1** | Evidence store: append-only, write-once, SHA-256 content-addressed; items immutable |\\r\\n| **DA-2** | Evidence identity per IF-2 — distinct immutable items, never mutation |\\r\\n| **DA-3** | Provenance tags: acquisition timestamp, source, reliability tier, run type, expiration. Artifact-level chain: analyst → claim → evidence ID → source → acquisition timestamp |\\r\\n| **DA-4** | **Store-vs-delivery separation**: acquisition — including all overnight pre-fetch — populates the store. Nothing enters a package except through IF-2. The store was always shared; the package never was (CR-1) |\\r\\n| **DA-5** | Store backup: store snapshots + the §0 backup set are the whole-store failure recovery mechanism |\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §5 — Validation Stack Contracts\\r\\n\\r\\n| ID | Contract |\\r\\n|---|---|\\r\\n| **VL-1** | Layer 1 is deterministic code: traceability, statistical verification, temporal, logical, entity checks. Machine-checks the mechanical G4 classes (CH-1/2/4/5, CO-1/2/4) |\\r\\n| **VL-2** | **L1 semantic-classification router** *(spec completion under CR-4)*: L1 FAILs requiring semantic classification (CO-3/5, UC-1–4) route to the L2 validator assigned to that analyst. Classification events logged per-analysis |\\r\\n| **VL-3** | Layer 2: pairwise family-difference vs. the analyst it validates; checks factual accuracy and reasoning soundness; never receives the analyst's raw confidence expression |\\r\\n| **VL-4** | Layer 3: outside the analyst pool; receives the analysis plus L1/L2 reports; red-team stance; pre-approved fallback provider (EX-2) |\\r\\n| **VL-5** | G4 action table is deterministic per methodology §7.1. Class assignment is recorded per-analysis; **classification reliability is a measured quantity** (Luce audit surface) |\\r\\n| **VL-6** | Retry protocol: validation report sealed; corrections delivered only as replacement evidence items with new provenance; re-run of Stage 3 in the same session; full re-validation; second FAIL (any class) → exclusion |\\r\\n| **VL-7** | Forward-only (I3): no data path from validation outputs to analyst context exists in the topology |\\r\\n| **VL-8** | Accounting: `ran_n` counts analyst slots; retries increment the cost ledger, not `ran_n` |\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §6 — Normalization Contracts\\r\\n\\r\\n| ID | Contract |\\r\\n|---|---|\\r\\n| **NO-1** | Neutral model; inputs exactly {self-assessment, evidence sufficiency score, validation state, validation flags}; never receives reasoning, selection, or peer outputs |\\r\\n| **NO-2** | Stateless, per-analyst invocation. No cross-analyst context, no batching |\\r\\n| **NO-3** | Input set is a versioned contract; changes shift tier comparability downstream → version-gated |\\r\\n| **NO-4** | Non-collapsing: final tier + justification + all four input components preserved separately in the artifact |\\r\\n| **NO-5** | Sufficiency score: deterministic code (formula owned by methodology); never a model call; replay-consistent |\\r\\n| **NO-6** | `Contradicted` is system-assignable only — it depends on validation state analysts cannot see. Tier enum versioned independently |\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §7 — Failure Domains\\r\\n\\r\\n| Domain | Blast radius | Behavior |\\r\\n|---|---|---|\\r\\n| Single analyst execution failure | One slot | Re-run or exclude; artifact continues; effective-N records it |\\r\\n| Correctable validation failure | One slot | Retry once (VL-6); second FAIL → exclude |\\r\\n| Critical hallucination / uncorrectable | One slot | Immediate exclusion, per-exclusion reason recorded |\\r\\n| L2 execution failure | That analyst's entry | Blocks entry; retry; never skipped (I5) |\\r\\n| L3 primary outage | Whole slate (if unmitigated) | Pre-approved fallback activates; fallback outage → entries blocked, never bypassed |\\r\\n| Normalizer failure | Whole artifact | Blocks artifact; retry; never bypassed |\\r\\n| Acquisition / source outage | Requesting analysts | Partial-data mode; `unfilled(reason)`; severe gaps flagged |\\r\\n| Orchestrator failure mid-run | The run | **Checkpoint at each gate; resume from last persisted gate state** *(spec completion under the standing gates-as-checkpoints ruling)* |\\r\\n| Overnight failure | Overnight only | Cheap redo at Morning (data-only run; no analyst state lost) |\\r\\n| Whole-store failure | The system | Run aborts; recovery = DA-5 backup/restore; **no artifact is ever preferable to a wrong artifact** |\\r\\n| Full pipeline failure | The slate | Reject; alert operators; honest absence recorded |\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §8 — Security & Trust Boundaries\\r\\n\\r\\n- **SE-1** The acquisition engine is the trust boundary. All external data enters here; scraped/social/news sources are untrusted text.\\r\\n- **SE-2** Structured-first: canonical structured evidence format; free-text passthrough minimized to genuinely unstructured classes.\\r\\n- **SE-3** Untrusted text is marked and sanitized at the boundary — containment over prevention.\\r\\n- **SE-4** Blast radius: poisoned evidence reaches only requesting analysts (per-analyst delivery is containment by construction); market data further scoped to Persona D.\\r\\n- **SE-5** Secrets managed from the first API call; per-component credential isolation; no credentials in prompts, logs, or artifacts.\\r\\n- **SE-6** Injection defense-in-depth: evidence packaged as data, not instructions (IF-2 format discipline); provenance and reliability tiers; validation stack as backstop.\\r\\n- **SE-7** On-demand trust boundary: deferred; revival conditions in §12/CR-2.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §9 — Observability & Cost Instrumentation\\r\\n\\r\\n- **OB-1** Ledger unit: provider-billable request + token counts (re-analysis requests carry full first-pass context — call counts alone understate; the ledger carries both).\\r\\n- **OB-2** Granularity: per component, run, analyst slot, layer, source.\\r\\n- **OB-3** Metered at execution point inside the provider abstraction; **retrofitting is forbidden** — that is how 645-vs-795 happens.\\r\\n- **OB-4** Happy-path scheduled budget: **53/slate** (1 + 26 + 26), ~795/day at 15 slates. Retries excluded from budget, included in ledger. **Budget is reference; ledger is truth.**\\r\\n- **OB-5** Metric emit-points: contamination rate, hallucination by layer, gate outcomes, framing completeness per snapshot, market request rate by persona, effective-N vs. configured, classification reliability.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §10 — Build Plan\\r\\n\\r\\n| Phase | Scope | Exit criteria |\\r\\n|---|---|---|\\r\\n| **0 — Foundation** | Evidence store (DA-1..5), secrets (SE-5), data-layer schema | Store round-trips evidence with identity + provenance; secrets isolated |\\r\\n| **1 — Orchestration** | Provider abstraction with ledger hooks and observability emit-points, same layer | Mocked end-to-end call path meters correctly (OB-3) |\\r\\n| **2 — Isolation & wiring** | EX-1..6, IF-2 choke point, VL stack, NO stack, L3 fallback | All contract Verify lines pass in integration |\\r\\n| **3 — Pilot** | §11 | Pilot acceptance criteria |\\r\\n\\r\\nScalability and failure-domain *testing* at scale are post-pilot — with the §11 seeded failures as the mandatory exception.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §11 — Pilot Design\\r\\n\\r\\n**Scope**: one MLB slate; scheduled cadence only (Overnight → Morning → Pre-Game); N=5; full validation; full measurement.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Seeded failure tests — mandatory, one per class:**\\r\\n(a) G4 correctable retry (VL-6 full protocol); (b) L3 primary→fallback switchover; (c) one source outage in partial-data mode; (d) one analyst exclusion, visible in effective-N.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Acceptance criteria — architectural, not signal:**\\r\\n1. Terminal artifact complete, nine sections, provenance chain **reconciles against provider invoices**.\\r\\n2. Every gate fired deterministically; outcomes in the integrity report.\\r\\n3. All four seeded failures behaved per the §7 table.\\r\\n4. Isolation verified: canaries unique per analyst per run; package audit clean (IF-2).\\r\\n5. Ledger measured vs. budget: variance reported with component breakdown.\\r\\n\\r\\n**The pilot is not**: a signal-quality test, a calibration test, or a scale test. Metrics accumulate from run one; conclusions come later, through Luce and methodology §9.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §12 — Gate Register\\r\\n\\r\\n| ID | Ruling | Provenance |\\r\\n|---|---|---|\\r\\n| **CR-1** | Evidence delivery is request-gated; pre-fetch populates the store only; package invariant per I1 | Chiave gate ruling, v0.3.1 |\\r\\n| **CR-2** | On-demand removed from pilot scope | Chiave recommendation → **Don scope ruling**. **Revival conditions preserved here**: G0 window bound (pre-first-pitch only); single canonical terminal per slate (most-recently-completed terminal, pointer semantics, all artifacts immutable); failure-domain independence from scheduled runs; trust boundary with authn/authz + quota enforcement + requester attribution in provenance; **plus two Don policy lines — who may trigger, and quota — required before build** |\\r\\n| **CR-3** | Cost ledger unit = provider-billable request + tokens; true figures 26/run, 53/slate, ~795/day | Chiave gate ruling, v0.3.1 |\\r\\n| **CR-4** | G4 deterministic; Kimi's §7.1 protocol accepted with recorded conditions (VL-2, VL-5, VL-8) | Chiave gate ruling + Kimi methodology decision |\\r\\n| **CR-5** | Framing schema 0.3-MLB approved; field content owned by methodology | Chiave gate ruling, v0.3.1 |\\r\\n\\r\\n**Gate reopen triggers**: framing schema major revision · artifact schema change · on-demand surface build · pilot contract violation · new cross-system dependency · store architecture change.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §13 — Ownership Boundary Map\\r\\n\\r\\n| Seat | Owns |\\r\\n|---|---|\\r\\n| **Don** | Strategy, scope, policy lines (on-demand trigger/quota when revived), thresholds, cost ceiling posture |\\r\\n| **Kimi** | Methodology, prompts, personas, G4 class semantics, tolerance refinements, sufficiency formula |\\r\\n| **Chiave** | This document: structure, interfaces, failure domains, instrumentation design, invariants |\\r\\n| **Talon** | Scheduling, monitoring cadence and response, source maintenance, L3 fallback coordination, cost reporting |\\r\\n| **Luce** | Verification: layer effectiveness, classification reliability, contamination-audit accuracy, calibration audit, post-pilot go/no-go |\\r\\n| **Governance** | Data usage policy, ToS compliance, regulatory |\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §14 — Traceability & Pending\\r\\n\\r\\n**Rulings → contracts**: CR-1 → IF-2/DA-4 · CR-2 → §12/SE-7 · CR-3 → OB-1..4 · CR-4 → VL-1..8 · CR-5 → IF-1.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Pending on methodology v0.3.2 (Kimi's six fixes)**: brief regeneration as a derived artifact · `OnDemand` enum removal · Stage 6 terminal line · ruling numbering + CR-2 content preservation · attribution of the on-demand removal · H1 version. **This document preserves CR-2's content independently, so the backup set is safe regardless of v0.3.2 timing.**\\r\\n\\r\\n**Spec completions issued under standing authority** (flagged, not new rulings): VL-2 (L1 router) · §7 checkpoint/resume semantics.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n**Boundary check**: I consolidated the architecture layer into its durable document — no new rulings beyond two flagged completions of standing ones. The backup set is defined and version-lockable. Still owed by others: Kimi's six record fixes (this document makes the backup safe without them, but the Coder handoff still needs the regenerated brief). My next move is Phase 0 design against §10. Save this as `EC8_Architecture_v1.0.md` alongside the methodology — the manifest binds them.\"},{\"url\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J89-TbW4N9H1t2lZvUICwKH0tDk-2LMB/view?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"EC8_NFL_METHODOLOGY_TO_BUILD_ANCHOR_COMMIT_2026-09-20.md\",\"id\":\"1J89-TbW4N9H1t2lZvUICwKH0tDk-2LMB\",\"mime_type\":\"text/markdown\",\"size\":\"6154\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-20T23:03:01.479Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-20T23:03:41.420Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":null,\"display_title\":\"EC8_NFL_METHODOLOGY_TO_BUILD_ANCHOR_COMMIT_2026-09-20.md\",\"display_url\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J89-TbW4N9H1t2lZvUICwKH0tDk-2LMB/view?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1IdFGWLiZWuVXnsxSRnVB7jV1ToLJy1xp\"],\"shared\":true,\"content\":\"# EC⁸ EDGE CREW QUANT — NFL METHODOLOGY → BUILD ANCHOR COMMIT\\n\\nDATE: 2026-09-20\\nSESSION: NFL Methodology / Data Sufficiency / Phase 2 Validation\\nSEAT: Coda — Strategic Advisor / Governance\\nCURRENT GATE: PAUSE after methodology/data discovery; prepare GCE architecture → Design & Build → implementation passage\\n\\n## ANCHOR PURPOSE\\n\\nFreeze the state reached in the NFL discovery thread so the main Edge Crew Quant methodology thread can review the methodology, reconcile prior evidence, and deliberately move the work through the GCE stack into an implementable technical specification.\\n\\nThis anchor DOES NOT authorize implementation.\\n\\n## FACT / GIVEN — PRESERVED STATE\\n\\n1. The cross-sport Edge Crew Quant spine remains the governing parent process. NFL work is sport-specific evidence and methodology under that spine.\\n2. NFL structural design established in session:\\n   PLAYER PROFILE → UNIT PROFILE → SIDE-OF-BALL PROFILE → TEAM PROFILE\\n   + explicit MATCHUP INTERACTIONS → NFL FAIR STATE.\\n3. First-pass NFL component/profile specification exists as:\\n   `EC8_EDGE_CREW_QUANT_NFL_COMPONENT_PROFILE_v0.1_2026-09-20.md`.\\n4. Variable discipline: target roughly 5–10 high-value variables per player/position/unit profile; additional analytics must earn inclusion.\\n5. Baseline remains separate from Don Delta.\\n6. Data acquisition was deliberately separated from methodology definition.\\n7. Data Hound preflight/reconciliation established the reusable chain:\\n   methodology → variable requirements → source/gap discovery → reconciliation → phased acquisition → validation.\\n8. Reconciled NFL surface reported:\\n   182 governing variables; 39 direct; 91 derivable; 16 proxy; 27 unavailable; 9 mixed.\\n   Phase allocation: P1 117; P2 36; P3 24; P4 5.\\n   These are Data Hound reconciliation results, not model weights.\\n9. Phase 1 free evidence acquisition was authorized; premium PFF/Odds acquisition was held.\\n10. Phase 2 weather join defect was repaired and independently VERIFIED by Luce:\\n    31 valid FORECAST rows; 241 legitimate NO_HORIZON; 0 invalid FORECAST; 16/16 package equivalence; no scoring/methodology change.\\n11. Remaining weather-related debt is separate:\\n    stale documentation refresh; Rams venue registry identity; upstream padded-abbreviation producer.\\n12. Historical `FOOTBALL_QUANT_v1.0-LOCK_2026-09-06` was discovered. Its relationship to the current component/profile methodology remains UNKNOWN until explicit reconciliation. It must not be silently merged or superseded.\\n\\n## PROPOSED — REUSABLE SPORT PROCESS\\n\\nSPORT-SPECIFIC METHODOLOGY\\n→ COMPONENT / PROFILE MODEL\\n→ FIRST-PASS VARIABLES\\n→ GOVERNING SPORT SPEC\\n→ DATA HOUND PREFLIGHT\\n→ REQUIREMENTS MATRIX\\n→ SOURCE INVENTORY\\n→ GAP REPORT\\n→ METHODOLOGY ↔ DATA RECONCILIATION\\n→ PHASED ACQUISITION PLAN\\n→ STORAGE PLAN\\n→ PHASE-SPECIFIC ACQUISITION\\n→ DATA VALIDATION\\n→ METHODOLOGY RECONCILIATION\\n→ NORMALIZATION / AGGREGATION DESIGN\\n→ WEIGHTING / FAIR STATE\\n→ MARKET COMPARISON / EDGE / EV\\n→ HISTORICAL + LIVE VALIDATION\\n→ PRODUCTION AUTHORITY\\n\\nThis process is PROPOSED cross-sport doctrine pending review in the main methodology thread.\\n\\n## PAUSE / DEBT REGISTER\\n\\n### D1 — Methodology review before architecture\\nThe NFL Component/Profile v0.1 is a working specification, not a final locked methodology. Review component completeness, variable acceptance, interaction semantics, uncertainty, aggregation boundaries, and anti-double-counting rules.\\n\\n### D2 — Prior locked Football Quant relationship\\nReview `FOOTBALL_QUANT_v1.0-LOCK_2026-09-06` as evidence/provenance. Determine whether it is:\\n- compatible prior implementation evidence,\\n- a predecessor methodology,\\n- an adapter/market engine downstream of the new methodology,\\n- or partially superseded.\\nNo silent merge.\\n\\n### D3 — 45 reconciliation-missing variables\\nDo not bulk restore or strip. Classify by methodological role and data value.\\n\\n### D4 — Architecture not yet ruled\\nDurable topology, interfaces, contracts, identity boundaries, provenance boundaries, failure domains, security boundaries, and storage/runtime relationships require Chiave only where materially architectural.\\n\\n### D5 — Design & Build not yet specified\\nKimi owns technical-stack methodology and Design & Build direction after governance framing and any required architecture ruling. Kimi may propose tools, components, schemas, workflows, prototypes, tests, and build packages.\\n\\n### D6 — Implementation runner not yet selected\\nKimi or GLM may later execute in Don's terminal, but executor selection does not grant methodology, architecture, or governance authority. MODEL != SEAT.\\n\\n### D7 — Operations and verification remain downstream\\nTalon owns deployment/sustained operations. Luce independently verifies evidence/execution. Neither implementation success nor verification creates methodology authority.\\n\\n## GCE PASSAGE FOR THE NEXT THREAD\\n\\nDON INTENT\\n→ CODA governance framing / methodology reconciliation\\n→ KIMI technical methodology\\n→ CHIAVE architecture when materially required\\n→ KIMI Design & Build specification\\n→ DON implementation authorization\\n→ terminal executor (Kimi/GLM or approved implementation agent)\\n→ TALON operations\\n→ LUCE verification\\n→ CODA reconciliation\\n→ DON decision\\n\\n## STOP RULE\\n\\nDo not code yet.\\nDo not ask an implementation model to “build the NFL system” from this anchor.\\nDo not assign weights.\\nDo not silently canonize the 182-variable reconciliation surface.\\nDo not merge the September 6 locked Football Quant artifact without a ruling.\\nDo not turn architecture into a choke point for ordinary technical choices.\\n\\nSTATUS: CHECKPOINT\\nCONFIDENCE: 99%\\nREASON: NFL discovery, data sufficiency, and validation have produced enough evidence to begin formal methodology review and build specification, but the methodology/architecture/design gates have not been completed.\\nNEXT GATE: Main Edge Crew Quant methodology review → governance decision package → Kimi methodology / Chiave architecture as required.\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: Yes — conduct the methodology review and decide what is ready to promote toward build.\\n\"},{\"url\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fSkGj6jpEHNWvFGJpi9XNSc5fr2A1WF1/view?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"K3_256K_SWARM_AUDITION_OUTPUT_2026-09-06.txt\",\"id\":\"1fSkGj6jpEHNWvFGJpi9XNSc5fr2A1WF1\",\"mime_type\":\"text/plain\",\"size\":\"56811\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:47:39.932Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:47:39.932Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":null,\"display_title\":\"K3_256K_SWARM_AUDITION_OUTPUT_2026-09-06.txt\",\"display_url\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fSkGj6jpEHNWvFGJpi9XNSc5fr2A1WF1/view?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1EXzOuIyaLkTFB0pL6g5xXTWddHcbjN3O\"],\"shared\":true,\"content\":\"Desktop\\\\GCE_DON\\\\GCE_EC8\\\\EC8_Methodology_Architecture_Reconciliation_v0.2\\r\\n   .md (supersedes the prior v0.1 pass). Deliverable below, in the required\\r\\n   order.\\r\\n\\r\\n   Sources: S1 = methodology v0.3.1 (handoff-zip copy) · S2 = methodology\\r\\n   v0.3.1 (methodology-zip copy — stale) · S3 = v0.3 (provenance) · S4 =\\r\\n   Architecture Specification v1.0 (the supplied .txt) · S5 =\\r\\n   HANDOFF_v0.3.1.md · S6 = prompts 01–09 both copies (handoff copies\\r\\n   verified newer).\\r\\n\\r\\n   ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\n   1. Executive Reconciliation\\r\\n\\r\\n   FACT — The accepted methodology (S1) and accepted architecture (S4) are\\r\\n   substantively aligned on every major contract. Isolation (I2/EX-1/EX-6),\\r\\n   request-gated evidence (CR-1/DA-4/IF-2), the package invariant, G4\\r\\n   determinism (14 tests, retry-once for Correctable only), forward-only\\r\\n   validation (I3/VL-7), normalization blindness (NO-1), effective-N,\\r\\n   terminal SAP-PreGame, and the 53-call/slate cost baseline all trace\\r\\n   cleanly in both directions. Zero Missing, zero substantive Conflicts in\\r\\n   requirements — every live conflict is a record defect (IDs, versions,\\r\\n   status claims), not a design defect.\\r\\n\\r\\n   Resolved since the v0.1 pass (it left these open; the newer S1 copy\\r\\n   answers them):\\r\\n\\r\\n   • §8.1 Overnight — Overnight = 1 model call (framing, Stage 0) +\\r\\n     deterministic API acquisition. No analysts. \\\"Data-only\\\" means \\\"no\\r\\n     analysts,\\\" not \\\"no model.\\\" Data acquisition and model execution are\\r\\n     separated in both documents.\\r\\n   • §8.2 Framing count — 3 calls/slate, explicit in S1 §9.1 (\\\"Morning and\\r\\n     Pre-Game each require a fresh framing snapshot\\\"). A fresh snapshot\\r\\n     does require a new model invocation — stated, not assumed.\\r\\n   • 53-call decomposition — 26/run = 1 framing + 25 pipeline; 53 = 3 +\\r\\n     10×5; ~795/day = 45 + 750. Internally consistent in S1 only.\\r\\n\\r\\n   Still live: ruling-ID drift (CR-2/CR-4 collisions); two divergent copies\\r\\n   both labeled v0.3.1; architecture's \\\"pending v0.3.2\\\" list partially\\r\\n   stale; G2 threshold valueless; artifact schema version never assigned;\\r\\n   handoff \\\"unblocked\\\" vs architecture \\\"post-gate, pre-build\\\" (narrowed to\\r\\n   record-fix-sized).\\r\\n\\r\\n   Verdict: PARTIALLY BLOCKED — narrower than v0.1. Phases 0–1 are READY\\r\\n   WITH NON-BLOCKING FIXES; five named surfaces are blocked, none requiring\\r\\n   redesign.\\r\\n\\r\\n   ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\n   2. System Intent Summary\\r\\n\\r\\n   • Objective: an independent analytical landscape of N=5 differentiated\\r\\n     AI analysts on one MLB game — selections, confidence tiers,\\r\\n     divergence, uncertainty — as a terminal artifact. Not recommendations,\\r\\n     consensus, or blended picks.\\r\\n   • Unit: a slate = one scheduled MLB game; multi-game days = independent\\r\\n     slates (S1 §2.1).\\r\\n   • Cadence: Overnight (T-24h→T-12h, store-population only, no analysts) →\\r\\n     Morning (T-12h→T-4h) → Pre-Game (T-90min, [T-120, T-30]). Scheduled\\r\\n     only; on-demand removed from pilot (Don #18 / S4 CR-2).\\r\\n   • Framing: form-filler model, fixed enumerated schema 0.3-MLB, zero\\r\\n     discretion, null+reason-code; fresh snapshot per run; prior snapshots\\r\\n     retained as record, never delivered.\\r\\n   • Topology: 5 personas (Situational, Form, Structural, Market, Micro),\\r\\n     ≥3 model families, unique prompts/sampling; coherence rule (know EC⁸\\r\\n     and their lane; don't know N, peers, or that divergence is measured).\\r\\n   • Independence: separate execution contexts; no peer\\r\\n     outputs/reasoning/gaps; canaries + fingerprinting per analyst per run\\r\\n     → integrity report.\\r\\n   • Evidence: analysts emit gaps → semantic dedup → acquisition →\\r\\n     provenance-tagged store; delivery is request-gated even though the\\r\\n     store is shared (CR-1/DA-4).\\r\\n   • Market isolation: market-class evidence → Persona D only, enforced\\r\\n     role-keyed at the gap boundary; framing-schema baseline lines ride the\\r\\n     shared baseline to all (S4 IF-2 explicit).\\r\\n   • Validation: L1 deterministic (no model), L2 different-architecture per\\r\\n     pair (no raw confidence), L3 outside-pool red-team with pre-approved\\r\\n     fallback; forward-only; no layer skippable.\\r\\n   • G4: FAILs classified by observable tests — Critical Hallucination\\r\\n     (CH-1..5) / Uncorrectable (UC-1..4) → immediate exclusion; Correctable\\r\\n     (CO-1..5) → one same-session retry, second FAIL → exclusion.\\r\\n   • Normalization: neutral model, exactly 4 inputs, blind to\\r\\n     reasoning/selection/peers; tiers\\r\\n     Conviction/Lean/Tentative/Pass/Contradicted; Pass sacred; Contradicted\\r\\n     system-assignable.\\r\\n   • Artifacts: nine-section SAP per run; SAP-Morning non-terminal;\\r\\n     SAP-PreGame terminal, immutable after G6.\\r\\n   • Cost: unit = provider-billable request + tokens; budget reference\\r\\n     53/slate, ledger is sole truth; no cap (Don #8).\\r\\n   • Failure/replay: blocks never bypass; checkpoint/resume at gates;\\r\\n     replay-as-record; \\\"no artifact is ever preferable to a wrong\\r\\n     artifact.\\\"\\r\\n   • Pilot: one MLB slate topology, N=5, four mandatory seeded failure\\r\\n     tests; acceptance is architectural (gates fired, isolation verified,\\r\\n     ledger reconciles to invoices), not signal quality.\\r\\n\\r\\n   ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\n   3. Methodology → Architecture Traceability Matrix\\r\\n\\r\\n   ┌───────────────┬─────────┬───────────┬─────────┬──────────────────────┐\\r\\n   │ Methodology   │ Source  │ Architect │ Status  │ Notes              