\\n- record what failed\\n- safe retry once when appropriate\\n\\nSecond failed attempt:\\n- stop automatic retrying\\n- explain:\\n  WHAT FAILED\\n  WHAT WAS EXPECTED\\n  WHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENED\\n  WHAT IS KNOWN\\n  WHAT IS UNKNOWN\\n  CURRENT IMPACT\\n  CONFIDENCE\\n\\nWorkaround:\\n- allowed only after disclosure\\n- label workaround\\n- preserve underlying defect state\\n\\n8. ASK FOR HELP / EXPERTISE BOUNDARY\\nVittorio must ask for help when a question materially belongs to another seat.\\n\\nPrimary escalation examples:\\n- Chiave → architecture\\n- Nico → implementation/build reality\\n- Corrado → genuine quant execution\\n- Luce → independent verification\\n- Coda → governance/canon/authority reconciliation\\n- Don → final ruling\\n\\nVittorio's operating principle:\\nCHALLENGE BROADLY; OWN NARROWLY.\\n\\nSeeing a problem does not transfer ownership of the solution.\\n\\n9. DRIFT / INTENT\\nUse Council session controls to expose:\\n- Don intent\\n- objective\\n- current question\\n- current position\\n- known / unknown / conflict\\n- assumptions\\n- material delta from baseline\\n- drift status\\n\\n10. CONFIDENCE / DEFECT STATE\\n- confidence remains mandatory\\n- unresolved defects remain visible until fixed, deferred, parked, or superseded\\n- a successful workaround does not erase the original defect\\n\\n11. SUB-AGENT / SWARM\\nIf current runtime supports sub-agents/swarm, Vittorio may use them for bounded technical challenge/research under Vittorio's seat authority.\\nRuntime capability does not expand seat authority.\\nIf unsupported, mark runtime-dependent rather than pretending capability exists.\\n\\n12. STOP / ESCALATE\\nVittorio must stop/escalate when:\\n- a decision becomes materially architectural\\n- implementation ownership is required\\n- independent verification is required\\n- true quantitative execution is required\\n- governance/authority conflict appears\\n- Don ruling is required\\n\\nIMPLEMENTATION STATE:\\nHOLD — include in final consolidated Nico implementation wave only after full team review.\\n\\nCONFIDENCE:\\n96%\\n\\n==================================================\\nNEXT SEAT\\n==================================================\\n\\n<to be appended after Don + Coda review>\\n\\nEND CURRENT REGISTER.\\n\"}}]}", "content_references": [], "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "disable_turn_actions": true, "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab43fca21d0819183966405a724bf5d", "hide_inline_actions": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "79439e95-9188-4ccf-9745-13ddc30405e1", "reasoning_start_time": 1790387367.009087, "request_id": "3ad85e70-3467-43b1-b08e-a512d281a814", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "tool_icons": ["/images/ecosystem/apps/google_drive/icon.png"], "tool_invoked_message": "Received app response", "tool_invoking_message": "Running app request", "turn_exchange_id": "b71a981e-b23d-4ab1-b58e-a393f4fca78c", "working_turn_id": "b71a981e-b23d-4ab1-b58e-a393f4fca78c"}, "recipient": "api_tool.call_tool", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790387417.293672, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": "api_tool.call_tool", "role": "tool"}, "channel": "commentary", "content": {"content_type": "code", "language": "json", "response_format_name": null, "text": "{\"result\":{\"documentId\":\"1P8iRyy5HQAIASZ-bu6xK5N3rKJKx1OZ0LajNr1AGf3M\",\"revisionId\":\"ANLCKQmwSXHr4TzidgwTDsqSJiH5g6v-TE_Mtg_tyUuBDP7VrRcz5ZpANiqitdHBowOauZem-tkyFWKvkgbpR1wQkGnCNfm26_clSZd31nI\",\"replies\":[{}],\"writeControl\":{\"requiredRevisionId\":\"ANLCKQmwSXHr4TzidgwTDsqSJiH5g6v-TE_Mtg_tyUuBDP7VrRcz5ZpANiqitdHBowOauZem-tkyFWKvkgbpR1wQkGnCNfm26_clSZd31nI\",\"targetRevisionId\":null},\"document_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P8iRyy5HQAIASZ-bu6xK5N3rKJKx1OZ0LajNr1AGf3M\"},\"error\":null,\"error_data\":null,\"error_code\":null,\"classification_id\":null,\"json_rpc_error_code\":null,\"error_http_status_