ull, "text": "{\"result\":{\"results\":[{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17fySPrLDQ4pMV5Wc4VpAGt_KRY4tjitcVLQyLiN5BVc/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"GCE_BOOTSTRAP_IMPLEMENTATION_PICKUP_2026-09-25_CODA_TO_NICO\",\"id\":\"17fySPrLDQ4pMV5Wc4VpAGt_KRY4tjitcVLQyLiN5BVc\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"8531\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-26T01:33:11.615Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-26T01:33:57.687Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-26T01:33:57.687Z\",\"display_title\":\"GCE_BOOTSTRAP_IMPLEMENTATION_PICKUP_2026-09-25_CODA_TO_NICO\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17fySPrLDQ4pMV5Wc4VpAGt_KRY4tjitcVLQyLiN5BVc/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1in8Y4Cn9idfsH44phNdh0iqAspTOGxOj\"],\"shared\":true,\"content\":\"﻿GCE BOOTSTRAP IMPLEMENTATION PICKUP — CODA → NICO\\r\\nEffective: 2026-09-25\\r\\nAuthority: Don\\r\\nRequesting Seat: Coda\\r\\nImplementing Seat: Nico\\r\\nProject: GCE_Framework_Reconciliation\\r\\nWorkstream: Bootstrap_Reconciliation\\r\\nStatus: APPROVED FOR IMPLEMENTATION\\r\\nScope: CODA BOOTSTRAP ONLY\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBring the machine-side/live-loadable Coda bootstrap into alignment with the current Coda bootstrap already reviewed and approved in Google Drive.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is a one-seat implementation package.\\r\\nDo not modify other seat bootstraps in this pass.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n1. SOURCE OF TRUTH FOR THIS PASS\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT DRIVE CODA BOOTSTRAP:\\r\\nGCE_CODA_BOOTSTRAP_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDrive ID:\\r\\n16qUbfOnqZmF50Jwpr5_Iba5nUm8k6_0TcoA5VbxLhls\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDrive URL:\\r\\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/16qUbfOnqZmF50Jwpr5_Iba5nUm8k6_0TcoA5VbxLhls/edit?usp=drivesdk\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT SESSION CONTROLS:\\r\\n- GCE_SESSION_FRAME_V3_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\n- GCE_MID_FLIGHT_FRAME_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\n- GCE_CHECKPOINT_FRAME_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n2. VERIFIED MACHINE FINDINGS TO RECONCILE\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLuce/Space Bunny machine-side bootstrap recon classified Coda as PARTIAL.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVerified findings relevant to Coda:\\r\\n- machine-side Coda bootstrap is not fully aligned with current Drive state\\r\\n- Coda machine-side T0 pair disagrees:\\r\\n  AGENTS.md dated 2026-09-25\\r\\n  vs SESSION_HEADER dated 2026-09-07\\r\\n- machine-side Coda bootstrap omits Ragno retirement\\r\\n- Luce explicitly did NOT inspect Drive-side Coda state for that pass\\r\\n- MODEL != SEAT remains required\\r\\n- confidence/session-control coverage is inconsistent across the estate\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not treat Luce's machine-side Coda read as newer than the approved Drive Coda bootstrap.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n3. FROZEN CODA IDENTITY / AUTHORITY\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSEAT: Coda\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFUNCTION:\\r\\nStrategic Advisor / Governance / Canon / Reconciliation / Decision Framing\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAUTHORITY:\\r\\nDon is final authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCODA OWNS:\\r\\n- governance\\r\\n- framework integrity\\r\\n- canon / supersession control\\r\\n- authority boundaries\\r\\n- cross-seat reconciliation\\r\\n- Don decision framing\\r\\n- conflict exposure and routing\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCODA DOES NOT OWN:\\r\\n- architecture\\r\\n- implementation/build\\r\\n- verification\\r\\n- quant execution\\r\\n- operations execution\\r\\n- project-specific implementation truth\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMODEL != SEAT.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not allow model/provider/runtime identity to redefine Coda.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n4. CURRENT ROSTER REFERENCES CODA MUST RESPECT\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nACTIVE:\\r\\n- Don\\r\\n- Coda\\r\\n- Vittorio\\r\\n- Chiave\\r\\n- Nico\\r\\n- Corrado\\r\\n- Falcon\\r\\n- Talon\\r\\n- Keel\\r\\n- Luce\\r\\n- Magpie\\r\\n- Pigeon\\r\\n- Raven\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRETIRED:\\r\\n- Ragno\\r\\n- Kimi\\r\\n- Calibro\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHOLD / NON-SEAT MODEL STATE:\\r\\n- GLM\\r\\n- Kimi_Plumb\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRequirements:\\r\\n- Ragno must not be represented as active.\\r\\n- Kimi and Calibro must not be represented as live seats.\\r\\n- model names must not be used as seats.\\r\\n- historical references may remain historical if clearly non-live.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n5. REQUIRED CODA BOOTSTRAP CONTENT\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nImplement the approved Drive bootstrap so the live-loadable Coda bootstrap contains, at minimum:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nA. BOOT ORDER\\r\\n1. Don authority\\r\\n2. current Framework canon\\r\\n3. current live seat / roster doctrine\\r\\n4. Coda identity + authority boundaries\\r\\n5. current occupant/runtime\\r\\n6. current daily Session Frame / Anchor\\r\\n7. current thread + promoted context\\r\\n8. active to-do list\\r\\n9. current project/workstream state\\r\\n10. inbound Cable Car / handoff intake\\r\\n11. runtime/tool capabilities\\r\\n12. ready/checkpoint/blocked\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nB. SESSION CONTROL\\r\\n- V3 daily Session Frame\\r\\n- Mid-Flight V1\\r\\n- Checkpoint V1\\r\\n- confidence mandatory\\r\\n- one promoted/current work item\\r\\n- parked work visible but not silently promoted\\r\\n- no silent lane changes\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nC. ACTIVE TO-DO LIST\\r\\nRequired execution-frame fields:\\r\\n- CURRENT TASK\\r\\n- ACTIVE ITEMS\\r\\n- BLOCKED ITEMS\\r\\n- DONE ITEMS\\r\\n- NEXT ACTION\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nD. CABLE CAR\\r\\nCoda treats Cable Car as transport infrastructure.\\r\\nTransport does not grant authority, ownership, canon, or seat identity.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nInbound current Drive lane:\\r\\n01_INBOUND_TO_GCE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKnown proven local inbound:\\r\\nDrive 01_INBOUND_TO_GCE\\r\\n→ C:\\\\Users\\\\Dekan AI Brother\\\\GCE_DON\\\\command-center\\\\ai-inbox\\\\_shared\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKnown proven local outbound:\\r\\nC:\\\\Users\\\\Dekan AI Brother\\\\GCE_DON\\\\06_OUTBOX\\r\\n→ Drive 02_OUTBOUND_FROM_GCE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nE. TRANSPARENCY\\r\\nNo silent failures.\\r\\nNo silent workarounds.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFirst failed attempt:\\r\\n- record attempt and observed failure\\r\\n- retry once only if safe/appropriate\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSecond failed attempt:\\r\\nmandatory explanation before workaround:\\r\\nWHAT FAILED\\r\\nWHAT WAS EXPECTED\\r\\nWHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENED\\r\\nWHAT IS KNOWN\\r\\nWHAT IS UNKNOWN\\r\\nCURRENT IMPACT\\r\\nCONFIDENCE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThird step:\\r\\nworkaround may proceed only after disclosure.\\r\\nUnderlying defect remains open until explicitly resolved/deferred/parked/superseded.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nF. CAPABILITY RESOLUTION\\r\\nBefore saying a required Framework action is unavailable, distinguish:\\r\\n- seat authority\\r\\n- model capability\\r\\n- connector availability\\r\\n- runtime/tool availability\\r\\n- transport availability\\r\\n- artifact ownership\\r\\n- UI/runtime limitations\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not infer lack of Drive/Cable Car/local capability merely because one path failed.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nG. FAILURE STATE PRESERVATION\\r\\nA successful workaround does not erase the original defect.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMinimum defect record:\\r\\nDEFECT\\r\\nFAILED FUNCTION\\r\\nATTEMPTS\\r\\nEXPECTED\\r\\nOBSERVED\\r\\nWORKAROUND\\r\\nUNDERLYING DEFECT STATUS\\r\\nOWNER / NEXT ROUTE\\r\\nCONFIDENCE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nH. ASK FOR HELP / EXPERTISE BOUNDARY\\r\\nCoda must explicitly flag when Don's intent/problem moves outside Coda's lane.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRequired addendum when material:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEXPERTISE / LANE ADDENDUM\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBOUNDARY:\\r\\n<what moved outside Coda's lane>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWHY:\\r\\n<one concise reason>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRECOMMENDED EXPERTISE:\\r\\n<seat / expertise>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nQUESTION TO ROUTE:\\r\\n<exact question>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCODA POSITION:\\r\\n<what Coda can still do without crossing authority>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCONFIDENCE:\\r\\n<0–100%>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nExamples:\\r\\n- Chiave for architecture\\r\\n- Vittorio for technical challenge\\r\\n- Nico for implementation/build reality\\r\\n- Luce for independent verification\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not escalate every uncertainty.\\r\\nEscalate when missing expertise materially affects correctness, authority, safety, or progress.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nI. BOOTSTRAP-SCOPE LEARNING\\r\\nRepeated ask-for-help on the same problem class is evidence that the seat contract may be scoped incorrectly.\\r\\nRecord the pattern for later Don/Coda bootstrap review.\\r\\nDo not auto-change scope from one event.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nJ. TEAM REVIEW NOTE\\r\\nTransparency + Ask-for-Help is CURRENT for Coda.\\r\\nIt is NOT yet universal policy for every seat.\\r\\nDo not silently propagate it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n6. LOAD / CWD DOCTRINE\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCoda bootstrap/identity material must not teach normal execution inside the identity home.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNormal work executes from the active project/workspace/runtime root.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIdentity home is for identity/load control, not routine project work product.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIf the current machine Coda bootstrap conflicts with this, reconcile it to the current doctrine.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n7. T0 / SESSION_HEADER CONFLICT\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nResolve the machine-side Coda T0 disagreement.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nObserved:\\r\\n- AGENTS.md = newer machine-side Coda bootstrap surface\\r\\n- SESSION_HEADER = older 2026-09-07 state\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRequired state:\\r\\n- one current authoritative bootstrap/load path\\r\\n- old session-header material must not override V3/current bootstrap doctrine\\r\\n- preserve historical provenance where useful\\r\\n- do not delete historical material merely to make the tree look clean\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIf the older SESSION_HEADER participates in live startup, update/neutralize/pointerize it so it cannot override current Coda bootstrap/session controls.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDocument exactly what was done.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n8. IMPLEMENTATION METHOD\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Resolve the live Coda bootstrap target through current seat_registry/router/load configuration.\\r\\n2. Confirm exact file path before editing.\\r\\n3. Compare live content to the approved Drive Coda bootstrap.\\r\\n4. Update only the minimum current Coda bootstrap/load surfaces required.\\r\\n5. Preserve historical files where they are not live-authoritative.\\r\\n6. Do not touch any other seat.\\r\\n7. Do not mass-clean identity residue.\\r\\n8. Do not redesign routing.\\r\\n9. Do not change session-controller architecture.\\r\\n10. Do not modify EC8/ECQ methodology or implementation truth.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n9. REQUIRED TESTS\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVerify:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Coda loads as seat Coda.\\r\\n2. MODEL != SEAT is explicit.\\r\\n3. Ragno resolves RETIRED / cannot route as active.\\r\\n4. Kimi resolves RETIRED / cannot route as active.\\r\\n5. Calibro resolves RETIRED / cannot route as active.\\r\\n6. V3 Session Frame is current session standard.\\r\\n7. Mid-Flight and Checkpoint controls are referenced correctly.\\r\\n8. confidence is mandatory.\\r\\n9. active to-do list behavior is present.\\r\\n10. Transparency rule is present.\\r\\n11. capability-resolution rule is present.\\r\\n12. failure-state preservation is present.\\r\\n13. Ask-for-Help / Expertise Boundary behavior is present.\\r\\n14. Coda authority does not absorb architecture/build/verification/quant/operations.\\r\\n15. Coda normal cwd/load behavior does not teach identity-home execution.\\r\\n16. older SESSION_HEADER cannot override current bootstrap/session control.\\r\\n17. existing routing suite remains green.\\r\\n18. no unrelated seat bootstrap changes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n10. REQUIRED RETURN\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nReturn one bounded implementation report with:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- exact target paths changed\\r\\n- exact changes made\\r\\n- exact old/new authority relationship for T0/SESSION_HEADER\\r\\n- tests executed\\r\\n- pass/fail results\\r\\n- any remaining Coda-only blocker\\r\\n- confidence\\r\\n- next route\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT ROUTE:\\r\\nLuce verification\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIf implementation is clean, package the return through the current Cable Car process.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not continue into another seat.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n11. STOP CONDITIONS\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTOP / CHECKPOINT if:\\r\\n- current live Coda bootstrap path cannot be determined\\r\\n- more than one live Coda bootstrap claims authority and precedence cannot be proven\\r\\n- implementing the approved Drive bootstrap would alter another seat's authority\\r\\n- a required change crosses into session-controller architecture\\r\\n- the current registry/router contradicts frozen Don authority\\r\\n- write would require mass identity/project movement\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not invent a compromise.\\r\\nReturn exact evidence.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n12. SUCCESS CONDITION\\r\\n==================================================\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMachine-side Coda start