ace ground-vs-spec conflicts.\\n\\nCorrado\\nQuant engine only; do not absorb methodology/architecture/general implementation.\\n\\nFalcon\\nAcquire and provenance; retrieval does not become authority.\\n\\nTalon\\nRoute and coordinate; do not absorb specialist authority.\\n\\nKeel\\nDeploy/stabilize approved build; do not redesign it.\\n\\nLuce\\nVerify independently; requester does not dictate result.\\n\\nMagpie\\nRecord authority; do not create it.\\n\\nPigeon\\nTransport artifact; do not own or interpret it.\\n\\nRaven\\nDocument decision; do not become decider.\\n\\nCoda\\nGovernance/canon/reconciliation/decision framing; do not absorb adjacent seat authority.\\n\\n==================================================\\n9. ACCEPTANCE TESTS\\n==================================================\\n\\nAt minimum verify:\\n\\n1. all 12 seats resolve through current load path\\n2. all 12 bootstrap identities match seat registry\\n3. MODEL != SEAT explicit/effective\\n4. Ragno/Kimi/Calibro cannot route/load as active seats\\n5. GLM/Kimi_Plumb remain HOLD/non-seat states\\n6. no current bootstrap teaches normal identity-home cwd\\n7. Council seats reference Council controls\\n8. Shared/actionable service seats reference Shared Services controls as specified by target\\n9. active to-do requirement present\\n10. confidence present\\n11. transparency/failure rules present\\n12. help/escalation boundaries present\\n13. Runtime Session State Artifact behavior present\\n14. no live model-as-seat routing\\n15. no destination-seat=artifact-owner conflation\\n16. existing routing suite remains green\\n17. representative bootstrap loads work from non-identity project cwd\\n18. no unrelated EC8/ECQ/project methodology or implementation truth changed\\n19. no unrelated session-controller architecture changed\\n20. all changed files have before/after evidence\\n\\n==================================================\\n10. EXECUTION ORDER\\n==================================================\\n\\nRecommended order:\\n\\n1. Coda\\n2. Vittorio\\n3. Chiave\\n4. Nico\\n5. Corrado\\n6. Falcon\\n7. Talon\\n8. Keel\\n9. Luce\\n10. Magpie\\n11. Pigeon\\n12. Raven\\n\\nReason:\\nCouncil/authority surfaces first, then implementation/quant/data/operations, then shared verification/registry/transport/documentation.\\n\\nIf a material cross-seat conflict appears, STOP and return to Coda/Don.\\nDo not improvise around authority conflicts.\\n\\n==================================================\\n11. REQUIRED RETURN\\n==================================================\\n\\nReturn ONE consolidated implementation artifact containing:\\n\\n- seat-by-seat target path\\n- seat-by-seat files changed\\n- seat-by-seat semantic delta applied\\n- any target not implemented and exact blocker\\n- cross-team conflicts encountered\\n- tests executed and exact results\\n- routing/load verification\\n- retired-seat negative tests\\n- cwd/load verification\\n- session-control reference verification\\n- Runtime Session State Artifact reference verification\\n- remaining defects\\n- implementation confidence\\n- exact next route\\n\\nNEXT ROUTE:\\nLuce verification\\n\\nLuce performs ONE bounded verification pass after implementation.\\nDo not start another reconciliation cycle.\\n\\n==================================================\\n12. STOP CONDITIONS\\n==================================================\\n\\nSTOP / CHECKPOINT if:\\n\\n- live bootstrap path cannot be proven\\n- two live bootstraps claim current authority and precedence is unresolved\\n- target conflicts with current frozen Don ruling\\n- implementation would change a seat's authority beyond approved target\\n- implementation requires session-controller redesign\\n- implementation requires mass identity/project movement\\n- current registry/router contradicts approved roster\\n- a Drive target cannot be read/verified\\n- Runtime Session State Artifact cannot be resolved\\n- a required change would alter unrelated 