8. Do not redesign routing/session-controller/Cable Car architecture.\\n9. Do not widen any seat's authority.\\n10. Do not reinterpret seat class from the session-control family reference.\\n11. Verify after each seat, then run the full acceptance suite at the end.\\n\\n==================================================\\n6. REQUIRED CROSS-TEAM CONTROLS\\n==================================================\\n\\nEvery implemented bootstrap must correctly preserve:\\n\\n- stable seat identity\\n- MODEL != SEAT\\n- current frozen roster\\n- retired-seat fail-closed behavior\\n- correct role/authority boundaries\\n- current class-appropriate session-control references\\n- explicit active to-do state\\n- Runtime Session State Artifact behavior at lifecycle boundaries\\n- transparency / no silent failure\\n- no silent workaround\\n- failure-state preservation\\n- capability resolution before unavailable claims\\n- Ask for Help / expertise-boundary behavior\\n- project/workspace cwd doctrine; identity home is load-control only\\n- confidence\\n- handoff/Cable Car semantics\\n- destination seat != artifact owner\\n- no false PUBLISHED/RECEIVED claims\\n- sub-agent/swarm use only when runtime-supported and still bounded by seat authority\\n\\n==================================================\\n7. KNOWN MACHINE-SIDE ITEMS TO HANDLE\\n==================================================\\n\\nFrom Luce/Space Bunny recon:\\n\\n- 12/12 loadable seat bootstraps were read in full.\\n- classifications:\\n  CURRENT: Nico, Corrado, Keel, Raven\\n  PARTIAL: Coda, Talon, Luce\\n  STALE: Vittorio, Magpie, Pigeon\\n  CONFLICTED: Falcon, Chiave\\n- Coda T0 AGENTS vs older SESSION_HEADER conflict.\\n- machine-side Coda omits Ragno retirement.\\n- Falcon contains internal contradiction against newer D-5 banner.\\n- Luce/Talon/Falcon identity homes contain project work product; do not mass-move in this package.\\n- Magpie and Pigeon lack newer D-5 banner/router pointer.\\n- prior D-1..D-5 patch introduced text corruption in multiple bootstraps; repair only where current target proves intended text.\\n- F-18 competing DeepSeek seat-impersonating AGENTS tree exists in operative EC8 surface. Treat as implementation-critical competing-bootstrap defect, but do not delete historical/project content blindly.\\n- F-19 gate wiring is LOW-MED and outside this bootstrap package unless required to prove bootstrap load/routing acceptance.\\n\\n==================================================\\n8. SEAT-SPECIFIC NON-NEGOTIABLES\\n==================================================\\n\\nVittorio\\nChallenge broadly; own narrowly.\\n\\nChiave\\nArchitect only when architecture is material.\\n\\nNico\\nBuild accepted package; surface ground-vs-spec conflicts.\\n\\nCorrado\\nQuant engine only; do not absorb methodology/architecture/general implementation.\\n\\nFalcon\\nAcquire and provenance; retrieval does not become authority.\\n\\nTalon\\nRoute and coordinate; do not absorb specialist authority.\\n\\nKeel\\nDeploy/stabilize approved build; do not redesign it.\\n\\nLuce\\nVerify independently; requester does not dictate result.\\n\\nMagpie\\nRecord authority; do not create it.\\n\\nPigeon\\nTransport artifact; do not own or interpret it.\\n\\nRaven\\nDocument decision; do not become decider.\\n\\nCoda\\nGovernance/canon/reconciliation/decision framing; do not absorb adjacent seat authority.\\n\\n==================================================\\n9. ACCEPTANCE TESTS\\n==================================================\\n\\nAt minimum verify:\\n\\n1. all 12 seats resolve through current load path\\n2. all 12 bootstrap identities match seat registry\\n3. MODEL != SEAT explicit/effective\\n4. Ragno/Kimi/Calibro cannot route/load as active seats\\n5. GLM/Kimi_Plumb remain HOLD/non-seat states\\n6. no current bootstrap teaches normal identity-home cwd\\n7. Council seats reference Council controls\\n8. Shared/actionable service seats reference Shared Services controls as specified by target\\n9. active to-do requirement present\\n10. confidence present\\n11. transparency/failure rules present\\n12. help/escalation boundaries present\\n13. Runtime Session State Artifact behavior present\\n14. no live model-as-seat routing\\n15. no destination-seat=artifact-owner conflation\\n16. existing routing suite remains green\\n17. representative bootstrap loads work from non-identity project cwd\\n18. no unrelated EC8/ECQ/project methodology or implementation truth changed\\n19. no unrelated session-controller architecture changed\\n20. all changed files have before/after evidence\\n\\n==================================================\\n10. EXECUTION ORDER\\n==================================================\\n\\nRecommended order:\\n\\n1. Coda\\n2. Vittorio\\n3. Chiave\\n4. Nico\\n5. Corrado\\n6. Falcon\\n7. Talon\\n8. Keel\\n9. Luce\\n10. Magpie\\n11. Pigeon\\n12. Raven\\n\\nReason:\\nCouncil/authority surfaces first, then implementation/quant/data/operations, then shared verification/registry/transport/documentation.\\n\\nIf a material cross-seat conflict appears, STOP and return to Coda/Don.\\nDo not improvise around authority conflicts.\\n\\n==================================================\\n11. REQUIRED RETURN\\n==================================================\\n\\nReturn ONE consolidated implementation artifact containing:\\n\\n- seat-by-seat target path\\n- seat-by-seat files changed\\n- seat-by-seat semantic delta applied\\n- any target not implemented and exact blocker\\n- cross-team conflicts encountered\\n- tests executed and exact results\\n- routing/load verification\\n- retired-seat negative tests\\n- cwd/load verification\\n- session-control reference verification\\n- Runtime Session State Artifact reference verification\\n- remaining defects\\n- implementation confidence\\n- exact next route\\n\\nNEXT ROUTE:\\nLuce verification\\n\\nLuce performs ONE bounded verification pass after implementation.\\nDo not start another reconciliation cycle.\\n\\n==================================================\\n12. STOP CONDITIONS\\n==================================================\\n\\nSTOP / CHECKPOINT if:\\n\\n- live bootstrap path cannot be proven\\n- two live bootstraps claim current authority and precedence is unresolved\\n- target conflicts with current frozen Don ruling\\n- implementation would change a seat's authority beyond approved target\\n- implementation requires session-controller redesign\\n- implementation requires mass identity/project movement\\n- current registry/router contradicts approved roster\\n- a Drive target cannot be read/verified\\n- Runtime Session State Artifact cannot be resolved\\n- a required change would alter unrelated project implementation truth\\n\\n==================================================\\n13. SUCCESS CONDITION\\n==================================================\\n\\nAll 12 loadable seats align with the approved target estate;\\ncurrent session controls are correctly referenced;\\ncurrent roster/authority is preserved;\\nknown stale/conflicted bootstrap defects are reconciled;\\ntests remain green;\\nand one consolidated return is ready for Luce verification.\\n\\nEND PACKAGE.\\n\"}}]}", "content_references": [], "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "disable_turn_actions": true, "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab43fca21d0819183966405a724bf5d", "hide_inline_actions": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "e7012e10-cd75-4b88-b613-1fe8ffef6741", "reasoning_start_time": 1790388289.2554357, "request_id": "28f3421a-ea8c-4ff1-a12e-62f38def625b", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "tool_icons": ["/images/ecosystem/apps/google_drive/icon.png"], "tool_invoked_message": "Received app response", "tool_invoking_message": "Running app request", "turn_exchange_id": "203e83f4-0a9c-471f-8b13-28e5d1a653dc", "working_turn_id": "203e83f4-0a9c-471f-8b13-28e5d1a653dc"}, "recipient":