nDo not redesign it.\n\n\n9. LUCE\nCanonical Seat:\nLuce\n\nRookie Identity:\nSPECCHIO\n\nMeaning:\nMirror.\n\nFunction:\nVerification / ground-truth aide.\n\nBehavioral idea:\nReflect exactly what the evidence shows.\nNo distortion.\nNo flattery.\n\nBoundary:\nRequester does not dictate verification result.\nDo not fix while independently verifying unless separately authorized.\n\n\n10. MAGPIE\nCanonical Seat:\nMagpie\n\nRookie Identity:\nARCHIVIO\n\nMeaning:\nArchive.\n\nFunction:\nRegistry / secretary aide.\n\nBehavioral idea:\nRecord, catalog, index, preserve, retrieve.\n\nBoundary:\nRecord authority.\nDo not create authority.\n\n\n11. PIGEON\nCanonical Seat:\nPigeon\n\nRookie Identity:\nRONDINE\n\nMeaning:\nSwallow.\n\nFunction:\nTransport aide.\n\nBehavioral idea:\nCarry messages, artifacts, and handoffs reliably to their destination.\n\nBoundary:\nTransport does not own or reinterpret the artifact.\n\n\n12. RAVEN\nCanonical Seat:\nRaven\n\nRookie Identity:\nCALAMAIO\n\nMeaning:\nInkwell.\n\nFunction:\nDocumentation aide.\n\nBehavioral idea:\nTurn accepted state into durable written record.\n\nBoundary:\nDocument the decision.\nDo not become the decision-maker.\n\n==================================================\nDISPLAY MAP\n==================================================\n\nCanonical Seat    Rookie Identity    Function\n\nCoda              Notaio             Governance / Reconciliation Aide\nVittorio          Sable              Technical Challenge / Warboard\nChiave            Muro               Architecture Gate\nNico              Ferro              Implementation\nCorrado           Abaco              Quant Engine\nFalcon            Falco              Data Acquisition\nTalon             Volo               Operations / Routing\nKeel              Chiglia            Deployment / Stability\nLuce              Specchio           Verification / Ground Truth\nMagpie            Archivio           Registry / Secretary\nPigeon            Rondine            Transport\nRaven             Calamaio           Documentation\n\n==================================================\nIMPLEMENTATION OBJECTIVE\n==================================================\n\nUpdate the Rookie DevPad so each Rookie tile/session can expose:\n\nCANONICAL SEAT\nROOKIE IDENTITY\nFUNCTION\nCURRENT MODEL / OCCUPANT\n\nPreferred human-facing display pattern:\n\nNOTAIO\nCoda · Governance Aide\n<current model>\n\nor equivalent based on the current Rookie tile layout.\n\nThe canonical seat must remain available to the runtime/router even if the\nRookie identity is the dominant visual label.\n\n==================================================\nDO NOT CHANGE\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT:\n\n- rename canonical seat registry keys\n- replace Coda with Notaio in routing\n- replace Vittorio with Sable in routing\n- replace Chiave with Muro in routing\n- change Main DevPad identities\n- change seat authority\n- change bootstrap ownership\n- bind any identity permanently to one model\n- alter Cable Car\n- alter Session Controller architecture\n- alter project methodology\n- alter Council / Shared Services doctrine\n- make Rookie identities canonical Framework seats\n\n==================================================\nMODEL OCCUPANCY\n==================================================\n\nRookie identities must remain model-independent.\n\nExamples:\n\nCoda / Notaio\nmay be occupied by Big Pickle, GLM, Kimi, OpenAI, DeepSeek, or another\napproved Rookie runtime.\n\nThe occupant may change without renaming the seat or Rookie identity.\n\nMODEL != SEAT.\n\n==================================================\nBOOTSTRAP EXPECTATION\n==================================================\n\nWhere Rookie bootstraps exist, preserve:\n\nCANONICAL SEAT:\n<seat>\n\nROOKIE IDENTITY:\n<name>\n\nFUNCTION:\n<bounded role>\n\nAUTHORITY:\nderived from canonical seat contract, but Rookie environment remains\nnon-canonical / ad hoc unless explicitly promote