rity, ownership, lifecycle, or current use cannot be proven.\n\nAction:\nDO NOT MOVE.\nDO NOT DELETE.\nREPORT.\n\n==================================================\nARCHIVE RULE\n==================================================\n\nCreate/use a dated operational archive for this cleanup pass.\n\nPreferred structure:\n\n<appropriate existing archive root>\\\n2026-09-25_HANDOFF_INBOX_CLEANUP\\\n\nIf the canonical Framework archive structure already has a current location for operational handoff provenance, use that instead.\n\nDo NOT invent a second archive taxonomy if a valid current one exists.\n\nWithin the archive preserve enough context to recover:\n\n- original filename\n- original path\n- original Drive ID when applicable\n- source seat\n- destination seat\n- project\n- workstream\n- handoff ID\n- lifecycle status\n- classification\n- archive timestamp\n- content hash where practical\n\n==================================================\nARCHIVE MANIFEST REQUIRED\n==================================================\n\nCreate one archive manifest for the pass.\n\nSuggested name:\n\nGCE_HANDOFF_INBOX_ARCHIVE_MANIFEST_2026-09-25\n\nManifest must record:\n\nARTIFACT\nORIGINAL PATH / DRIVE ID\nCLASSIFICATION\nACTION\nDESTINATION\nSOURCE SEAT\nDESTINATION SEAT\nPROJECT\nWORKSTREAM\nHANDOFF ID\nHASH\nREASON\nCONFIDENCE\n\nThe archive manifest becomes the durable cleanup evidence.\n\n==================================================\nRECON PHASE\n==================================================\n\nBefore any write/move/delete:\n\n1. inventory all discovered active inbox directories\n2. inventory all discovered handoff directories\n3. inventory Drive inbound/outbound operational surfaces\n4. inventory seat inboxes\n5. inventory active return/pickup envelopes\n6. identify current vs historical\n7. identify duplicates\n8. identify orphaned files\n9. identify unresolved handoffs\n10. identify files referenced by current routing/config\n11. identify files waiting on current Framework/Rookie work\n12. identify transport copies whose durable counterpart is proven\n\nProduce an internal recon table BEFORE action.\n\n==================================================\nSPECIAL CABLE CAR RULE\n==================================================\n\nCable Car is transport infrastructure.\n\nDo NOT confuse:\n- transport copy\n- current authoritative artifact\n- artifact owner\n- destination seat\n- routing envelope\n\nKnown finding:\n\nNative Google Docs are not automatically delivered by normal inbound polling when:\n- they are not in 01_INBOUND_TO_GCE\n- supported_payload_types is JSON-only\n\nDo NOT \"fix\" this architecture during cleanup.\n\nRecord it as an open Framework transport finding.\n\nDo not delete authenticated Drive-source artifacts merely because they are not poll-consumable.\n\n==================================================\nCURRENT TRANSPORT FINDING TO PRESERVE\n==================================================\n\nThe canonical bootstrap implementation package required authenticated Drive client export because normal Cable Car polling could not retrieve the native Google Doc.\n\nPreserve this as an open finding:\n\nNATIVE GOOGLE DOC PICKUP PATH != NORMAL JSON POLL PATH\n\nDo not resolve it in this cleanup pass unless Don separately authorizes transport redesign.\n\n==================================================\nINBOX CLEARING RULE\n==================================================\n\nAn inbox item may be cleared ONLY when:\n\n1. it has been consumed OR explicitly superseded\n2. its durable/canonical counterpart is proven\n3. no active workflow still references it\n4. no unresolved route depends on it\n5. required provenance is archived or preserved\n6. action is recorded in the archive manifest\n\nGoal after pass:\n\nACTIVE INBOXES contain ONLY:\n- genuinely live/unconsumed work\n- unresolved/unknown items awaiting ruling\n\nEverything else should be archived or cleared.\n\n==================================================\nHANDOFF CLEARING RULE\n==================================================\n\nA handoff may leave the active handoff queue when:\n\n- delivery is proven\n- required recipient action is completed\n- return/verification lifecycle is complete\n- durable evidence is preserved\n- no current route references that active copy\n\nCompleted handoffs should NOT remain mixed with active queue traffic indefinitely.\n\n==================================================\nDUPLICATE RULE\n==================================================\n\nDo not delete duplicates merely by filename similarity.\n\nPrefer:\n1. SHA-256 match\n2. exact byte match\n3. exact Drive/local transport evidence\n4. explicit supersession relationship\n\nIf only semantic similarity exists:\nARCHIVE rather than delete.\n\n==================================================\nDO NOT TOUCH\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT modify:\n\n- seat bootstrap content\n- seat registry content\n- seat authority\n- Rookie bootstrap draft content\n- Session Controller architecture\n- Cable Car architecture\n- routing architecture\n- EC8 methodology\n- ECQ methodology\n- project implementation truth\n- current session-control schemas\n- current Drive taxonomy\n- model bindings\n\nThis is cleanup, not redesign.\n\n==================================================\nDELETE POLICY\n==================================================\n\nPermanent deletion is the LAST option.\n\nPrefer:\n\nKEEP\nor\nARCHIVE\nor\nCLEAR TRANSPORT COPY\n\nPermanent deletion only when all are true:\n\n- duplicate is proven\n- authoritative copy exists\n- no unique provenance exists\n- no live references exist\n- no unresolved ownership exists\n- hash/content evidence supports deletion\n\nIf uncertain:\nARCHIVE.\n\n==================================================\nSTOP CONDITIONS\n==================================================\n\nSTOP / CHECKPOINT before destructive action if:\n\n- no authoritative counterpa