ileciteturn0file0L245-L270\n\n---\n\n# D. MOVE LIST\n\n### Immediate move list: **NONE established from this handoff alone**\n\nThere is not enough path-by-path evidence here to justify physical moves of existing estates.\n\nA move becomes justified only when:\n\n1. content demonstrably belongs to a different current function/project authority; and\n2. its present placement causes authority confusion.\n\nTherefore the next physical-filesystem phase should **inventory first, move second**.\n\nOne conceptual correction is already settled: **GCE Stack belongs in the project layer, not as a Framework governance silo.** Existing components should not be mass-moved immediately; first create/materialize its parent anchor, then map current components into that authority model. fileciteturn0file0L307-L335\n\n---\n\n# E. SUPERSESSION LIST\n\n## P0/P2 practical priority\n\n### `GCE_FRAMEWORK_HANDOFF_NEW_CHAT_2026-09-20.docx`\n\n**Treatment:**\n- preserve;\n- do not edit;\n- do not rename;\n- do not rewrite its old seat terminology;\n- explicitly classify it as **historical/reset provenance**;\n- mark it **not valid as current seat authority** through the new current pointer surface.\n\nThis is the clearest structural defect because that DOCX is presently alone in the Framework folder and can therefore be mistaken for current doctrine. fileciteturn0file0L68-L94\n\nThis is **supersession-by-pointer**, not destruction or mutation of history.\n\n---\n\n# F. ARCHIVE LIST\n\n### Immediate archive actions: **NONE**\n\nThe handoff gives no reason to physically archive the Sep-20 DOCX yet. In fact, the recommended local pattern leaves it in the Framework folder beside the new current pointer and current anchor.\n\nArchive later only where a path audit establishes that an artifact:\n\n- is purely historical;\n- is no longer useful on the live surface;\n- and its continued presence creates ambiguity.\n\nThe rule is deliberately conservative: historical naming that remains accurate is **not** cleanup debt by itself. fileciteturn0file0L262-L271\n\n---\n\n# G. NEW SURFACES REQUIRED\n\n## 1. `README_CURRENT_FRAMEWORK.md` — **REQUIRED**\n\nAt:\n\n`GCE_DON\\GCE_Framework\\README_CURRENT_FRAMEWORK.md`\n\nThis should be a **thin pointer/safety layer**, not another giant doctrine document.\n\nIt should establish:\n\n- folder contains both current and historical Framework materials;\n- Sep-20 DOCX is historical/reset provenance;\n- Sep-20 DOCX is not current seat authority;\n- identity-first / seat-first operating doctrine;\n- Sep-22 frozen roster is current;\n- projects own implementation truth;\n- historical materials remain historically accurate;\n- current continuation uses the current Framework anchor;\n- current Drive anchor/reference once reconciled/materialized.\n\nThat treatment is explicitly prescribed by the handoff. fileciteturn0file0L97-L132\n\n## 2. Current Framework authority artifact — **REQUIRED**\n\nProposed naming pattern:\n\n`GCE_FRAMEWORK_CURRENT_2026-09-23.md`\n\nIts role should be tightly bounded to **current authority**, not a rewrite of the entire Framework history.\n\nMinimum contents:\n\n- current roster;\n- authority hierarchy;\n- identity/seat/model separation;\n- Framework vs Project boundary;\n- current root doctrine;\n- current continuation pointer;\n- explicit supersession relationship to the Sep-20 DOCX.\n\n## 3. Framework Reconciliation parent — **REQUIRED**\n\nThis is a distinct project/workstream and must remain separate from live Framework governance.\n\nScope:\n\n- stale-chat intake;\n- Wave registry;\n- authority classification;\n- artifact mapping;\n- read-only Drive reconciliation;\n- conflict/supersession registry;\n- successor-anchor preparation.\n\nIts current state is **HANDOFF ONLY**, so durable materialization is justified. fileciteturn0file0L338-L358\n\n## 4. GCE Stack parent — **REQUIRED**\n\nMaterialize the parent first.\n\nThen map:\n\n- VoiceBridge;\n- Web Bridge/scraping;\n- transport;\n- synchronization;\n- runtime plumbing;\n- local services/daemons;\n- APIs/adapters;\n- developer utilities;\n- archival/recovery tooling;\n- Command Center supporting tech;\n- Walking Capture.\n\nDo **not** perform a component migration sweep at the same time. fileciteturn0file0L307-L335\n\n## 5. Model Test Registry — **REQUIRED, lightweight**\n\nClassification:\n\n**Framework research workstream / Technical Strategy**\n\nRegistry should point to, not duplicate:\n\n- Disney Test Case\n- Monitor / identical-prompt harness\n- Kimi / EC8 real-world validation\n- Black Pearl\n- future model evaluations\n\nNo separate project is justified yet. fileciteturn0file0L361-L380\n\n---\n\n# H. DRIVE / LOCAL DIFFERENCES\n\nThere are two important differences to reconcile.\n\n### Local\n\n`GCE_DON\\GCE_Framework\\` currently has **only the Sep-20 DOCX**, with no README, current pointer, supersession marker, or current authority artifact. That creates a live-authority ambiguity. fileciteturn0file0L65-L94\n\n### Google Drive\n\nThe current known reference is:\n\n`GCE_GOOGLE_DRIVE_STRUCTURE_MANIFEST_CURRENT_2026-09-21`\n\nIts high-level model includes:\n\n- `GCE_ORG/`\n- `03_Projects/`\n- `06_Frozen_State_and_Archive/`\n\nand functional Framework estates including Strategic Governance, Technical Strategy, Operations, Architecture, Shared Enterprise Services, and Implementation. fileciteturn0file0L210-L230\n\nThe critical reconciliation principle is:\n\n> **Sep-21 predating the Sep-22 roster does not make its functional taxonomy obsolete.**\n\nWhat must be separated is:\n\n**durable functional estate**  \nversus  \n**obsolete live seat/identity coupling**. fileciteturn0file0L232-L242\n\nTherefore **Drive remains READ-ONLY** during this phase.\n\n---\n\n# I. DON DECISIONS REQUIRED\n\nI see **four actual Don rulings**, not twenty.\n\n1. **Approve the thin-current-surface pattern**  \n   `README_CURRENT_FRAMEWORK.md` + `GCE_FRAMEWORK_CURRENT_2026-09-23.md` + untouched Sep-20 DOCX.\n\n2. **Approve parent materialization** for:\n   - Framework Reconciliation\n   - GCE Stack\n\n3. **Approve Model Testing as a Technical Strategy research registry**, not a standalone project.\n\n4. **Approve the execution principle:**  \n   no mass reorganization; path-specific audit must prove authority/routing defects before rename/move/archive.\n\nEverything else in this handoff is already substantially resolved.\n\n---\n\n# J. EXECUTION PLAN\n\n## Wave 1 — Current Framework safety layer\n\n**Local only. Surgical.**\n\nCreate:\n\n```text\nGCE_DON\\GCE_Framework\\\n    README_CURRENT_FRAMEWORK.md\n    GCE_FRAMEWORK_CURRENT_2026-09-23.md\n    GCE_FRAMEWORK_HANDOFF_NEW_CHAT_2026-09-20.docx\n```\n\nNo modification of the DOCX.\n\nThis closes the most dangerous retrieval ambiguity first.\n\n## Wave 2 — Materialize project parents\n\nCreate only the minimum durable parent surfaces for:\n\n- Framework Reconciliation\n- GCE Stack\n\nDo not migrate every child/component yet.\n\n## Wave 3 — Build live taxonomy inventory\n\nFor each Framework node capture exactly:\n\n```text\nPATH\nCURRENT FUNCTION\nCURRENT OWNER / AUTHORITY\nLIVE / SUPPORTING / HISTORICAL\nFUNCTIONAL NAME OR OLD-SEAT NAME\nKEEP / RENAME / MOVE / SUPERSEDE / ARCHIVE / UNKNOWN\n```\n\nThat schema is already prescribed by the handoff and should be used without embellishment. fileciteturn0file0L165-L182\n\n## Wave 4 — Reconcile against Drive manifest\n\nRead-only comparison against the Sep-21 Drive manifest.\n\nFor every mismatch classify:\n\n- valid functional survival;\n- obsolete identity coupling;\n- local-only current surface;\n- Drive-only current surface;\n- duplicate authority;\n- historical provenance;\n- UNKNOWN / needs Don ruling.\n\n**Still no Drive mutation.**\n\n## Wave 5 — Don ruling\n\nReturn only genuine exceptions:\n\n- rename candidates;\n- moves;\n- supersessions;\n- archive candidates;\n- unresolved owner/authority collisions.\n\n## Wave 6 — Execute accepted surgical changes\n\nOnly after Don accepts the exception list.\n\n## Wave 7 — Luce verification\n\nVerify:\n\n- current pointer resolves;\n- historical artifacts cannot masquerade as current;\n- no duplicate current authority;\n- no project implementation truth moved into Framework;\n- no retired seats revived by taxonomy;\n- Drive/local references reconcile;\n- retrieval from a fresh session reaches current authority without inference.\n\n---\n\n# Coda reconciliation ruling\n\nThe Framework itself **does not need another redesign**.\n\nThe remaining work is predominantly **authority surfacing and taxonomy hygiene**:\n\n**1. Expose current authority.  \n2. Preserve provenance.  \n3. Materialize two missing parents.  \n4. Inventory functional estates.  \n5. Change only the nodes that actually misstate authority.**\n\nThat is consistent with the governing execution sequence already frozen in the handoff:\n\n**Truth → map → reconcile → Don ruling → execute → Luce verify.** fileciteturn0file0L477-L504\n\n**My recommended Don ruling: accept this plan and authorize Wave 1 + Wave 2 as the next local execution package. Google Drive remains read-only.**"]}, "create_time": 1790204374.813955, "end_turn": true, "id": "cb6ed263-7652-4ffd-a8db-de7efd0a4581", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 538, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "4b08ab6c-d4c9-4c5d-92b7-cfb9d659d414", "cited_message_idx": 17, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_ccb2b8102f588191a4d36e8ed94d401b", "line_range": [5, 8], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 0, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id": "file_00000000c