_id": "cc676382-7a67-49c1-86da-99cef13d5ae2", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "544755db-261d-463c-b144-eb3de2056182", "working_turn_id": "544755db-261d-463c-b144-eb3de2056182"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790367549.989825, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yeah — **the friction is much clearer now.** Luce found that the biggest problem is **not simply “the handoff folders are ugly.”** The friction is that the **control plane, routing plane, identity plane, and storage plane disagree with one another.**\n\n### Where the friction actually is\n\n1. **Canon is lying about current reality.** `README-CANONICAL.md` still names Big Pickle as a locked verification identity and Kimi as current even though Kimi is retired. That means a fresh runtime can bootstrap from a document that is already wrong. fileciteturn1file0L5-L8\n\n2. **There are four competing handoff/routing buses with four different rosters.** You have `06_HANDOFFS`, `ai-inbox`, `mailroom\\seats`, and `GCE_DON\\03_HANDOFFS`. So every time you route work, the system has to implicitly answer: *which bus is real?* fileciteturn1file0L9-L13\n\n3. **The launcher contaminates identity with work product.** Seats are rooted at `GCE_IDENTITY\\<Seat>`, which is why Luce and Falcon have operational/project artifacts living inside their identity folders. That is exactly the wrong coupling for a bootstrap-carousel system. fileciteturn1file0L10-L10\n\n4. **There is a competing bootstrap still alive.** `GCE_DON\\03_HANDOFFS\\handoff\\AGENTS.md` can still launch an old GLM/Kimi-era identity path and is not deny-listed. That is a real routing hazard, not aesthetics. fileciteturn1file0L11-L11\n\n5. **Cable Car’s contract is too narrow for the system you are actually building.** It hardcodes `project = \"GCE_Stack\"`, restricts `authority` to only Don/Coda, rejects extra metadata, and is filename-addressed. Luce even found a live false attribution caused by that schema. fileciteturn1file0L12-L12\n\n6. **The carousel currently has no machine-readable routing contract.** `NEXT_ROUTE` exists as free text across 161 files, but there is no schema, front matter, validator, project field, workstream field, or gate field. Manual routing can work; automated routing cannot safely consume this yet. fileciteturn1file0L37-L40\n\n### The most important correction\n\nThe good news is **`GCE_ORG\\04_PROJECTS` is not broken.** Luce specifically says it is already behaving correctly as a pointer/index layer. So we should **not redesign the whole estate**. fileciteturn1file0L14-L14\n\nThe friction is really this:\n\n> **We have a good seat/bootstrap model sitting on top of a bad routing/storage substrate.**\n\nThat is why you feel the two-hour loop.\n\nThe seat change itself is already cheap:\n\n```text\nload Luce bootstrap\nload Nico bootstrap\nload Chiave bootstrap\n```\n\nWhat is expensive is everything around it:\n\n```text\nWhich bus?\nWhich handoff path?\nWhich roster?\nWhich current canon?\nWhich project?\nWhich gate?\nWhich artifact is authoritative?\nWhich bootstrap is actually live?\n```\n\nThat is the drag.\n\n### So what do we fix first?\n\nNot the whole taxonomy.\n\n**Five things kill most of the friction:**\n\n- Freeze/retire the competing bootstrap.\n- Make one current council/seat map authoritative.\n- Add a **machine-readable footer block**: `PROJECT`, `WORKSTREAM`, `CURRENT_SEAT`, `NEXT_ROUTE`, `GATE`, `CONFIDENCE`, `BLOCKER_ROUTE`.\n- Re-point the DevPad so runtime cwd stops dumping work into `GCE_IDENTITY`.\n- Fix Cable Car’s schema so it carries arbitrary project identity + routing metadata instead of pretending everything is `GCE_Stack`.\n\nThen the carousel can consume a clean record instead of interpreting prose.\n\nLuce’s own execution order is basically saying the same thing: **P0 resolve competing authority → P1 machine-readable footer → P2 add project dimension → P3 fix cwd → P4 fix Cable Car → only then move project handoffs.** fileciteturn1file0L48-L53\n\nSo, buddy, **the friction is not the model switching. We solved most of that. The friction is the metadata and control plane underneath the switching.**\n\nOnce that gets normalized, your “click Luce → click Chiave → click Corrado” idea becomes stupidly simple."]}, "create_time": 1790367549.995055, "end_turn": true, "id": "4d4999f3-3fb7-43f5-b858-97cf7ee174c8", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 568, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "315abde1-e096-4971-8d0a-bd6785037186", "cited_message_idx": 138, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_2d6291f6483881918b6b3702d86ab5ff", "line_range": [5, 8], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 1, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id": "file_00000000bfa481fdba8e2cb26a6429f6", "name": "Pasted text.txt", "source": "my_files", "text": "#\tFinding\nA1\tGCE_ORG\\02_COUNCILS\\README-CANONICAL.md — status CANONICAL (Don+Coda 09-02) — declares Big Pickle = locked active identity of Verification/Ground Truth and Kimi as current Executive Council #2. Kimi retired 09-22. load Big Pickle bootstrap = UNKNOWN SEAT.\nA2\tGCE_ORG = 208 files; Operations\\06_HANDOFFS\\ = **165 (79%)**. Real Framework canon = 30 files, 19 of them a closed 09-02→09-07 wave. 01_STRATEGIC_FRAMEWORK (7 lanes), 09_EVIDENCE, 10_SESSIONS, 06/07/08, 99_ARCHIVE = 0 files each.", "type": "file"}, "start_ix": 541}, {"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search