ories.\n\nIdentity must remain bootstrap/load-control, not become project working storage.\n\nD. PROJECT OWNERSHIP PRINCIPLE IS VALID\nGCE_ORG\\04_PROJECTS is already a compliant pointer/index layer.\n\nProject-scoped artifacts belong with the project.\nFramework-general artifacts belong in GCE_ORG.\nRouting destination does NOT determine artifact ownership.\n\nE. NEXT_ROUTE IS NOT MACHINE SAFE\nNEXT_ROUTE exists widely as free text.\nThere is no stable machine-readable footer schema / validator carrying:\n- project\n- workstream\n- current seat\n- next route\n- gate\n- confidence\n- blocker route\n\nF. CABLE CAR CONTRACT IS TOO NARROW\nCurrent contract:\n- hardcodes project = GCE_Stack\n- authority enum is too narrow and has already caused false attribution\n- rejects required routing metadata\n- is filename-addressed\n- must be corrected BEFORE Drive integration hardens\n\nG. MANUAL CAROUSEL IS CONDITIONALLY READY\nAutomated carousel is not.\n\nLuce specifically found:\n- board does not cover all required seats\n- no Corrado tile\n- panes have no project/workstream/gate dimension\n- NEXT_ROUTE is free text\n\nH. ACTIVE EC8 MUST NOT BE MOVED\nEC8 / Edge Crew Quant physical implementation is coherent and live.\nDo not destabilize it in this pass.\n\n==================================================\n3. PRIMARY PASS OBJECTIVE\n==================================================\n\nAt completion, the following must be true:\n\n1. ONE authoritative current bootstrap/routing authority exists.\n2. Known competing stale bootstrap cannot silently launch.\n3. Seat identity directories no longer receive normal project work product.\n4. A machine-readable session/footer routing contract exists.\n5. The DevPad runtime can identify:\n       PROJECT\n       WORKSTREAM\n       CURRENT_SEAT\n       NEXT_ROUTE\n       GATE\n       CONFIDENCE\n       BLOCKER_ROUTE\n6. The seat registry / board supports the frozen active roster required for routing.\n7. Cable Car contract can carry arbitrary project/workstream/routing information without false authority attribution.\n8. Existing live project paths continue working.\n9. No historical provenance is rewritten.\n10. No Google Drive writes occur.\n11. No mass filesystem migration occurs.\n12. The result is immediately usable as the substrate for:\n       click seat → load bootstrap → continue.\n\n==================================================\n4. USE SUB-AGENTS\n==================================================\n\nNico owns the build.\n\nLaunch parallel sub-agents to inspect / implement bounded pieces where useful.\n\nSuggested lanes:\n\nSUB-AGENT A — BOOTSTRAP / AUTHORITY\n- current bootstrap sources\n- competing GCE_DON bootstrap\n- authoritative seat/council mapping\n- deny-list / retirement behavior\n- ensure no retired Kimi/Calibro/model identity can silently become current\n\nSUB-AGENT B — DEVPAD / ROUTER\n- seat registry\n- seats.js\n- inventory.js\n- tile coverage\n- project/workstream/gate fields\n- NEXT_ROUTE consumption path\n- cwd behavior\n\nSUB-AGENT C — FOOTER CONTRACT\n- define minimal machine-readable routing footer\n- parser\n- validator\n- backward-compatible treatment for old free-text footers\n\nSUB-AGENT D — CABLE CAR\n- contract/schema\n- project identifier\n- workstream\n- created_by semantics\n- routing hint\n- metadata block\n- primary artifact addressing\n- compatibility with current transport implementation\n\nSUB-AGENT E — REGRESSION / PATH DEPENDENCY\n- search live code for hard-coded old routing paths\n- identify anything that will break when re-pointed\n- distinguish historical references from runtime dependencies\n\nSUB-AGENT F — TEST / INTEGRATION\n- integration tests\n- bootstrap swap\n- footer parse\n- seat resolution\n- Cable Car packet\n- old-path compatibility / fail-loud behavior\n\nUse more or fewer agents if warranted.\n\nDO NOT let sub-agents invent separate architectures.\nNico reconciles their output into ONE implementation.\n\n==================================================\n5. MACHINE-READABLE FOOTER — REQUIRED\n==================================================\n\nCreate one minimal routing block.\n\nExact syntax may follow existing code conventions, but it must reliably represent at least:\n\n    PROJECT\n    WORKSTREAM\n    SESSION_ID\n    CURRENT_SEAT\n    STATUS\n    GATE\n    CONFIDENCE\n    NEXT_ROUTE\n    BLOCKER_ROUTE\n    CURRENT_ANCHOR\n\nOptional:\n    AFTER_PASS\n    FINAL_GATE\n\nRequirements:\n\n- deterministic parse\n- schema or validator\n- invalid seat fails loudly\n- retired seat fails loudly\n- model names cannot satisfy seat fields\n- project/workstream not inferred from seat\n- missing legacy fields may degrade to MANUAL/UNKNOWN, never invented\n- old handoffs remain readable\n- do NOT bulk-rewrite historical files\n\nThe carousel should consume this block.\n\nThe prose footer can remain human-readable if desired, but machine routing must no longer depend on prose interpretation.\n\n==================================================\n6. AUTHORITATIVE SEAT REGISTRY\n==================================================\n\nUse the frozen roster.\n\nDon\nCoda\nVittorio\nChiave\nNico\nCorrado\nFalcon\nTalon\nKeel\nLuce\nRagno\nMagpie\nPigeon\nRaven\n\nMODEL != SEAT.\n\nSpace Bunny, Big Pickle, Kimi, GLM, etc. are occupants/providers/models and must never become authoritative seat identifiers merely because they occupy a runtime.\n\nEnsure the routing registry and UI draw from one authoritative source.\n\nDo not maintain four roster copies if one registry can drive them.\n\n==================================================\n7. COMPETING BOOTSTRAP\n==================================================\n\nThe stale competing bootstrap identified by Luce must not remain silently executable.\n\nDo the smallest safe fix.\n\nAcceptable patterns include:\n- explicit retired/superseded marker\n- deny-list\n- redirect/pointer to current authority\n- hard fail with correct current load instruction\n\nDo 