mmand / key\n        ↓\n    default Windows handler opens the handoff\n\n==================================================\n1. REQUIRED STATE FILE\n==================================================\n\nUse one fixed project/runtime-local state file:\n\n    .gce\\handoff-latest.txt\n\nContents:\n\n    absolute Windows path to the latest handoff artifact\n\nExample:\n\n    C:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\GCE_DON\\GCE_EC8\\...\\20260925-NICO-TO-LUCE.md\n\nRules:\n\n- absolute path only\n- UTF-8\n- one path\n- overwrite on each newly created handoff\n- do not append history here\n- do not infer path later\n- only update after the handoff file has successfully been written\n- verify target exists before declaring success\n\n==================================================\n2. WRITER BEHAVIOR\n==================================================\n\nAt the point where a seat creates a handoff artifact:\n\n1. create/write handoff\n2. verify handoff exists\n3. write absolute path to:\n\n       .gce\\handoff-latest.txt\n\n4. preserve existing handoff-generation behavior\n5. do not alter artifact ownership or routing semantics\n\nPseudo-PowerShell:\n\n    $handoffPath = (Resolve-Path $createdHandoff).Path\n    New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force \".gce\" | Out-Null\n    Set-Content `\n        -Path \".gce\\handoff-latest.txt\" `\n        -Value $handoffPath `\n        -Encoding UTF8\n\nThe actual implementation should follow current runtime/code conventions rather than injecting PowerShell if the writer is Node/TS.\n\n==================================================\n3. OPEN COMMAND\n==================================================\n\nCreate a deterministic helper command:\n\n    oh\n\nMeaning:\n\n    OPEN HANDOFF\n\nBehavior:\n\n    read .gce\\handoff-latest.txt\n    trim content\n    validate non-empty\n    validate path exists\n    Start-Process target\n    exit\n\nExpected PowerShell implementation:\n\n    function oh {\n        $state = \".gce\\handoff-latest.txt\"\n\n        if (-not (Test-Path $state)) {\n            Write-Host \"No handoff state found.\"\n            return\n        }\n\n        $p = (Get-Content $state -Raw).Trim()\n\n        if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($p)) {\n            Write-Host \"No handoff recorded.\"\n            return\n        }\n\n        if (-not (Test-Path $p)) {\n            Write-Host \"Handoff not found: $p\"\n            return\n        }\n\n        Start-Process $p\n    }\n\nPrefer the user's default Windows association for .md/.txt rather than hardcoding Notepad or VS Code.\n\n==================================================\n4. RUNTIME LOCATION RULE\n==================================================\n\nThe helper must resolve the CURRENT PROJECT RUNTIME correctly.\n\nDo not create a global ambiguous:\n\n    C:\\Users\\...\\ .gce\\handoff-latest.txt\n\nif multiple DevPads/projects can be active.\n\nPreferred model:\n\n    <active-project-runtime>\\.gce\\handoff-latest.txt\n\nEach isolated DevPad/project therefore owns its own latest-handoff pointer.\n\nExample:\n\n    GCE_EdgeCrew_Quant\\\n        .gce\\\n            handoff-latest.txt\n\n    VoiceBridge\\\n        .gce\\\n            handoff-latest.txt\n\nThis prevents one project from opening another project's handoff.\n\nIf the current DevPad already has a stable runtime/project-root resolver, use it.\n\nDo not invent another project-root mechanism.\n\n==================================================\n5. OPTIONAL GLOBAL COMMAND RESOLUTION\n==================================================\n\nThe `oh` command may be installed globally in the PowerShell profile, but it must resolve the active project's `.gce\\handoff-latest.txt`.\n\nPreferred resolution order:\n\n1. current runtime/project root supplied by DevPad\n2. nearest parent containing `.gce`\n3. current working directory `.gce`\n4. fail loudly\n\nDo not silently fall back to another project's state.\n\n==================================================\n6. AUTO-OPEN SUPPORT\n==================================================\n\nAdd support for:\n\n    AutoOpenHandoff\n\nDefault:\n\n    false\n\nFor now, Don wants deterministic manual open first.\n\nBehavior when enabled:\n\n    if artifact type == handoff\n        and write succeeded\n        and target exists\n            Start-Process handoff\n\nDo NOT auto-open:\n\n- ordinary evidence\n- logs\n- manifests\n- test reports\n- intermediate artifacts\n\nFuture configurable artifact classes are fine, but do not overbuild them now.\n\n==================================================\n7. DEVPAD / FOOTER HOOK\n==================================================\n\nExpose the current handoff path as runtime data so the DevPad can later render:\n\n    OPEN HANDOFF\n\nDo not depend on this UI work for completion.\n\nRequired data surface:\n\n    LATEST_HANDOFF_PATH\n\nor equivalent existing state field.\n\nIf trivial, add the button now.\n\nIf not trivial, return the exact UI hook/API required.\n\nNo LLM/model call should be required to open the file.\n\n==================================================\n8. CLICKABLE LINKS\n==================================================\n\nOptional only.\n\nIf existing rendering supports it safely, a generated handoff response may additionally expose:\n\n    file:///C:/...\n\nBut:\n\n- hyperlink support is NOT part of acceptance\n- do not rely on OSC 8\n- do not route opening through OpenCode model commands\n- do not use vscode:// as the default\n\nLinks are polish.\n\n`oh` is the deterministic control.\n\n==================================================\n9. FAILURE BEHAVIOR\n==================================================\n\nFail loudly and cheaply.\n\nCases:\n\nSTATE FILE ABSENT:\n    \"No handoff state found.\"\n\nEMPTY STATE:\n    \"No handoff recorded.\"\n\nTARGET MISSING:\n    \"Handoff not found: <path>\"\n\nINVALID PROJECT ROOT:\n    \"Unable to resolve active project runtime.\"\n\nDo not invoke an LLM to diagnose these.\n\n==================================================\n10. CONCURRENCY / SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nBecause multiple seats may operate within one project:\n\n- latest successful handoff wins\n- write atomically if practical\n- do not leave partial path content\n- reader must tolerate newline/BOM\n- path with spaces must work\n- do not shell-concatenate untrusted strings\n- use Start-Process/path APIs directly\n\nDo not solve multi-project global arbitration here.\nProject isolation already owns that.\n\n==================================================\n11. TESTS\n==================================================\n\nMinimum acceptance tests:\n\nA. Create test handoff.\nB. Confirm `.gce\\handoff-latest.txt` contains exact absolute path.\nC. `oh` opens valid file.\nD. Paths containing spaces work.\nE. Missing pointer fails cleanly.\nF. Empty pointer fails cleanly.\nG. Deleted target fails cleanly.\nH. Project A cannot silently resolve Project B pointer.\nI. Creating handoff #2 replaces handoff #1 as latest.\nJ. Existing handoff-generation behavior remains unchanged.\nK. No model/API/token call occurs when running `oh`.\n\n==================================================\n12. DO NOT DO\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT:\n\n- redesign the carousel\n- redesign routing\n- change taxonomy\n- move handoffs\n- change seat doctrine\n- alter Cable Car\n- rewrite OpenCode rendering\n- build a document viewer\n- hardcode Notepad\n- introduce a model call\n- create another handoff registry\n\nThis is a utility.\n\n==================================================\n13. SUCCESS CONDITION\n==================================================\n\nUser experience:\n\n    Nico finishes handoff\n        ↓\n    handoff-latest.txt updates\n        ↓\n    Don types:\n\n        oh\n\n        ↓\n    handoff opens immediately\n\nNo copy/paste.\nNo browsing directories.\nNo model call.\nNo renderer dependency.\n\n=================================